Sciences (CNS) Nursing Public Health and Health Sciences (SPHHS) Social & Behavioral Sciences (SBS) University Without Walls (UWW) Connect with UMass Alumni Using LinkedIn How to Network Jobs & Internships Expand Menu Item Internships, Co-ops, and Other Field Experiences Expand Menu Item Field Experience Definitions Internships Co-ops Research Civic Engagement and Service Learning Internships and Co-Ops at Charles River Campus UMass Internship Partner Programs Scholarships for Field Experiences Jobs Searching for Jobs & Internships Can I Do an Internship? Negotiating Job Offers Interviewing Using Handshake Carousel Your Career Journey Whether you are a prospective student or about to graduate, your career journey is unique to you. Visit the Career Journey page to find out where you are on the path and see what the next steps might be. Career Journey > Overview Start your Career Journey here Professional Photo Appointments Schedule a session to take your picture using the Iris Photo Booth. The booth provides the camera, lighting, and guides for a professional picture - you just need to bring yourself. Resources > Photo Booth Learn about the Iris Photo Booth UMass Professional Wardrobe Closet The UMass Professional Wardrobe Closet is a free resource to help you put together an outfit that will make you stand out from the crowd at career fairs and interviews. Closet UMass Professional Wardrobe Closet Intern in Boston The Charles River Campus in Newton, MA is the ideal place for you to stay while completing an internship or co-op in the Boston area. About > Charles River Campus About the Charles River Campus Get Experience Did you know you can earn academic credit when you do an internship? Internships are a great way to get experience while also working towards completing your degree. Jobs & Internships > Internships Learn More about Internships Upcoming Career Fairs UMass hosts over 20 career fairs every year, ranging from major-specific job fairs to far-reaching internship fairs. Learn more on your career fair page. Employers  > Career Fairs Career Fair List Start Your Career Journey Explore Resources What is Handshake? Outcome Highlights for the Class of 2025 The Class of 2025 has thrived in their first 6 months after graduating, finding success across a wide variety of companies and industries. The data below represent the results from the First Destination Survey for the Class of 2025 . 88% Undergraduate students who obtained a career outcome related to their field of study 79% Knowledge rate for the Class of 2025 (Average knowledge rate for other colleges: 55%) 40 Number of different states the Class of 2025 are working in post graduation 24 Number of different countries the Class of 2025 are working in post graduation Featured Articles Read More Go to: How to Write Your LinkedIn Profile April 29, 2026 Internship Photo Contest 2026 Each year, the Career Hub at UMass hosts an internship photo contest with prizes for the best submissions. Any UMass Amherst student who completed an internship, co-op, research, or other field experience from September 1, 2025 to August 31st, 2026 is eligible to enter. Go to: How to Write Your LinkedIn Profile January 22, 2026 Considering Relocating After Graduation? Maybe You Should. Have you ever considering relocating after graduation? If not, you may want to. The Wall Street Journal just released the top cities where the class of 2025 landed jobs and the list is a little surprising. The list highlights a bunch of great, developing cities you may not have considered. Go to: How to Write Your LinkedIn Profile September 22, 2025 Amherst Area Internship Fair Kicks Off Career Fair Season at UMass The Amherst Area Internship Fair returned to the Campus Center Auditorium on Friday, September 5, bringing together more than 40 local businesses, non-profits, and campus departments offering part-time jobs, internships, and work-study opportunities. Now in its fifth year, the fair has grown steadily—from 17 employers in its first year to more than 40 this fall—reflecting the strong demand for meaningful student work experiences in the Pioneer Valley. Career Centers Across UMass Amherst Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Education College of Education Riccio College of Engineering Riccio College of Engineering College of Humanities & Fine Arts College of Humanities & Fine Arts College of Natural Sciences College of Natural Sciences College of Social & Behavioral Sciences College of Social & Behavioral Sciences Nursing Elaine Marieb College of Nursing Isenberg School of Management Isenberg School of Management Manning College of Information & Computer Sciences Manning College of Information & Computer Sciences School of Public Health & Health Sciences School of Public Health & Health Sciences University Without Walls Career Services University Without Walls Career Services Graduate School Office of Professional Development Graduate School Office of Professional Development Charles River Campus Internship and Co-ops Charles River Campus Internship and Co-ops Career Development & Professional Connections Whether you’re wondering where to begin, looking for an internship, or starting your job search, we will guide you through the process of your unique career development. Address: Goodell Hall | 140 Hicks Way | Amherst, MA 01003 Main Office Number: (413) 545-2224 Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Footer Students Career Journey Career Centers Resource Library Employers Handshake Contact Us UMass collegiate M - University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2025 University of Massachusetts Amherst · Site Policies · Accessibility"
