    "https://www.umass.edu/careers/about/charles-river-campus": {
      "title": "The Charles River Campus",
      "description": "Our Newton Campus : Career Development & Professional Connections : UMass Amherst Skip to main content The University of Massachusetts Amherst Open UMass Global Links Menu Visit Apply Give Search UMass.edu Menu Career Development & Professional Connections About Us Our Staff Career Centers Across UMass Our Newton Campus Handshake Login Student Outcomes Students Undergraduates Graduates Alumni Identity-Based Resources International Students Prospective Students UWW Students Employers Post Jobs and Internships Host an Event Career Fairs at UMass Why Recruit at UMass Internship Program Best Practices Recruiting Guidelines Contact Us Faculty Sponsor an Intern Career Events for Students Request a Presentation Resource Library Career Journey Expand Menu Item Self Discovery and Career Exploration Build Career Skills: Resumes, Job-searching, and Interviewing Learn Additional Technical, Creative, and Professional Skills Your Career Support Team Gain Experience: Internships, Co-ops, Research, and More! Is Graduate School Right for Me? Year-by-Year Checklist Tool Kits Expand Menu Item Resumes Cover Letters Career Fair Preparation Interviewing LinkedIn Learning Networking What Skills Do Employers Want? Applying to Grad School Photo Booth for Headshots Professional Wardrobe Closet Connections Expand Menu Item Career Communities Expand Menu Item Arts, Multimedia, and Entertainment Business, Financial Services, and Consulting Data and Information Technology Education, Human Services, and Counseling Engineering Government and Public Service Healthcare, Life Sciences, and Nursing Infrastructure and Transportation Law and Legal Services Research Sustainability, Environment, and Agriculture Career Centers Across UMass Expand Menu Item Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Education Engineering Graduate School Office of Professional Development Humanities & Fine Arts (HFA) Information & Computer Sciences (CICS) Isenberg School of Management (ISOM) Natural Sciences (CNS) Nursing Public Health and Health Sciences (SPHHS) Social & Behavioral Sciences (SBS) University Without Walls (UWW) Connect with UMass Alumni Using LinkedIn How to Network Jobs & Internships Expand Menu Item Internships, Co-ops, and Other Field Experiences Expand Menu Item Field Experience Definitions Internships Co-ops Research Civic Engagement and Service Learning Internships and Co-Ops at Charles River Campus UMass Internship Partner Programs Scholarships for Field Experiences Jobs Searching for Jobs & Internships Can I Do an Internship? Negotiating Job Offers Interviewing Using Handshake The Charles River Campus A center for student-focused experiential learning and a hub of research-industry collaboration. Connecting the state’s flagship public research university to the Greater Boston business community. The Charles River Campus of UMass Amherst serves as a center for student experiential learning, industry engagement, academic and research collaboration, and fundraising in Greater Boston, which is home to a plurality of UMass Amherst students and alumni. By enhancing opportunities for our students to grow professionally while contributing to our state’s vibrant economy, UMass Amherst, the commonwealth’s only public land-grant university and its flagship campus, is building on its long history of service to the state, while fostering upward economic mobility for the citizens of Massachusetts and the world. The campus is located at 100 Carlson Avenue in Newton, Mass., within the N-Squared Innovation District , eight miles from downtown Boston. Much more than just professional experience Participating in one or more field experiences—co-ops and internships—while at UMass is one of the best ways to prepare for your career. There are a wide range of field experience opportunities for students. You can intern or be on co-op during an academic semester or during the summer. All co-ops are paid, while only some internships are paid. They all provide valuable experience for you and improve your résumé. Internships and co-ops in the Greater Boston area Internships and co-ops in the Greater Boston area Housing Housing options on the Charles River Campus include New Hall, a modern, air-conditioned residence, and Malloy Hall, a suite-style residence. Inquire about Charles River Housing Inquire about Charles River Housing Career Development & Professional Connections Whether you’re wondering where to begin, looking for an internship, or starting your job search, we will guide you through the process of your unique career development. Address: Goodell Hall | 140 Hicks Way | Amherst, MA 01003 Main Office Number: (413) 545-2224 Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Footer Students Career Journey Career Centers Resource Library Employers Handshake Contact Us UMass collegiate M - University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2025 University of Massachusetts Amherst · Site Policies · Accessibility"
