ISOM) Natural Sciences (CNS) Nursing Public Health and Health Sciences (SPHHS) Social & Behavioral Sciences (SBS) University Without Walls (UWW) Connect with UMass Alumni Using LinkedIn How to Network Jobs & Internships Expand Menu Item Internships, Co-ops, and Other Field Experiences Expand Menu Item Field Experience Definitions Internships Co-ops Research Civic Engagement and Service Learning Internships and Co-Ops at Charles River Campus UMass Internship Partner Programs Scholarships for Field Experiences Jobs Searching for Jobs & Internships Can I Do an Internship? Negotiating Job Offers Interviewing Using Handshake Career Resources for Undergraduate Students Welcome to the University of Massachusetts Amherst's Career Development and Professional Connections Hub. Over the course of your college career, you'll be developing your personal and professional skills in many ways, and we're excited to be there to support you during this journey. As an undergraduate student, you have access to many tools and resources to aid you in your career development. The career offices on campus are here to both provide you access to these resources, as well as guidance on how to make the most of them over the next few years. Whether you're just starting out or preparing to graduate, you can find help with career strategizing, resume writing, interviewing, job and internship searching, and much more. Take advantage of the many resources available to you through the career offices on campus and to get involved in our events and workshops. Starting Resources for Undergraduate Students: With so many resources at your disposal, choosing where to start can be a little overwhelming. Here are a few to get you started: Review the Career Journey for a broad overview of what you may want to accomplish while at UMass Amherst Dive into the different resources available, including resume guides , interview support , and graduate school planning . Explore Handshake to find thousands of jobs and internships posted for UMass Amherst students, as well as career fairs, events, and networking opportunities. Career Centers Across UMass Amherst Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Education College of Education Riccio College of Engineering Riccio College of Engineering College of Humanities & Fine Arts College of Humanities & Fine Arts College of Natural Sciences College of Natural Sciences College of Social & Behavioral Sciences College of Social & Behavioral Sciences Nursing Elaine Marieb College of Nursing Isenberg School of Management Isenberg School of Management Manning College of Information & Computer Sciences Manning College of Information & Computer Sciences School of Public Health & Health Sciences School of Public Health & Health Sciences University Without Walls Career Services University Without Walls Career Services Graduate School Office of Professional Development Graduate School Office of Professional Development Charles River Campus Internship and Co-ops Charles River Campus Internship and Co-ops Career Development & Professional Connections Whether you’re wondering where to begin, looking for an internship, or starting your job search, we will guide you through the process of your unique career development. Address: Goodell Hall | 140 Hicks Way | Amherst, MA 01003 Main Office Number: (413) 545-2224 Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Footer Students Career Journey Career Centers Resource Library Employers Handshake Contact Us UMass collegiate M - University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2025 University of Massachusetts Amherst · Site Policies · Accessibility"
