    "https://www.umass.edu/careers/graduate-students": {
      "title": "Career Resources for Graduate Students",
      "description": "Graduate Students : Career Development & Professional Connections : UMass Amherst Skip to main content The University of Massachusetts Amherst Open UMass Global Links Menu Visit Apply Give Search UMass.edu Menu Career Development & Professional Connections About Us Our Staff Career Centers Across UMass Our Newton Campus Handshake Login Student Outcomes Students Undergraduates Graduates Alumni Identity-Based Resources International Students Prospective Students UWW Students Employers Post Jobs and Internships Host an Event Career Fairs at UMass Why Recruit at UMass Internship Program Best Practices Recruiting Guidelines Contact Us Faculty Sponsor an Intern Career Events for Students Request a Presentation Resource Library Career Journey Expand Menu Item Self Discovery and Career Exploration Build Career Skills: Resumes, Job-searching, and Interviewing Learn Additional Technical, Creative, and Professional Skills Your Career Support Team Gain Experience: Internships, Co-ops, Research, and More! Is Graduate School Right for Me? Year-by-Year Checklist Tool Kits Expand Menu Item Resumes Cover Letters Career Fair Preparation Interviewing LinkedIn Learning Networking What Skills Do Employers Want? Applying to Grad School Photo Booth for Headshots Professional Wardrobe Closet Connections Expand Menu Item Career Communities Expand Menu Item Arts, Multimedia, and Entertainment Business, Financial Services, and Consulting Data and Information Technology Education, Human Services, and Counseling Engineering Government and Public Service Healthcare, Life Sciences, and Nursing Infrastructure and Transportation Law and Legal Services Research Sustainability, Environment, and Agriculture Career Centers Across UMass Expand Menu Item Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Education Engineering Graduate School Office of Professional Development Humanities & Fine Arts (HFA) Information & Computer Sciences (CICS) Isenberg School of Management (ISOM) Natural Sciences (CNS) Nursing Public Health and Health Sciences (SPHHS) Social & Behavioral Sciences (SBS) University Without Walls (UWW) Connect with UMass Alumni Using LinkedIn How to Network Jobs & Internships Expand Menu Item Internships, Co-ops, and Other Field Experiences Expand Menu Item Field Experience Definitions Internships Co-ops Research Civic Engagement and Service Learning Internships and Co-Ops at Charles River Campus UMass Internship Partner Programs Scholarships for Field Experiences Jobs Searching for Jobs & Internships Can I Do an Internship? Negotiating Job Offers Interviewing Using Handshake Career Resources for Graduate Students Welcome to the University of Massachusetts Career and Professional Development Hub. We are delighted to have you here and look forward to working with you as you prepare to embark on your professional career. Whether you are pursuing a master's or doctoral degree, we understand that career planning and development are crucial to your success. While graduate students obtain invaluable career guidance from the faculty in their respective fields, the Career Development Hub at UMass has collected resources to supplement your professional skill development. Whether you are looking to network with UMass Amherst alumni or are seeing unique opportunities to match your skills, you can get support on this site. We encourage you to take advantage of all the resources available to you during your time at UMass Amherst. Resources for Graduate Students Graduate students have unique needs depending on their course of study and career goals. Below is a list of curated resources design to help you hone your professional skills. Graduate School Office of Professional Development (OPD) Browse resources to support graduate students while at UMass, primarily through the 400+ workshops OPD hosts each year ranging from career skills to applying for grants. Beyond Graduate School Self-paced courses, workbooks, and live trainings/webinars to help Master's students develop the knowledge and confidence they need to successfully advance their careers. Beyond the Professoriate Unique curriculum, information, and strategies to help doctoral students confidently apply for faculty/academic jobs or to build a nonacademic career. Connect UMass Meet thousands of UMass Amherst alumni that are seeking to network with currently enrolled students. Career Communities are specialized affinity groups on the platform that specialize in 11 different industries. LinkedIn Learning LinkedIn Learning is a free resource made available to UMass Amherst students. LinkedIn Learning has thousands of courses in hundreds of disciplines. Jump into a 3 minute video or take a full 2 hour course at your own pace. Career Fairs UMass hosts over 20 career fairs on-campus every year. Meet employers in person and find out about opportunities in Massachusetts and beyond. International Student Resources The curated international students career page is a collection of information and resources to clarify what opportunities are available for international students. Graduate Student Resource Library A collection of guides and resources for graduate students seeking to develop their career skills, including resume and cover letter writing, virtual interview training, networking, and more. Career Development & Professional Connections Whether you’re wondering where to begin, looking for an internship, or starting your job search, we will guide you through the process of your unique career development. Address: Goodell Hall | 140 Hicks Way | Amherst, MA 01003 Main Office Number: (413) 545-2224 Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Footer Students Career Journey Career Centers Resource Library Employers Handshake Contact Us UMass collegiate M - University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2025 University of Massachusetts Amherst · Site Policies · Accessibility"
    },
    "https://www.umass.edu/careers/alumni": {
      "title": "Welcome UMass Amherst Alumni!",
      "description": "Alumni : Career Development & Professional Connections : UMass Amherst Skip to main content The University of Massachusetts Amherst Open UMass Global Links Menu Visit Apply Give Search UMass.edu Menu Career Development & Professional Connections About Us Our Staff Career Centers Across UMass Our Newton Campus Handshake Login Student Outcomes Students Undergraduates Graduates Alumni Identity-Based Resources International Students Prospective Students UWW Students Employers Post Jobs and Internships Host an Event Career Fairs at UMass Why Recruit at UMass Internship Program Best Practices Recruiting Guidelines Contact Us Faculty Sponsor an Intern Career Events for Students Request a Presentation Resource Library Career Journey Expand Menu Item Self Discovery and Career Exploration Build Career Skills: Resumes, Job-searching, and Interviewing Learn Additional Technical, Creative, and Professional Skills Your Career Support Team Gain Experience: Internships, Co-ops, Research, and More! Is Graduate School Right for Me? Year-by-Year Checklist Tool Kits Expand Menu Item Resumes Cover Letters Career Fair Preparation Interviewing LinkedIn Learning Networking What Skills Do Employers Want? Applying to Grad School Photo Booth for Headshots Professional Wardrobe Closet Connections Expand Menu Item Career Communities Expand Menu Item Arts, Multimedia, and Entertainment Business, Financial Services, and Consulting Data and Information Technology Education, Human Services, and Counseling Engineering Government and Public Service Healthcare, Life Sciences, and Nursing Infrastructure and Transportation Law and Legal Services Research Sustainability, Environment, and Agriculture Career Centers Across UMass Expand Menu Item Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Education Engineering Graduate School Office of Professional Development Humanities & Fine Arts (HFA) Information & Computer Sciences (CICS) Isenberg School of Management (ISOM) Natural Sciences (CNS) Nursing Public Health and Health Sciences (SPHHS) Social & Behavioral Sciences (SBS) University Without Walls (UWW) Connect with UMass Alumni Using LinkedIn How to Network Jobs & Internships Expand Menu Item Internships, Co-ops, and Other Field Experiences Expand Menu Item Field Experience Definitions Internships Co-ops Research Civic Engagement and Service Learning Internships and Co-Ops at Charles River Campus UMass Internship Partner Programs Scholarships for Field Experiences Jobs Searching for Jobs & Internships Can I Do an Internship? Negotiating Job Offers Interviewing Using Handshake Welcome UMass Amherst Alumni! As an alumni, you are an important part of the UMass Amherst community. Your career journey doesn't end after graduation, and UMass has career resources to aid in your professional success. Whether you're looking to make a career change, seeking professional development opportunities, or simply looking to connect with other alumni, we want to help. For undergraduate students who have graduated recently, many of the career centers offer support for the months after graduation, including job search assistance, career counseling, networking events, and much more. For graduate student alumni or undergraduate alumni who have graduated later, the UMass Alumni Office can connect you with professional career counselors to provide assistance. We also encourage you to share your expertise and knowledge with current students by joining Connect UMass, a virtual networking platform that can connect you with thousands of students and alumni. Career Resources for Alumni Career growth doesn't stop with graduating. Here is a small list of curated resources for UMass Amherst alumni: Visit the UMass Amherst Alumni Office Career page for advice on job searching, networking, and to view upcoming career events Speak with a UMass alumni professional career counselor for support on resume reviews, mock interviews, and life coaching Join Connect UMass to meet current students and network with other alumni from UMass Amherst Connect with other UMass Amherst alumni on the official alumni LinkedIn group Career Development & Professional Connections Whether you’re wondering where to begin, looking for an internship, or starting your job search, we will guide you through the process of your unique career development. Address: Goodell Hall | 140 Hicks Way | Amherst, MA 01003 Main Office Number: (413) 545-2224 Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Footer Students Career Journey Career Centers Resource Library Employers Handshake Contact Us UMass collegiate M - University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2025 University of Massachusetts Amherst · Site Policies · Accessibility"
    },
    "https://www.umass.edu/careers/identity-based-resources": {
      "title": "Identity-Based Resources",
      "description": "Identity-Based Resources : Career Development & Professional Connections : UMass Amherst Skip to main content The University of Massachusetts Amherst Open UMass Global Links Menu Visit Apply Give Search UMass.edu Menu Career Development & Professional Connections About Us Our Staff Career Centers Across UMass Our Newton Campus Handshake Login Student Outcomes Students Undergraduates Graduates Alumni Identity-Based Resources International Students Prospective Students UWW Students Employers Post Jobs and Internships Host an Event Career Fairs at UMass Why Recruit at UMass Internship Program Best Practices Recruiting Guidelines Contact Us Faculty Sponsor an Intern Career Events for Students Request a Presentation Resource Library Career Journey Expand Menu Item Self Discovery and Career Exploration Build Career Skills: Resumes, Job-searching, and Interviewing Learn Additional Technical, Creative, and Professional Skills Your Career Support Team Gain Experience: Internships, Co-ops, Research, and More! Is Graduate School Right for Me? Year-by-Year Checklist Tool Kits Expand Menu Item Resumes Cover Letters Career Fair Preparation Interviewing LinkedIn Learning Networking What Skills Do Employers Want? Applying to Grad School Photo Booth for Headshots Professional Wardrobe Closet Connections Expand Menu Item Career Communities Expand Menu Item Arts, Multimedia, and Entertainment Business, Financial Services, and Consulting Data and Information Technology Education, Human Services, and Counseling Engineering Government and Public Service Healthcare, Life Sciences, and Nursing Infrastructure and Transportation Law and Legal Services Research Sustainability, Environment, and Agriculture Career Centers Across UMass Expand Menu Item Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Education Engineering Graduate School Office of Professional Development Humanities & Fine Arts (HFA) Information & Computer Sciences (CICS) Isenberg School of Management (ISOM) Natural Sciences (CNS) Nursing Public Health and Health Sciences (SPHHS) Social & Behavioral Sciences (SBS) University Without Walls (UWW) Connect with UMass Alumni Using LinkedIn How to Network Jobs & Internships Expand Menu Item Internships, Co-ops, and Other Field Experiences Expand Menu Item Field Experience Definitions Internships Co-ops Research Civic Engagement and Service Learning Internships and Co-Ops at Charles River Campus UMass Internship Partner Programs Scholarships for Field Experiences Jobs Searching for Jobs & Internships Can I Do an Internship? Negotiating Job Offers Interviewing Using Handshake Identity-Based Resources Careers Identity Based Resources We are committed to providing UMass Amherst students with tools for ongoing professional success.  In addition to the myriad of resources available on our site, we've compiled a list of resources to help supplement the job search process for students based on identity. We understand that identity is intersectional and complex, and that any list of resources might feel incomplete. We will continue to update this page with additional links. Overall Resources Best Companies for Women: June 2024 Best Companies for Women: June 2024 Dear Female Job Seeker Dear Female Job Seeker Diversity Working Diversity Working Diversity.com Diversity.com Forbes' America’s Best Employers for Diversity Forbes' America’s Best Employers for Diversity IMDiversity IMDiversity Inclusive Hiring Inclusive Hiring Management Leadership Tomorrow Management Leadership Tomorrow BIPOC Students These links are dedicated to providing you with resources that celebrate diversity, equity, and inclusion in the professional world. From internships and scholarships to mentorship programs and networking opportunities, these resources are tailored to support your success and empowerment. Browse these resources and discover a opportunities to help you thrive in your chosen field. BIA US Bureau of Indian Affairs BIA US Bureau of Indian Affairs Black Career Women's Network Black Career Women's Network The Black Collegiate Employers The Black Collegiate Employers Black Engineer Black Engineer Find Native American Programs Find Native American Programs Hispanic Career Alliance Hispanic Career Alliance Internships and Fellowships for Native Americans Internships and Fellowships for Native Americans Jopwell Jopwell Nemnet Nemnet Saludos Saludos First Generation Students There are unique challenges and experiences that come with being the first in your family to pursue higher education and navigate the professional world. We've compiled these links to provide you with the guidance, inspiration, for your career journey. These resources are designed to empower you with the knowledge and opportunities to thrive in your chosen field. A Career Roadmap for First Gen A Career Roadmap for First Gen Federal Trio Program Federal Trio Program First Gen Fellows First Gen Fellows I’m First I’m First Jobs and Internships for First Generation Grads Jobs and Internships for First Generation Grads International Student Resources These resources are dedicated to providing essential resources for navigating your career path as an international student. From internships and co-op opportunities to visa regulations and work authorization guidelines, these resources are tailored to address the specific needs and challenges faced by international students studying in the US. International Student and Scholar Services (UMass Amherst) International Student and Scholar Services (UMass Amherst) Employers that Hired UMass International Students (Handshake access required) Employers that Hired UMass International Students (Handshake access required) H1B Visa Jobs H1B Visa Jobs The International Advantage The International Advantage International Student Job Search International Student Job Search MyVisaJobs MyVisaJobs OPT Nation OPT Nation United OPT United OPT UNIWORLD: Directories of American Firms Operating in Foreign Countries and Fore… UNIWORLD: Directories of American Firms Operating in Foreign Countries and Fore… LGBTQ+ Students From LGBTQ+ friendly employers and mentorship programs to resources on inclusion, these links are designed to help you thrive as you are in your chosen field. Human Rights Workplace Human Rights Workplace Out Professionals Out Professionals Pride at Work Pride at Work Neurodiverse Students and Students with Disabilities These links aim to connect you with resources, organizations, and tools tailored to empower neurodiverse individuals and those with disabilities. Whether you're job searching or seeking guidance on how to request accommodations, these links will equip you with the knowledge and support you need to thrive in your chosen career path. Explore these resources and unlock a world of possibilities tailored to your unique strengths and talents. UMass Amherst Disability Resources for Students UMass Amherst Disability Resources for Students Disability Scoop Disability Scoop Disability:IN Disability:IN Guide to Scholarships and Resources for Students with Disabilities Guide to Scholarships and Resources for Students with Disabilities Integrate Integrate Job Accommodations Network Job Accommodations Network Lime Connect Lime Connect Massachusetts Rehabilitation Commission Massachusetts Rehabilitation Commission Mentra: Neurodiverse Employment Network Mentra: Neurodiverse Employment Network National Organization on Disability National Organization on Disability Neurodiversity Career Connector Neurodiversity Career Connector Work Without Limits Work Without Limits Veterans Students with a background from the military bring unique skills that can benefit them when applying for positions in the civilian world. From translating your military experience into a civilian resume to connecting with veteran-friendly employers and accessing educational and training programs, these resources will equip you with the tools and knowledge to thrive in your post-service career. GI Jobs GI Jobs Hire a Hero Hire a Hero Military Hire Military Hire Veteran's Guide to Job Hunting in the Civilian Market Veteran's Guide to Job Hunting in the Civilian Market Veterans Job Search Veterans Job Search Career Development & Professional Connections Whether you’re wondering where to begin, looking for an internship, or starting your job search, we will guide you through the process of your unique career development. Address: Goodell Hall | 140 Hicks Way | Amherst, MA 01003 Main Office Number: (413) 545-2224 Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Footer Students Career Journey Career Centers Resource Library Employers Handshake Contact Us UMass collegiate M - University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2025 University of Massachusetts Amherst · Site Policies · Accessibility"
