    "https://www.umass.edu/careers/employers/post-jobs-and-internships": {
      "title": "Post Jobs and Internships",
      "description": "Post Jobs and Internships : Career Development & Professional Connections : UMass Amherst Skip to main content The University of Massachusetts Amherst Open UMass Global Links Menu Visit Apply Give Search UMass.edu Menu Career Development & Professional Connections About Us Our Staff Career Centers Across UMass Our Newton Campus Handshake Login Student Outcomes Students Undergraduates Graduates Alumni Identity-Based Resources International Students Prospective Students UWW Students Employers Post Jobs and Internships Host an Event Career Fairs at UMass Why Recruit at UMass Internship Program Best Practices Recruiting Guidelines Contact Us Faculty Sponsor an Intern Career Events for Students Request a Presentation Resource Library Career Journey Expand Menu Item Self Discovery and Career Exploration Build Career Skills: Resumes, Job-searching, and Interviewing Learn Additional Technical, Creative, and Professional Skills Your Career Support Team Gain Experience: Internships, Co-ops, Research, and More! Is Graduate School Right for Me? Year-by-Year Checklist Tool Kits Expand Menu Item Resumes Cover Letters Career Fair Preparation Interviewing LinkedIn Learning Networking What Skills Do Employers Want? Applying to Grad School Photo Booth for Headshots Professional Wardrobe Closet Connections Expand Menu Item Career Communities Expand Menu Item Arts, Multimedia, and Entertainment Business, Financial Services, and Consulting Data and Information Technology Education, Human Services, and Counseling Engineering Government and Public Service Healthcare, Life Sciences, and Nursing Infrastructure and Transportation Law and Legal Services Research Sustainability, Environment, and Agriculture Career Centers Across UMass Expand Menu Item Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Education Engineering Graduate School Office of Professional Development Humanities & Fine Arts (HFA) Information & Computer Sciences (CICS) Isenberg School of Management (ISOM) Natural Sciences (CNS) Nursing Public Health and Health Sciences (SPHHS) Social & Behavioral Sciences (SBS) University Without Walls (UWW) Connect with UMass Alumni Using LinkedIn How to Network Jobs & Internships Expand Menu Item Internships, Co-ops, and Other Field Experiences Expand Menu Item Field Experience Definitions Internships Co-ops Research Civic Engagement and Service Learning Internships and Co-Ops at Charles River Campus UMass Internship Partner Programs Scholarships for Field Experiences Jobs Searching for Jobs & Internships Can I Do an Internship? Negotiating Job Offers Interviewing Using Handshake Post Jobs and Internships Careers Employers Post Jobs And Internships Close Menu Employers: Quick Links Handshake Login Career Fairs UMass Amherst Academic Calendar Contact Us Handshake For career/major related employment, UMass Amherst uses Handshake , a free job board and internship platform that employers can use to post a job or internship. This allows students and recent alumni to search and easily apply according to the directions you specify in your job ad. Handshake Best Practices Setting Up an Account on Handshake If you don’t have a Handshake account, signing up is free and easy. Step-by-step directions on how to make an account can be found on Handshake . It only takes a few minutes. After signing up with Handshake, be sure to add University of Massachusetts Amherst as one of your schools so you can post jobs to our students and alumni: Directions for Adding a School . UMass Amherst students are very savvy with Handshake and often go there as a first stop when looking for work opportunities, so this is definitely a great way to ensure the most fair and equitable distribution of your roles for our entire student population. Maximizing Your Company Profile The following fields are key fields to populate in your Handshake profile: Description Please keep in mind the information you include here is to inform a potential hire about your company and to provide a basic overview of what you do in terms anyone can understand. This language may need to be a little different than what is found on your website for a potential customer/client. Key information to highlight includes: What the company does and/or the company mission Who are your customers Briefly highlight what makes your organization unique Location(s) – for employers local to campus, include accessible by PVTA if relevant Social Media Links (LinkedIn, Facebook, Twitter) Students love to research and social media is their go-to research tool. If your company utilizes any of these social media tools, populate the Handshake fields for LinkedIn, Facebook and Twitter page links to guide students to your organization. Logo and Banner If possible, upload both a logo (square) and banner (horizontal) to your profile, which will make ensure a professional appearance for your organization. Posting a Successful Job Opportunity The more fields you complete when posting a job opportunity, the more well defined your posting will be, and the more likely you will attract well-qualified candidates. Here are some important fields to pay particular attention to when posting your roles on Handshake: Job Title Use a title that accurately describes the job function For internships and co-ops, add the word intern, internship, or co-op to your title. Additionally, it is helpful to include the season/year you are seeking to have the intern work (ex: Fall 2023 or Summer 2024) Graduation Date Range The common recommendation is to skip entering a graduation date range and use the “School Years” picker instead There are many instances where employers accidentally choose conflicting graduation dates and school years and then by default no students match the position Selecting Majors in a Posting Choose major groups or individual majors purposefully Make sure the qualifications listed in your job description match the majors you have selected Handshake utilizes an AI feature that suggests potential matching job opportunities to students. One of the key fields used in the AI matching is major. The more purposeful you are about selecting the best fitting majors for your postings, the more likely the students you are seeking will see your postings at the top of their search results. Students tell us they are looking for employers who are specifically looking for them. When students conduct a job search in Handshake they use filters to find jobs where there is a potential match. Many students use the filters for Job Type, School Year, and Major. Posting a job in Handshake takes about 5-10 minutes. This Handshake help article will walk you through all the steps and explain each of the fields: How to Post a Job Tips for Writing a Great Student Internship Posting A well thought out internship posting will make students excited about what your company does and the opportunity to learn within your organization. And most importantly, it will proactively answer most of the questions a student may have about the internship, which will make it more likely they will hit the apply button. These are the important sections for writing a great Student Internship Posting: Internship Job Title Use a job title that has meaning to a college student and will also look attractive on their resume The job title should include the description of the job function and the word “intern” or “internship” Also include the season/year you are seeking to have an intern work (ex: Fall 2022 or Summer 2023) Company Description Briefly explain what your company does and/or the mission Highlight what makes your organization unique; why would someone want to work here? Position Description Describe the role the intern will perform Explain how this internship experience will benefit the company Describe the learning benefits and outcomes for the student Desired Qualifications Professional skills (often referred to as soft skills) Technical skills and experience School year and/or expected graduation date Relevant Details – this may include the following: Compensation Length of internship opportunity Desired schedule and/or hours Virtual, In-Person, or Hybrid work schedule Application instructions and deadlines Work attire Include accessibility by public transportation if relevant Student Job Board For part-time and seasonal work opportunities, the UMass Student Job Board is available for local employers to advertise non-major/non-career related work opportunities for students. Career Development & Professional Connections Whether you’re wondering where to begin, looking for an internship, or starting your job search, we will guide you through the process of your unique career development. Address: Goodell Hall | 140 Hicks Way | Amherst, MA 01003 Main Office Number: (413) 545-2224 Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Footer Students Career Journey Career Centers Resource Library Employers Handshake Contact Us UMass collegiate M - University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2025 University of Massachusetts Amherst · Site Policies · Accessibility"
    },
    "https://www.umass.edu/careers/employers/host-event": {
      "title": "Host an Event",
      "description": "Host an Event : Career Development & Professional Connections : UMass Amherst Skip to main content The University of Massachusetts Amherst Open UMass Global Links Menu Visit Apply Give Search UMass.edu Menu Career Development & Professional Connections About Us Our Staff Career Centers Across UMass Our Newton Campus Handshake Login Student Outcomes Students Undergraduates Graduates Alumni Identity-Based Resources International Students Prospective Students UWW Students Employers Post Jobs and Internships Host an Event Career Fairs at UMass Why Recruit at UMass Internship Program Best Practices Recruiting Guidelines Contact Us Faculty Sponsor an Intern Career Events for Students Request a Presentation Resource Library Career Journey Expand Menu Item Self Discovery and Career Exploration Build Career Skills: Resumes, Job-searching, and Interviewing Learn Additional Technical, Creative, and Professional Skills Your Career Support Team Gain Experience: Internships, Co-ops, Research, and More! Is Graduate School Right for Me? Year-by-Year Checklist Tool Kits Expand Menu Item Resumes Cover Letters Career Fair Preparation Interviewing LinkedIn Learning Networking What Skills Do Employers Want? Applying to Grad School Photo Booth for Headshots Professional Wardrobe Closet Connections Expand Menu Item Career Communities Expand Menu Item Arts, Multimedia, and Entertainment Business, Financial Services, and Consulting Data and Information Technology Education, Human Services, and Counseling Engineering Government and Public Service Healthcare, Life Sciences, and Nursing Infrastructure and Transportation Law and Legal Services Research Sustainability, Environment, and Agriculture Career Centers Across UMass Expand Menu Item Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Education Engineering Graduate School Office of Professional Development Humanities & Fine Arts (HFA) Information & Computer Sciences (CICS) Isenberg School of Management (ISOM) Natural Sciences (CNS) Nursing Public Health and Health Sciences (SPHHS) Social & Behavioral Sciences (SBS) University Without Walls (UWW) Connect with UMass Alumni Using LinkedIn How to Network Jobs & Internships Expand Menu Item Internships, Co-ops, and Other Field Experiences Expand Menu Item Field Experience Definitions Internships Co-ops Research Civic Engagement and Service Learning Internships and Co-Ops at Charles River Campus UMass Internship Partner Programs Scholarships for Field Experiences Jobs Searching for Jobs & Internships Can I Do an Internship? Negotiating Job Offers Interviewing Using Handshake Host an Event Careers Employers Host Event Close Menu Employers: Quick Links Handshake Login Career Fairs UMass Amherst Academic Calendar Contact Us The Career Hub will host organizations for recruiting events that span multiple majors.  These events include information sessions, tabling, meet-ups, etc. These types of recruiting events are limited to no more than two per semester. Individual college career centers maintain their own policies for on-campus recruitment. Information Sessions and Workshops UMass Career Hub offers space for information sessions and workshops at no cost. Please contact Tiffany Appleton to make arrangements. Contact Tiffany Contact Tiffany On-Campus Interviews On-campus interviewing is available through the Career Hub. Please contact Tiffany Appleton for help with scheduling. In addition, some career centers provide on-campus interview space. Please contact the career center staff (below) for more information. Contact List for Career Centers Contact List for Career Centers Tabling The Career Hub offers an opportunity for employer tabling on the Goodell Lawn. This outdoor location in the center of campus is a heavily trafficked area great for chatting with students of many majors. Please note, tabling inside the student-run, Student Union Building is only allowed through partnering directly with a student organization host. Contact Tiffany Contact Tiffany Virtual Events Career Services is happy to partner with you to schedule and promote your virtual offerings for our students. For events that span multiple majors, contact Tiffany Appleton ( [email protected] ). For events targeting a specific major, contact the individual career center below for more details. Employers > Contact Us Contact List for Career Centers Other Recruiting Events We are here to help you find the best way to connect with students based upon your recruiting needs including networking events, pop-ups, facility tours, and other unique opportunities. Let us know what you are thinking and we are happy to brainstorm ideas with you too. Contact List for Career Centers Contact List for Career Centers Career Development & Professional Connections Whether you’re wondering where to begin, looking for an internship, or starting your job search, we will guide you through the process of your unique career development. Address: Goodell Hall | 140 Hicks Way | Amherst, MA 01003 Main Office Number: (413) 545-2224 Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Footer Students Career Journey Career Centers Resource Library Employers Handshake Contact Us UMass collegiate M - University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2025 University of Massachusetts Amherst · Site Policies · Accessibility"
    },
