ciences (CNS) Nursing Public Health and Health Sciences (SPHHS) Social & Behavioral Sciences (SBS) University Without Walls (UWW) Connect with UMass Alumni Using LinkedIn How to Network Jobs & Internships Expand Menu Item Internships, Co-ops, and Other Field Experiences Expand Menu Item Field Experience Definitions Internships Co-ops Research Civic Engagement and Service Learning Internships and Co-Ops at Charles River Campus UMass Internship Partner Programs Scholarships for Field Experiences Jobs Searching for Jobs & Internships Can I Do an Internship? Negotiating Job Offers Interviewing Using Handshake Faculty Careers Faculty Partner with Career Services at UMass to Support Our Students Faculty are instrumental partners when it comes to connecting students with the experience they need to achieve meaningful professional lives. Whether you’re interested in sponsoring internships, requesting in-classroom support, demonstrating how to use Handshake most effectively, or staying informed about upcoming career events, we're here to support you. Explore the resources below to enhance your students’ career readiness and strengthen their professional development journey. Career Advising Resources for UMass Faculty Sponsor an Internship or Co-op Career Events for UMass Students Request a Presentation Career Resources for Students Handshake Handshake is UMass Amherst's official career platform where students can find internships, jobs, and career events—all tailored to their major and interests. UMass students can use it to book appointments with career advisors in their college, connect with employers, and register for career fairs and events. Handshake Read More How to Use Handshake This guide helps students get started with Handshake, from creating their profile and scheduling appointments with career advisors to applying for jobs, internships, and attending virtual career fairs. How to Use Handshake Read More Experiential Learning Registration - Instructors Guide A step-by-step guide on how to manage Experiential Learning Requests in SPIRE. It includes instructions for reviewing student requests, editing submitted information, uploading or viewing documents, and either approving or denying requests. Experiential Learning Registration - Instructors Guide Read More Experiential Learning Registration - Student Guide UMass requires students to submit an Experiential Learning Request when participating in internships, co-ops, practicums, and externships. This process helps track students' involvement in these educational opportunities, as well as register them for credit and/or proper status through the University. Experiential Learning Registration - Student Guide Read More Career Development & Professional Connections Whether you’re wondering where to begin, looking for an internship, or starting your job search, we will guide you through the process of your unique career development. Address: Goodell Hall | 140 Hicks Way | Amherst, MA 01003 Main Office Number: (413) 545-2224 Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Footer Students Career Journey Career Centers Resource Library Employers Handshake Contact Us UMass collegiate M - University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2025 University of Massachusetts Amherst · Site Policies · Accessibility"
