      "title": "Career Journey",
      "description": "Career Journey : Career Development & Professional Connections : UMass Amherst Skip to main content The University of Massachusetts Amherst Open UMass Global Links Menu Visit Apply Give Search UMass.edu Menu Career Development & Professional Connections About Us Our Staff Career Centers Across UMass Our Newton Campus Handshake Login Student Outcomes Students Undergraduates Graduates Alumni Identity-Based Resources International Students Prospective Students UWW Students Employers Post Jobs and Internships Host an Event Career Fairs at UMass Why Recruit at UMass Internship Program Best Practices Recruiting Guidelines Contact Us Faculty Sponsor an Intern Career Events for Students Request a Presentation Resource Library Career Journey Expand Menu Item Self Discovery and Career Exploration Build Career Skills: Resumes, Job-searching, and Interviewing Learn Additional Technical, Creative, and Professional Skills Your Career Support Team Gain Experience: Internships, Co-ops, Research, and More! Is Graduate School Right for Me? Year-by-Year Checklist Tool Kits Expand Menu Item Resumes Cover Letters Career Fair Preparation Interviewing LinkedIn Learning Networking What Skills Do Employers Want? Applying to Grad School Photo Booth for Headshots Professional Wardrobe Closet Connections Expand Menu Item Career Communities Expand Menu Item Arts, Multimedia, and Entertainment Business, Financial Services, and Consulting Data and Information Technology Education, Human Services, and Counseling Engineering Government and Public Service Healthcare, Life Sciences, and Nursing Infrastructure and Transportation Law and Legal Services Research Sustainability, Environment, and Agriculture Career Centers Across UMass Expand Menu Item Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Education Engineering Graduate School Office of Professional Development Humanities & Fine Arts (HFA) Information & Computer Sciences (CICS) Isenberg School of Management (ISOM) Natural Sciences (CNS) Nursing Public Health and Health Sciences (SPHHS) Social & Behavioral Sciences (SBS) University Without Walls (UWW) Connect with UMass Alumni Using LinkedIn How to Network Jobs & Internships Expand Menu Item Internships, Co-ops, and Other Field Experiences Expand Menu Item Field Experience Definitions Internships Co-ops Research Civic Engagement and Service Learning Internships and Co-Ops at Charles River Campus UMass Internship Partner Programs Scholarships for Field Experiences Jobs Searching for Jobs & Internships Can I Do an Internship? Negotiating Job Offers Interviewing Using Handshake Career Journey Close Menu Career Journey Menu Overview Self Discovery Build Career Skills Learn Additional Skills Career Support Team Gain Experience Graduate School Year-by-Year Checklist Get Started on Your Career Journey! Your Career Journey, like other types of journeys, is the passage from one place or stage of life to another, with each stage bringing increased knowledge, learned skills, and new insights. The journey is made easier through assessments of self, majors, career fields, and employers, as well as skills development and professional connections.  UMass Career Services is here to guide you on this journey and to provide resources that will make the twists and turns easier and more effective. Think of this website as your roadmap to the future.  Let the adventure begin! Self Discovery and Career Exploration Self-assessments help you gain an understanding of your strengths, skills, and interests. Career exploration tools map those strengths and interests to meaningful careers and provide insights that can make you a marketable candidate to employers. Build Career Skills: Resumes, Job-searching, and Interviewing UMass Career Services provides assistance building a wide range of career skills such as resume and cover letter writing, job searching, interview preparation, and more. Learn Additional Technical, Creative, and Professional Skills Make sure you have developed the skills and competencies that employers are looking for. Supplement your academic learning through online badges and certificates. Your Career Support Team Your UMass Career Advisor will help you navigate your career path. Connect with them early to get the best possible start on your professional journey. Faculty, staff, peers, and alumni can also be great supports along the journey. Begin building these key relationships to help navigate the way. Gain Experience: Internships, Co-ops, Research, and More! Hands-on experiences gained in the workplace equip students with technical and professional skills, facilitate career exploration, and provide opportunities to make professional connections. Is Graduate School Right for Me? If you are deciding whether graduate school is the direction for you to go after graduation, these tips can help guide your decision-making. Year-by-Year Checklist Career Development & Professional Connections Whether you’re wondering where to begin, looking for an internship, or starting your job search, we will guide you through the process of your unique career development. Address: Goodell Hall | 140 Hicks Way | Amherst, MA 01003 Main Office Number: (413) 545-2224 Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Footer Students Career Journey Career Centers Resource Library Employers Handshake Contact Us UMass collegiate M - University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2025 University of Massachusetts Amherst · Site Policies · Accessibility"
