 (ISOM) Natural Sciences (CNS) Nursing Public Health and Health Sciences (SPHHS) Social & Behavioral Sciences (SBS) University Without Walls (UWW) Connect with UMass Alumni Using LinkedIn How to Network Jobs & Internships Expand Menu Item Internships, Co-ops, and Other Field Experiences Expand Menu Item Field Experience Definitions Internships Co-ops Research Civic Engagement and Service Learning Internships and Co-Ops at Charles River Campus UMass Internship Partner Programs Scholarships for Field Experiences Jobs Searching for Jobs & Internships Can I Do an Internship? Negotiating Job Offers Interviewing Using Handshake Your Career Support Team Careers Career Journey Support Team Close Menu Career Journey Menu Overview Self Discovery Build Career Skills Learn Additional Skills Career Support Team Gain Experience Graduate School Year-by-Year Checklist UMass Amherst has a hybrid \"hub and spoke\" model for Career Services. The Career Development and Professional Connections office serves as the \"Hub\", while career centers across campus serve as the \"Spokes\". The goal of our structure is to provide major-specific career content knowledge to students while also providing efficient, \"one-stop\" service to employers who are looking to engage with students across disciplines. We also have a dedicated career services professional on our Charles River campus in Newton, MA. Career Centers Across UMass Amherst Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Education College of Education Riccio College of Engineering Riccio College of Engineering College of Humanities & Fine Arts College of Humanities & Fine Arts College of Natural Sciences College of Natural Sciences College of Social & Behavioral Sciences College of Social & Behavioral Sciences Nursing Elaine Marieb College of Nursing Isenberg School of Management Isenberg School of Management Manning College of Information & Computer Sciences Manning College of Information & Computer Sciences School of Public Health & Health Sciences School of Public Health & Health Sciences University Without Walls Career Services University Without Walls Career Services Graduate School Office of Professional Development Graduate School Office of Professional Development Charles River Campus Internship and Co-ops Charles River Campus Internship and Co-ops Next Up: Gain Professional Experience Career Development & Professional Connections Whether you’re wondering where to begin, looking for an internship, or starting your job search, we will guide you through the process of your unique career development. Address: Goodell Hall | 140 Hicks Way | Amherst, MA 01003 Main Office Number: (413) 545-2224 Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Footer Students Career Journey Career Centers Resource Library Employers Handshake Contact Us UMass collegiate M - University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2025 University of Massachusetts Amherst · Site Policies · Accessibility"
