    "https://www.umass.edu/careers/connections": {
      "title": "Connections",
      "description": "Connections : Career Development & Professional Connections : UMass Amherst Skip to main content The University of Massachusetts Amherst Open UMass Global Links Menu Visit Apply Give Search UMass.edu Menu Career Development & Professional Connections About Us Our Staff Career Centers Across UMass Our Newton Campus Handshake Login Student Outcomes Students Undergraduates Graduates Alumni Identity-Based Resources International Students Prospective Students UWW Students Employers Post Jobs and Internships Host an Event Career Fairs at UMass Why Recruit at UMass Internship Program Best Practices Recruiting Guidelines Contact Us Faculty Sponsor an Intern Career Events for Students Request a Presentation Resource Library Career Journey Expand Menu Item Self Discovery and Career Exploration Build Career Skills: Resumes, Job-searching, and Interviewing Learn Additional Technical, Creative, and Professional Skills Your Career Support Team Gain Experience: Internships, Co-ops, Research, and More! Is Graduate School Right for Me? Year-by-Year Checklist Tool Kits Expand Menu Item Resumes Cover Letters Career Fair Preparation Interviewing LinkedIn Learning Networking What Skills Do Employers Want? Applying to Grad School Photo Booth for Headshots Professional Wardrobe Closet Connections Expand Menu Item Career Communities Expand Menu Item Arts, Multimedia, and Entertainment Business, Financial Services, and Consulting Data and Information Technology Education, Human Services, and Counseling Engineering Government and Public Service Healthcare, Life Sciences, and Nursing Infrastructure and Transportation Law and Legal Services Research Sustainability, Environment, and Agriculture Career Centers Across UMass Expand Menu Item Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Education Engineering Graduate School Office of Professional Development Humanities & Fine Arts (HFA) Information & Computer Sciences (CICS) Isenberg School of Management (ISOM) Natural Sciences (CNS) Nursing Public Health and Health Sciences (SPHHS) Social & Behavioral Sciences (SBS) University Without Walls (UWW) Connect with UMass Alumni Using LinkedIn How to Network Jobs & Internships Expand Menu Item Internships, Co-ops, and Other Field Experiences Expand Menu Item Field Experience Definitions Internships Co-ops Research Civic Engagement and Service Learning Internships and Co-Ops at Charles River Campus UMass Internship Partner Programs Scholarships for Field Experiences Jobs Searching for Jobs & Internships Can I Do an Internship? Negotiating Job Offers Interviewing Using Handshake Connections Careers Connections These resources will help you make meaningful connections with peers, alumni, and employers. Career Communities Career Communities Our eleven UMass Career Communities are based on industries and interests rather than on academic majors. Through Career Communities you can explore how you would apply your knowledge, skills, and interests to a range of careers AND connect with alumni who are working in those fields! Connect UMass Connect UMass Connect UMass is a platform that connects current students with alumni for conversations about careers, mentoring, and professional development. Connect UMass makes it easy for students to log on and network with alumni who are happy to help you out! Using LinkedIn Using LinkedIn LinkedIn is a professional network community designed to help students and employees make business connections, share their experiences, and showcase their resumes to find and apply for jobs. Go to www.LinkedIn.com to start creating your own profile page. How to Network How to Network The way we interact with others affects our ability to demonstrate our career-related interests, skills, and abilities. These tools will help you to effectively exchange information and develop professional connections. Career Development & Professional Connections Whether you’re wondering where to begin, looking for an internship, or starting your job search, we will guide you through the process of your unique career development. Address: Goodell Hall | 140 Hicks Way | Amherst, MA 01003 Main Office Number: (413) 545-2224 Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Footer Students Career Journey Career Centers Resource Library Employers Handshake Contact Us UMass collegiate M - University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2025 University of Massachusetts Amherst · Site Policies · Accessibility"
