    "https://www.umass.edu/careers/connections/career-communities/arts-multimedia-and-entertainment-career-community": {
      "title": "Arts, Multimedia, and Entertainment Career Community",
      "description": "Arts, Multimedia, and Entertainment Career Community : Career Development & Professional Connections : UMass Amherst Skip to main content The University of Massachusetts Amherst Open UMass Global Links Menu Visit Apply Give Search UMass.edu Menu Career Development & Professional Connections About Us Our Staff Career Centers Across UMass Our Newton Campus Handshake Login Student Outcomes Students Undergraduates Graduates Alumni Identity-Based Resources International Students Prospective Students UWW Students Employers Post Jobs and Internships Host an Event Career Fairs at UMass Why Recruit at UMass Internship Program Best Practices Recruiting Guidelines Contact Us Faculty Sponsor an Intern Career Events for Students Request a Presentation Resource Library Career Journey Expand Menu Item Self Discovery and Career Exploration Build Career Skills: Resumes, Job-searching, and Interviewing Learn Additional Technical, Creative, and Professional Skills Your Career Support Team Gain Experience: Internships, Co-ops, Research, and More! Is Graduate School Right for Me? Year-by-Year Checklist Tool Kits Expand Menu Item Resumes Cover Letters Career Fair Preparation Interviewing LinkedIn Learning Networking What Skills Do Employers Want? Applying to Grad School Photo Booth for Headshots Professional Wardrobe Closet Connections Expand Menu Item Career Communities Expand Menu Item Arts, Multimedia, and Entertainment Business, Financial Services, and Consulting Data and Information Technology Education, Human Services, and Counseling Engineering Government and Public Service Healthcare, Life Sciences, and Nursing Infrastructure and Transportation Law and Legal Services Research Sustainability, Environment, and Agriculture Career Centers Across UMass Expand Menu Item Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Education Engineering Graduate School Office of Professional Development Humanities & Fine Arts (HFA) Information & Computer Sciences (CICS) Isenberg School of Management (ISOM) Natural Sciences (CNS) Nursing Public Health and Health Sciences (SPHHS) Social & Behavioral Sciences (SBS) University Without Walls (UWW) Connect with UMass Alumni Using LinkedIn How to Network Jobs & Internships Expand Menu Item Internships, Co-ops, and Other Field Experiences Expand Menu Item Field Experience Definitions Internships Co-ops Research Civic Engagement and Service Learning Internships and Co-Ops at Charles River Campus UMass Internship Partner Programs Scholarships for Field Experiences Jobs Searching for Jobs & Internships Can I Do an Internship? Negotiating Job Offers Interviewing Using Handshake https://www.connectumassalumni.com/hub/umassamherst/groups/arts-multimedia-and-entertainment-career-community/about?showBack=true Learn More Arts, Multimedia, and Entertainment Career Community Arts, Multimedia and Entertainment professionals are creative, innovative professionals who work across various art, media, and performance industries. These careers are full of opportunities in not just digital and physical media, but also within hospitality, recreation, and any other creative expression. These roles help foster creativity, inspire emotion, and also provide a powerful means of communication. Through various mediums they connect individuals and communities across time and culture. Through their work, experts in these fields foster community through creative expression, continually redefining the meaning of art and its impact on society throughout the years. Is This Field Right for Me? What are Creative Industries? Creative industries are all around us. They can be seen in the clothes we wear, the buildings we live and work in, the music we listen to, the books we read, the adverts on our screens, the apps we use and in countless other places. When you take a good look, the creative industries show up everywhere in our daily lives and the world would be quite a different place without them. What are Creative Industries? Read More Jobs in this Field 24 Jobs in Multimedia Multimedia is a growing field with a range of opportunities for creative professionals. Jobs in this field allow you to use your technical skills and artistic passion to work on exciting projects. In this article, we discuss what jobs in multimedia are, the career outlook, salary and workplace environment for careers and multimedia and diverse types of jobs in multimedia. 24 Jobs in Multimedia Read More 12 Interesting Jobs for Creative People (With Salaries) Careers in creative fields usually involve imagination and original thinking, particularly through the creation of original work in the arts and media. Often, creative jobs require both dedication and time that extends beyond traditional business hours. Understanding some of the options for a creative career can help you find the right job for you. 12 Interesting Jobs for Creative People (With Salaries) Read More 25 Creative Jobs and Careers for Creative People Creativity is far from just a skill; it is an essential part of an identity. Why settle for a career that does not allow creative individuals to shine? Creative people deserve equally creative careers! 25 Creative Jobs and Careers for Creative People Read More Certifications and LinkedIn Learning Recommendations Certifications and supplemental classes can round out your education and help you explore new areas of interest. Below are a few ways you can customize your education while at UMass. 3D and Animation Careers: First Steps Take your first step into the 3D animation pipeline. Animator and educator George Maestri reviews the software and processes involved in bringing 3D characters and scenes to life, including modeling, texturing, rigging, animation, and rendering with lights and cameras 3D and Animation Careers: First Steps Read More Advance your Video Editing Skills Get the skills you need to edit videos using professional tools such as Adobe Premiere Pro and Apple Final Cut Pro. The courses in this learning path will help you develop a solid foundation in everything from story structure and editing techniques to dialog editing and color correction. Advance your Video Editing Skills Read More Contracting for Creatives Get an overview of the types of contracts that you can expect to see, the situations in which a particular type is used, and the specific red flags inherent in each. Seth discusses NDA (Non-Disclosure Agreement), work-for-hire and contractor agreements, and proposals, quotes, and SOWs. Contracting for Creatives Read More Creative Conventions of Film Editing Explore creative video editing techniques with a comprehensive study that includes both artistic analysis and technical instruction. Creative Conventions of Film Editing Read More Making a Short Film Explore the basic elements of screenwriting, production, and directing. This comprehensive beginner’s course is for anyone who has good ideas that they want to share with the world. Writer, director, and producer Avi Glijansky teaches the theory, skills, and core craft of visual storytelling for the big screen. Learn how to write your scripts; manage cameras, lighting, and sound; and work with actors. Plus, find out how to plan your production and keep your set running smoothly. Making a Short Film Read More Premier Pro Training This course helps beginners unlock the potential of the latest edition, Premiere Pro 2022. Instructor and filmmaker Ashley Kennedy teaches all the essentials while building a short promo video from start to finish. Premier Pro Training Read More Starting a Career in Design In this Creative Inspirations documentary, Kit shares highlights of recent projects, his renowned collection of American flags and American flag memorabilia, as well as the irrefutable wisdom of one who has stayed at the top of his game for five decades. Starting a Career in Design Read More Video Post-Production This series is designed to reveal productivity tips you can use to optimize the time and energy spent on the overhead involved in video post-production. Video Post-Production Read More How to Apply In addition to job boards like Handshake and LinkedIn , there are industry-specific job boards that can aid you in your search. General Careers in Art The Art Career Project helps individuals explore diverse career paths in the art and design industry, from traditional roles like acting, photography, and fashion design to emerging fields like UI/UX design and game development. There are also resources for those looking to be involved in the business aspect of these careers. Careers in Art Read More New England Museum Jobs Since 1918, NEMA has been the museum field’s regional resource for sharing best practices, connecting colleagues, and inspiring careers. New England Museum Jobs Read More California Museum Search The California Association of Museums (CAM) Job Directory provides a variety of listings for museum and cultural institution positions across California. It's a great resource for those interested in careers in museum curation, education, visitor engagement, marketing, and museum technology, offering opportunities in both permanent and temporary roles. California Museum Search Read More UMass Arts Extension Local and Remote Internships The Arts Extension Service at UMass Amherst offers a directory of arts and culture internships in various fields such as administration, marketing, programming, and theater. It's perfect for students seeking hands-on experience in the arts and humanities, whether in local or remote opportunities. UMass Arts Extension Local and Remote Internships Read More Hire Culture (Massachusetts) Hire Culture is a job portal dedicated to creative employment opportunities across Massachusetts, featuring positions in arts, culture, and nonprofit sectors. It's an excellent resource for students and professionals seeking roles in arts administration, programming, education, and more within museums, theaters, galleries, and other cultural organizations. Hire Culture (Massachusetts) Read More Animation World Animation World Network's job portal features a variety of career opportunities in the animation, visual effects, and gaming industries. This site is ideal for students or professionals pursuing careers in animation, game design, 3D modeling, storyboarding, and other related fields in the creative media industry. Animation World Read More Word of Mouth Newsletter Words of Mouth is a weekly newsletter that highlights creative and professional opportunities in fields such as design, arts, education, and the built environment. It’s an excellent resource for students and early-career professionals seeking jobs, calls for submissions, and networking opportunities across a variety of creative industries. Word of Mouth Newsletter Read More Coroflot (Design-related Careers) Coroflot's job board specializes in design-related careers, offering a wide range of opportunities for designers in fields such as graphic design, product design, UX/UI design, and industrial design. It's an excellent resource for students or professionals aiming to build a career in the creative and design industries, offering roles at all experience levels. Coroflot (Design-related Careers) Read More AIGA Design Jobs AIGA Design Jobs is a premier job board for design professionals, offering opportunities ranging from entry-level to executive positions in various design fields, including graphic design, branding, and web design. It's a go-to resource for those pursuing careers in the creative design industry, with access to internships, freelance gigs, and full-time roles. AIGA Design Jobs Read More Fashion Fashion Jobs Top recruiting platform for professionals in fashion, luxury, and beauty Fashion Jobs Read More Business of Fashion Careers Search New Jobs from 300 Top Fashion Companies Business of Fashion Careers Read More Style Careers Fashion specific jobs and industry advice. Also hosts hiring events and fairs. Style Careers Read More Media 80LV Job opportunities for game artists. 80LV Read More Artstation Find the world’s best freelance and full-time artists for hire in games, film, media, and entertainment. ArtStation Jobs is the industry’s largest job board for media & entertainment art positions. Artstation Read More Cinesite Studios Cinesite is an award-winning digital entertainment studio with 30 years of experience and has worked on hundreds of films, TV and streaming productions. Cinesite Studios Read More Creative Heads Leading job board for careers in animation, video game, VFX development. Creative Heads Read More Creativehotlist Creativehotlist is now a dedicated career resource for creative professionals in visual communications: Individuals can post resumes, job-wanted listings, and online portfolios. Creativehotlist Read More Entertainment Careers.net Jobs in entertainment, crossing multiple industries Entertainment Careers.net Read More LA/NY 411 LA 411 and NY 411 are production directories of high-end film and television studios, production companies, professionals and more. Every listing on their sites are verified. LA/NY 411 Read More Mandy.com The world’s largest creative community of actors, film and TV crews, theatre professionals, child actors, voiceover artists, dancers, singers, musicians, models, and extras. Mandy.com Read More Motionographer Motionographer Jobs is the industry's leading job board for opportunities in Motion design, Broadcast design, 3D, Interactive design, Live action, Graphic design, Visual effects, Producing. Motionographer Read More ShowbizJobs ShowbizJobs was built to solve the frustrations of finding jobs and internships in the entertainment industry. Rather than search generic career sites with mostly non-entertainment listings or hunt through dozens of entertainment company jobsites, find them all in one place. ShowbizJobs Read More WIFVNE New England Film Jobs WIFVNE Jobs is a community job board tailored to the New England film, television, and video production industry, offering paid and volunteer opportunities. It's ideal for students or emerging professionals looking for internships, casting calls, crew gigs, and other creative roles in the film and video production sector. WIFVNE New England Film Jobs Read More Communities at UMass and Beyond In addition to joining the Connect UMass Career Community for Arts, Multimedia, and Entertainment , there are many other ways you can meet and collaborate with people in these industries. UMass Registered Student Organizations of Interest 3D Printing Club Altitude Animation Club Arts and Media Council Association for Musical Performance Cosmetics Club Design Club DIY Umass Film Production Club Students for Sustainable Fashion and Art UDesign Professional Associations American Association of Cinematographers American Cinema Editors American Society of Interior Designers Animation World Network/AWN Art21 Council of Fashion Designers of America/CFDA Independent Film and Television Alliance Production Hub Women Make Movies Contact Information Career Development & Professional Connections Whether you’re wondering where to begin, looking for an internship, or starting your job search, we will guide you through the process of your unique career development. Address: Goodell Hall | 140 Hicks Way | Amherst, MA 01003 Main Office Number: (413) 545-2224 Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Footer Students Career Journey Career Centers Resource Library Employers Handshake Contact Us UMass collegiate M - University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2025 University of Massachusetts Amherst · Site Policies · Accessibility"
    },
    "https://www.umass.edu/careers/connections/career-communities/business-financial-services-and-consulting-career-community": {
      "title": "Business, Financial Services, and Consulting Career Community",
      "description": "Business, Financial Services, and Consulting Career Community : Career Development & Professional Connections : UMass Amherst Skip to main content The University of Massachusetts Amherst Open UMass Global Links Menu Visit Apply Give Search UMass.edu Menu Career Development & Professional Connections About Us Our Staff Career Centers Across UMass Our Newton Campus Handshake Login Student Outcomes Students Undergraduates Graduates Alumni Identity-Based Resources International Students Prospective Students UWW Students Employers Post Jobs and Internships Host an Event Career Fairs at UMass Why Recruit at UMass Internship Program Best Practices Recruiting Guidelines Contact Us Faculty Sponsor an Intern Career Events for Students Request a Presentation Resource Library Career Journey Expand Menu Item Self Discovery and Career Exploration Build Career Skills: Resumes, Job-searching, and Interviewing Learn Additional Technical, Creative, and Professional Skills Your Career Support Team Gain Experience: Internships, Co-ops, Research, and More! Is Graduate School Right for Me? Year-by-Year Checklist Tool Kits Expand Menu Item Resumes Cover Letters Career Fair Preparation Interviewing LinkedIn Learning Networking What Skills Do Employers Want? Applying to Grad School Photo Booth for Headshots Professional Wardrobe Closet Connections Expand Menu Item Career Communities Expand Menu Item Arts, Multimedia, and Entertainment Business, Financial Services, and Consulting Data and Information Technology Education, Human Services, and Counseling Engineering Government and Public Service Healthcare, Life Sciences, and Nursing Infrastructure and Transportation Law and Legal Services Research Sustainability, Environment, and Agriculture Career Centers Across UMass Expand Menu Item Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Education Engineering Graduate School Office of Professional Development Humanities & Fine Arts (HFA) Information & Computer Sciences (CICS) Isenberg School of Management (ISOM) Natural Sciences (CNS) Nursing Public Health and Health Sciences (SPHHS) Social & Behavioral Sciences (SBS) University Without Walls (UWW) Connect with UMass Alumni Using LinkedIn How to Network Jobs & Internships Expand Menu Item Internships, Co-ops, and Other Field Experiences Expand Menu Item Field Experience Definitions Internships Co-ops Research Civic Engagement and Service Learning Internships and Co-Ops at Charles River Campus UMass Internship Partner Programs Scholarships for Field Experiences Jobs Searching for Jobs & Internships Can I Do an Internship? Negotiating Job Offers Interviewing Using Handshake Join the Business, Financial Services, and Consulting Career Community Learn More Business, Financial Services, and Consulting Career Community Business, financial services, and consulting are interconnected industries that involve various aspects of strategy, finance, and professional advisory services. These roles are crucial in ensuring the smooth movement of money within businesses, from managing day-to-day finances to advising on long-term financial goals. Whether helping businesses secure funding, plan budgets, or navigate complex financial markets, careers in financial services shape how companies manage and grow their money. With a combination of financial knowledge and technology, they continue to reshape how businesses approach financial decision-making and ensure sustainability in an ever-evolving market. Is This Field Right for Me? Is a Career in Finance Right for You? (Harvard Business Review) Bryan Kuderna talks about his experience in finance, the two common paths to get a foot in the door, and which path (if either) is the right career path for you. Is a Career in Finance Right for You? (Harvard Business Review) Read More Is Finance a Good Career Path (Investopedia) Jobs in the financial sector can be highly lucrative, which helps explain why they’re in such great demand. This article breaks down common careers in finance, the pros and cons of finance jobs, and the salary you can expect in this field. Is Finance a Good Career Path (Investopedia) Read More 10 Business Skills Every Professional Needs (Harvard Business School Online) An overview of why it’s important to improve your business skills and ten you should prioritize to advance your career. 10 Business Skills Every Professional Needs (Harvard Business School Online) Read More 6 Business Skills You Need and How to Improve Them (Indeed) This article provides definitions of business skills, provides a list of six examples, describes how you can improve them, and reviews how to highlight them throughout the application process. 6 Business Skills You Need and How to Improve Them (Indeed) Read More Jobs in this Field Best Sales and Marketing Jobs (U.S. News) From entry-level positions like retail salesperson to jobs that require more experience and training, such as sales manager, the U.S. News list of the Best Sales and Marketing Jobs includes a variety of careers that are ideal for someone who is a people person. Best Sales and Marketing Jobs (U.S. News) Read More 7 Best Finance Jobs to Pursue (U.S. News) This article represents the top finance jobs according to U.S. News & World Report's Best Jobs rankings. Income and unemployment data are from the U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics. 7 Best Finance Jobs to Pursue (U.S. News) Read More Certifications and LinkedIn Learning Recommendations Certifications and supplemental classes can round out your education and help you explore new areas of interest. Below are a few ways you can customize your education while at UMass. Finance Certifications (Financial Management Association) If you have trouble understanding the difference between a CFA, CFP, CIC, ChFC or any of the other financial certifications, you're not alone. While certifications aren't everything, educated investors (and potential clients) give extra credit to those who have them, recognize that candidates put in long hours of study, and that they meet the highest ethical and professional standards. Finance Certifications (Financial Management Association) Read More Top Certifications for Sales Professionals Highlights from the top certifications you can earn in the sales field. Top Certifications for Sales Professionals Read More Business, Leadership, and Social Change Movements (LinkedIn Learning) Leslie Crutchfield shares knowledge and tools to help you understand and engage with movements in ways that can achieve positive results both for your company and society at large. Drawing on her research and experience working directly with hundreds of companies and foundations, Leslie presents frameworks to stimulate your thinking, and details real world examples that demonstrate how companies navigate the complex terrain of social change movements. Business, Leadership, and Social Change Movements (LinkedIn Learning) Read More Business Development Foundations (LinkedIn Learning) Management consultant Robbie Kellman Baxter shows you what business development is, how to land a BD job, how to thrive in your BD role, and how to manage the role within an organization. Business Development Foundations (LinkedIn Learning) Read More Strategic Business Analysis Essentials (LinkedIn Learning) Business consultant and instructor Christina Charenkova unpacks the IIBA guidance and shows you how to effectively map out and implement strategic business analysis to meet the specific needs of your organization. Strategic Business Analysis Essentials (LinkedIn Learning) Read More Corporate Finance Foundations (LinkedIn Learning) Professors Jim and Kay Stice lay the foundation for how corporate finance works and make the connections between business activity and finance. They discuss the role of risk in financial decision-making, the benefits of diversification, how short- and long-term financing can impact cash flow and business operations, and the various ways businesses use equity or debt to finance corporate capital. Corporate Finance Foundations (LinkedIn Learning) Read More How to Apply In addition to job boards like Handshake and LinkedIn , there are industry-specific job boards that can aid you in your search. American Marketing Association You can search for open marketing jobs, create an account to apply and manage your application(s), as well as set marketing \"job alerts\" so that you are among the first to know when a new marketing job opens that matches your requirements. American Marketing Association Read More Ladders A compensation-focused job search engine for individuals later in their careers. Ladders Read More Financial Jobs Web A job search engine dedicated to financial professionals. Financial Jobs Web Read More Career Bank Job postings for finance, banking, and accounting. Career Bank Read More Communities at UMass and Beyond In addition to joining the Connect UMass Career Community for Business, Financial Services, and Consulting , there are many other ways you can meet and collaborate with people in these industries. UMass Registered Student Organizations of Interest Accounting Association Board of Student Businesses Center for Student Business Entrepreneurship Club Finance Committee Isenberg Marketing Club Isenberg Operations and Management Club Isenberg Real Estate Association Isenberg Sales Club Isenberg Women in Business Jewish Leaders in Business Protect Our Breasts Smart Woman Securities SACL Finance Student Alumni Association Women in Sport Management Professional Associations The American Association of Bank Directors The American Guild of Appraisers American Society of Pension Professionals & Actuaries The Association of Accredited Small Business Consultants Association for Financial Professional Business Professionals of America The Center for Association Leadership - Consulting Members Financial Planning Association Independent Educational Consultants Association Institute of Management Consultants Security Traders Association Contact Information Career Development & Professional Connections Whether you’re wondering where to begin, looking for an internship, or starting your job search, we will guide you through the process of your unique career development. Address: Goodell Hall | 140 Hicks Way | Amherst, MA 01003 Main Office Number: (413) 545-2224 Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Footer Students Career Journey Career Centers Resource Library Employers Handshake Contact Us UMass collegiate M - University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2025 University of Massachusetts Amherst · Site Policies · Accessibility"
    },
    "https://www.umass.edu/careers/connections/career-communities/data-and-information-technology-career-community": {
      "title": "Data and Information Technology Career Community",
      "description": "Data and Information Technology Career Community : Career Development & Professional Connections : UMass Amherst Skip to main content The University of Massachusetts Amherst Open UMass Global Links Menu Visit Apply Give Search UMass.edu Menu Career Development & Professional Connections About Us Our Staff Career Centers Across UMass Our Newton Campus Handshake Login Student Outcomes Students Undergraduates Graduates Alumni Identity-Based Resources International Students Prospective Students UWW Students Employers Post Jobs and Internships Host an Event Career Fairs at UMass Why Recruit at UMass Internship Program Best Practices Recruiting Guidelines Contact Us Faculty Sponsor an Intern Career Events for Students Request a Presentation Resource Library Career Journey Expand Menu Item Self Discovery and Career Exploration Build Career Skills: Resumes, Job-searching, and Interviewing Learn Additional Technical, Creative, and Professional Skills Your Career Support Team Gain Experience: Internships, Co-ops, Research, and More! Is Graduate School Right for Me? Year-by-Year Checklist Tool Kits Expand Menu Item Resumes Cover Letters Career Fair Preparation Interviewing LinkedIn Learning Networking What Skills Do Employers Want? Applying to Grad School Photo Booth for Headshots Professional Wardrobe Closet Connections Expand Menu Item Career Communities Expand Menu Item Arts, Multimedia, and Entertainment Business, Financial Services, and Consulting Data and Information Technology Education, Human Services, and Counseling Engineering Government and Public Service Healthcare, Life Sciences, and Nursing Infrastructure and Transportation Law and Legal Services Research Sustainability, Environment, and Agriculture Career Centers Across UMass Expand Menu Item Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Education Engineering Graduate School Office of Professional Development Humanities & Fine Arts (HFA) Information & Computer Sciences (CICS) Isenberg School of Management (ISOM) Natural Sciences (CNS) Nursing Public Health and Health Sciences (SPHHS) Social & Behavioral Sciences (SBS) University Without Walls (UWW) Connect with UMass Alumni Using LinkedIn How to Network Jobs & Internships Expand Menu Item Internships, Co-ops, and Other Field Experiences Expand Menu Item Field Experience Definitions Internships Co-ops Research Civic Engagement and Service Learning Internships and Co-Ops at Charles River Campus UMass Internship Partner Programs Scholarships for Field Experiences Jobs Searching for Jobs & Internships Can I Do an Internship? Negotiating Job Offers Interviewing Using Handshake Join the Data and Information Technology Career Community Learn More Data and Information Technology Career Community Data and Information Technologies are fields focused on the collection, management, and interpretation of vast amounts of data to inform strategic decision-making. As technology advances, our ability to store and process vast amounts of data grows, posing the challenge of turning this wealth of information into actionable insights. Data science is crucial for extracting patterns and trends from large datasets, helping organizations improve operations, innovate, and enhance customer experiences. With a blend of technical expertise and analytical skills, professionals in these fields shape how businesses use data to meet challenges and achieve their goals. Is This Field Right for Me? Am I a Good Fit for a Career as a Data Analyst? Interested in what it takes to be a Data Analyst? Learn about the ins and outs of being a Data Analyst, and the skills needed to thrive in the field through this article. Am I a Good Fit for a Career as a Data Analyst? Read More Cybersecurity Quiz Ever wonder if a career in cybersecurity was right for you? This quiz focuses on 6 key aspects of cybersecurity to figure out if you’re a good fit. Cybersecurity Quiz Read More How to Know if Software Engineering is Right For You This article goes into depth about some key traits that are crucial in this career path. This is a wonderful way to learn about skills you should be strengthening or developing as you continue to delve deeper into the field. How to Know if Software Engineering is Right For You Read More Jobs In This Field 2023 Technology Industry Outlook Economic headwinds seem to be gathering, but there are many strategies that may spur innovation and growth in the technology industry in 2023 and beyond. 2023 Technology Industry Outlook Read More Top 10 Jobs For Computer Science Majors If you find yourself analyzing the latest and greatest tech releases, dreaming up your own tech creations, or even coming up with solutions to make current products better, then you might want to consider a career in the computer science field. Top 10 Jobs For Computer Science Majors Read More 6 Tips for Landing a Software Engineering Job without a STEM Degree According to recent Handshake data, 35% of more than 28,000 women applying to Software Engineering & Development roles have a non-STEM background - here are tips to close the gap on applying for these jobs without a STEM degree. 6 Tips for Landing a Software Engineering Job without a STEM Degree Read More 11 High-Paying Data Analytics Jobs Data analysts examine large datasets to find areas of waste or inefficiency and can find positions in multiple industries for a higher salary than many other occupations. As data analysts work for many types of businesses, you may find a financially rewarding data analyst job that matches your set of skills. 11 High-Paying Data Analytics Jobs Read More Certifications and LinkedIn Learning Recommendations Certifications and supplemental classes can round out your education and help you explore new areas of interest. Below are a few ways you can customize your education while at UMass. Best Certifications For Computer Networking The featured certifications represent all major tiers of networking job roles, from the entry level (Network+) to the expert level (CCIE). Best Certifications For Computer Networking Read More Cybersecurity Careers and Certification Learn about the nine most common cybersecurity jobs and the duties and qualifications for each role. Learn which cybersecurity certifications appear in job listings and which ones will help you get the job you want. Cybersecurity Careers and Certification Read More Data Analyst Certification The Power BI Data Analyst Associate certification verifies your capabilities as a data analyst professional to leverage the Microsoft Power BI data tool. Data Analyst Certification Read More Data Analytics Foundations In this course, instructor Robin Hunt brings you into the mind of an analyst. She defines and explains foundational concepts, such as how to think about data, how to work with others in different roles to get the data you need, and the tools you need to work with data, such as Excel and Microsoft Access. She introduces you to SQL queries, PowerBI, and more. Data Analytics Foundations Read More Defining Your Data Career Path Kate begins by explaining the benefits of pursuing a career in data, then dives into the specifics of what you would do in different roles, what skills and education are required for each, getting your first job on a career path, and progressing in that career. She also includes an interview with someone working in each of the roles she covers. Kate focuses on the roles of data analyst, data scientist, data engineer, data consultant, data steward, and chief data officer Defining Your Data Career Path Read More How to Apply In addition to job boards like Handshake and LinkedIn , there are industry-specific job boards that can aid you in your search. Dice Dice is the leading career marketplace for technologists, with 5.9M Dice Members in the United States. The platform helps technology professionals manage their careers and employers connect with highly skilled tech talent. Dice provides insights, data and career opportunities for technology professionals while putting state-of-the-art tools in the hands of recruiters and employers seeking tech talent. Dice Read More Hired With unbiased insights, DEI tools, tech skill assessments, sourcing services, and dedicated Customer Success Managers, Hired works with companies around the world, placing more than 20,000 active and qualified candidates in new roles. Backed by The Adecco Group, Hired is rated by G2 as a leader in Recruiting Automation, Job Search Sites, and Diversity Recruiting. Hired Read More Ladders A job search website that focuses on high-paying jobs. Ladders Read More Communities at UMass and Beyond In addition to joining the Connect UMass Career Community for Data and Information Technology , there are many other ways you can meet and collaborate with people in these industries. UMass Student Organizations BUILD UMass Black, Indigenous, and LatinX in Tech CICS PRIDE Cybersecurity Club Isenberg Operations & Information Management Club McCormick Strategy & Analytics Club oStem Society of Asian Scientists and Engineers Society of Women Engineers SOM Student Chapter of INFORMS UMass Robotics Women in Informatics and Computer Science Professional Associations Association of the Advancement of Artificial Intelligence Association for Computing Machinery Association of Information Technology Professionals Association for Information Systems Computing Research Association Digital Analytics Association Institute for Electrical and Electronics Engineers (IEEE) Computer Society International Webmasters Association Internet Society Software and Information Industry Association Contact Information Career Development & Professional Connections Whether you’re wondering where to begin, looking for an internship, or starting your job search, we will guide you through the process of your unique career development. Address: Goodell Hall | 140 Hicks Way | Amherst, MA 01003 Main Office Number: (413) 545-2224 Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Footer Students Career Journey Career Centers Resource Library Employers Handshake Contact Us UMass collegiate M - University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2025 University of Massachusetts Amherst · Site Policies · Accessibility"
