    "https://www.umass.edu/careers/people/education-human-services-and-counseling-career-community": {
      "title": "Education, Human Services, and Counseling Career Community",
      "description": "Education, Human Services, and Counseling Career Community : Career Development & Professional Connections : UMass Amherst Skip to main content The University of Massachusetts Amherst Open UMass Global Links Menu Visit Apply Give Search UMass.edu Menu Career Development & Professional Connections About Us Our Staff Career Centers Across UMass Our Newton Campus Handshake Login Student Outcomes Students Undergraduates Graduates Alumni Identity-Based Resources International Students Prospective Students UWW Students Employers Post Jobs and Internships Host an Event Career Fairs at UMass Why Recruit at UMass Internship Program Best Practices Recruiting Guidelines Contact Us Faculty Sponsor an Intern Career Events for Students Request a Presentation Resource Library Career Journey Expand Menu Item Self Discovery and Career Exploration Build Career Skills: Resumes, Job-searching, and Interviewing Learn Additional Technical, Creative, and Professional Skills Your Career Support Team Gain Experience: Internships, Co-ops, Research, and More! Is Graduate School Right for Me? Year-by-Year Checklist Tool Kits Expand Menu Item Resumes Cover Letters Career Fair Preparation Interviewing LinkedIn Learning Networking What Skills Do Employers Want? Applying to Grad School Photo Booth for Headshots Professional Wardrobe Closet Connections Expand Menu Item Career Communities Expand Menu Item Arts, Multimedia, and Entertainment Business, Financial Services, and Consulting Data and Information Technology Education, Human Services, and Counseling Engineering Government and Public Service Healthcare, Life Sciences, and Nursing Infrastructure and Transportation Law and Legal Services Research Sustainability, Environment, and Agriculture Career Centers Across UMass Expand Menu Item Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Education Engineering Graduate School Office of Professional Development Humanities & Fine Arts (HFA) Information & Computer Sciences (CICS) Isenberg School of Management (ISOM) Natural Sciences (CNS) Nursing Public Health and Health Sciences (SPHHS) Social & Behavioral Sciences (SBS) University Without Walls (UWW) Connect with UMass Alumni Using LinkedIn How to Network Jobs & Internships Expand Menu Item Internships, Co-ops, and Other Field Experiences Expand Menu Item Field Experience Definitions Internships Co-ops Research Civic Engagement and Service Learning Internships and Co-Ops at Charles River Campus UMass Internship Partner Programs Scholarships for Field Experiences Jobs Searching for Jobs & Internships Can I Do an Internship? Negotiating Job Offers Interviewing Using Handshake Join the Education, Human Services, and Counseling Career Community Learn More Education, Human Services, and Counseling Career Community Education, Human Services and Counseling careers are tied by their desire to help educate, develop, and support individuals and groups throughout different developmental stages in life. These roles support individuals and groups at various stages of life, helping them grow, develop, and overcome challenges. Whether working with children, families, or communities, their work fosters personal growth, well-being, and resilience. With a heart of empathy and an abundant amount of patience, these careers make a lasting impact, helping individuals navigate challenges and reach their full potential. Is This Field Right for Me? How I Turned My Love for Education into a Career Outside the Classroom When you are passionate about teaching and education, it is easy to think that your career options are limited to a classroom. But it turns out, there are plenty of education-related opportunities—and in places you might not expect, like leadership development, technology, and language. How I Turned My Love for Education into a Career Outside the Classroom Read More Jobs in this Field 25 Jobs in the Education Field From teachers who work inside classrooms to administrators who oversee an institution’s operations to coaches who provide instruction on the field or stadium floor, there are many types of jobs in education—and learning more about each can help you decide which path is right for you, your interests and career goals. 25 Jobs in the Education Field Read More Certifications and LinkedIn Learning Recommendations 20 Teacher Certifications Teacher certifications allow job seekers to demonstrate their competency as a teacher to employers. However, not all teacher certifications provide the same value for job seekers. 20 Teacher Certifications Read More Active Listening: The Secret to Effective Communication Learn how to discern between surface and empathetic listening and how to communicate more productively using listening loops. Plus, find out how to navigate the three levels of listening: what is said, what is meant, and what is felt. Active Listening: The Secret to Effective Communication Read More Allyship and Advocacy Across Differences Learning Path Organizations that prioritize diversity stand out from the rest. How can you foster diversity while overcoming the challenges that come with it? Learn about the challenges that can arise in diverse working environments and how to support and accommodate the needs of underrepresented groups (URGs). Allyship and Advocacy Across Differences Learning Path Read More Photoshop for Teaching and Learning Whether you are a teacher working on a presentation or a student tackling an assignment, you will need to use images to explain concepts. And while students, educators, and instructional designers do not necessarily need to be Photoshop power users, understanding how to work with the core tools in the powerful image-editing software can both empower individuals and help them produce more compelling images. Photoshop for Teaching and Learning Read More Teaching with Technology Put the \"tech\" into your teaching. Learn how to use technology to enhance course design, lesson planning, presentations, in-class activities, assessments, and student achievement and engagement. Teaching with Technology Read More Visual Teaching Strategies Visual Thinking Strategies (VTS) challenges the standard model of teaching by encouraging a reflection-and-response style of learning. Designed by art educator Philip Yenawine and developmental psychologist Abigail Housen, VTS relies on children's natural ability to observe, using imagery as the starting point for learning. The teacher asks open-ended questions; students reflect and respond. The process has been proven to strengthen critical thinking skills, language development, confidence, and collaboration. Watch VTS at work in three Louisiana schools and find out what alternative teaching methods like these might have in store for America's classrooms. Visual Teaching Strategies Read More Imagine a new career as a teacher Interested in pursuing a career in education? Becoming a teacher may be a whole lot easier than you think, especially now, when there is such a high demand for teachers and so many workers are looking for more meaningful and intentional professional opportunities. Imagine a new career as a teacher Read More How to Apply Job Boards Idealist Our job listings include opportunities spanning a variety of nonprofits, social-impact businesses, and corporate social responsibility (CSR) initiatives. Idealist Read More School Spring Whether you are just starting out or experienced, this is the best place to manage your education career.Access thousands of job openings nationwide. School Spring Read More Higher Ed Jobs HigherEdJobs is the leading source for jobs and career information in academia. More colleges and universities trust HigherEdJobs to recruit faculty and administrators than any other source. Higher Ed Jobs Read More Social Worker Career Center Social workers can use these resources to search national job listings and find professional development resources to help you at every stage of your career. Social Worker Career Center Read More The Chronicle of Philanthropy The Chronicle of Philanthropy's job board features a variety of career opportunities in the nonprofit and philanthropy sectors, including fundraising, grantmaking, and nonprofit management. It's perfect for those passionate about social impact and looking to build a career in charitable organizations, foundations, or community development. The Chronicle of Philanthropy Read More Devex (Jobs in International Development) Devex is a global platform for career opportunities in international development, featuring jobs in sectors like health, education, humanitarian aid, and sustainability. It's ideal for students and professionals looking to make a positive impact through roles with international organizations, NGOs, and development-focused companies. Devex (Jobs in International Development) Read More Foundation List Foundation List offers a variety of job opportunities in the nonprofit sector, with listings ranging from entry-level to executive positions in philanthropy, fundraising, and nonprofit management. It's a great resource for those looking to pursue careers in social good and community-driven organizations. Foundation List Read More Work for Good Work for Good is a job board focused on nonprofit careers, offering positions in areas like fundraising, social services, advocacy, and community outreach. It's a great platform for students and professionals eager to build a career dedicated to social impact, offering both entry-level and senior positions in organizations making a difference. Work for Good Read More Carney Sandoe & Associates Carney Sandoe & Associates specializes in faculty placement for private and independent schools worldwide, offering roles for educators, administrators, and leadership positions in K-12 education. This site is ideal for those seeking careers in teaching, school administration, or education leadership in the independent school sector. Carney Sandoe & Associates Read More National Center for Teacher Residencies (NCTR) The National Center for Teacher Residencies (NCTR) connects a network of teacher residency programs across the U.S., offering a rigorous apprenticeship and master's-level education to prepare teachers for district schools. This platform is ideal for those interested in becoming highly trained educators through hands-on classroom experience and advanced coursework, particularly in public school settings. National Center for Teacher Residencies (NCTR) Read More Communities at UMass and Beyond In addition to joining the Connect UMass Career Community for Education, Human Services and Counseling , there are many other ways you can meet and collaborate with people in these industries. UMass Registered Student Organizations of Interest Education Club Teacher Education and Curriculum Studies Graduate Social Justice Education Alliance for Afro-American Cultural Education School Counseling Association Center for Education Policy and Advocacy Active Minds Critical Education Research Collaboration Disability Culture Club Psi Chi BOLTWOOD project Stonewall Center Student Bridges Professional Associations Council for Exceptional Children National Education Association Society for Public Health Education American Federation of Teachers Association of Teacher Educators International Association of Teachers of English as a Foreign Language Association for Career and Technical Education National Art Education Association Music Teachers National Association Society of Health and Physical Educators National Dance Teachers Association of America American Association of School Administrators National Association of School Psychologists American College Personnel Association NASPA: Student Affairs Administrators in Higher Education International Coaching Federation American Association for Adult and Continuing Education National Association of Social Workers School Social Work Association of America National Council of Nonprofits National Organization for Human Services National Association of Community Health Centers American Psychological Association American Counseling Association Association for Lesbian, Gay, Bisexual, and Transgender Issues in Counseling Association for Multicultural Counseling and Development Expressive Arts Therapy Association American Association for Marriage and Family Therapy Contact Information Career Development & Professional Connections Whether you’re wondering where to begin, looking for an internship, or starting your job search, we will guide you through the process of your unique career development. Address: Goodell Hall | 140 Hicks Way | Amherst, MA 01003 Main Office Number: (413) 545-2224 Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Footer Students Career Journey Career Centers Resource Library Employers Handshake Contact Us UMass collegiate M - University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2025 University of Massachusetts Amherst · Site Policies · Accessibility"
