    "https://www.umass.edu/careers/people/research-career-community": {
      "title": "Research Career Community",
      "description": "Research Career Community : Career Development & Professional Connections : UMass Amherst Skip to main content The University of Massachusetts Amherst Open UMass Global Links Menu Visit Apply Give Search UMass.edu Menu Career Development & Professional Connections About Us Our Staff Career Centers Across UMass Our Newton Campus Handshake Login Student Outcomes Students Undergraduates Graduates Alumni Identity-Based Resources International Students Prospective Students UWW Students Employers Post Jobs and Internships Host an Event Career Fairs at UMass Why Recruit at UMass Internship Program Best Practices Recruiting Guidelines Contact Us Faculty Sponsor an Intern Career Events for Students Request a Presentation Resource Library Career Journey Expand Menu Item Self Discovery and Career Exploration Build Career Skills: Resumes, Job-searching, and Interviewing Learn Additional Technical, Creative, and Professional Skills Your Career Support Team Gain Experience: Internships, Co-ops, Research, and More! Is Graduate School Right for Me? Year-by-Year Checklist Tool Kits Expand Menu Item Resumes Cover Letters Career Fair Preparation Interviewing LinkedIn Learning Networking What Skills Do Employers Want? Applying to Grad School Photo Booth for Headshots Professional Wardrobe Closet Connections Expand Menu Item Career Communities Expand Menu Item Arts, Multimedia, and Entertainment Business, Financial Services, and Consulting Data and Information Technology Education, Human Services, and Counseling Engineering Government and Public Service Healthcare, Life Sciences, and Nursing Infrastructure and Transportation Law and Legal Services Research Sustainability, Environment, and Agriculture Career Centers Across UMass Expand Menu Item Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Education Engineering Graduate School Office of Professional Development Humanities & Fine Arts (HFA) Information & Computer Sciences (CICS) Isenberg School of Management (ISOM) Natural Sciences (CNS) Nursing Public Health and Health Sciences (SPHHS) Social & Behavioral Sciences (SBS) University Without Walls (UWW) Connect with UMass Alumni Using LinkedIn How to Network Jobs & Internships Expand Menu Item Internships, Co-ops, and Other Field Experiences Expand Menu Item Field Experience Definitions Internships Co-ops Research Civic Engagement and Service Learning Internships and Co-Ops at Charles River Campus UMass Internship Partner Programs Scholarships for Field Experiences Jobs Searching for Jobs & Internships Can I Do an Internship? Negotiating Job Offers Interviewing Using Handshake Join the Research Career Community Learn More Research Career Community Research careers drive discovery and innovation, focusing on exploring new ideas, solving complex problems, and developing groundbreaking solutions. These roles contribute to a greater understanding of the world around us, focusing on discovery and moving knowledge forwards. Whether conducting experiments, analyzing data, or testing hypotheses, professionals in research play a critical role in pushing the boundaries of knowledge and shaping the future of their industries. With a blend of analytical expertise and creative problem-solving, they work to uncover insights that drive progress and change. Is This Field Right For Me? Pros and Cons of a Career in Research Whether a career in research is for you or not will depend entirely on your own levels of determination and persistence, along with weighing the pros against the cons of research. In the end, only you can make the choice, but keep in mind the advantages and disadvantages of going down this career path. Pros and Cons of a Career in Research Read More Jobs In This Field Highest Paying Research Jobs Research is a vital aspect of many careers. History, anthropology, archeology, and sociology are just a few subjects that rely on the study of information. Other career paths with a heavy focus on data collection and analysis include forensic science technician, research analyst, medical scientist, agricultural and food science technician, computer and information research scientist, market researcher, archivist, and research associate Highest Paying Research Jobs Read More 15 Research Careers You Can Pursue If you like testing hypotheses, analyzing data, and drawing conclusions, you might be interested in a career in research. Research professionals can find work in many fields, including medical science, technology, and business. Knowing what research careers exist, what they do and how much they earn can help you determine if this is the right career path for you. In this article, we explore what researcher careers are, which researcher careers exist and how to pursue researcher careers to help you find a role that meets your professional goals. 15 Research Careers You Can Pursue Read More Certifications and LinkedIn Learning Recommendations Academic Research Foundations In this course, educator Rolin Moe explores the foundations of this methodology to help you confidently tackle your own quantitative research study. Rolin covers the characteristics of quantitative research and explains how to approach distinct parts of the research process, such as creating a solid research question and developing a literature review. He goes over the elements of a study, explains how to collect and analyze data, and shows how to present your data in written and numeric form. Academic Research Foundations Read More Learning Design Research With design research, designs are more meaningful and effective because they are grounded in a real-world context. The goal of this course is to introduce the process of design research and to help designers understand how critical it is to being able to develop great designs. Learning Design Research Read More Market Research Foundations Learn how to clarify your research goals, how to sell your company on research, how to find the best participants, and how to present your data in succinct, meaningful formats like customer personas and journey maps. Market Research Foundations Read More How to Apply ResearchGate.net In addition to posting many international research positions, ResearchGate has access to publications in related fields. ResearchGate.net Read More AIR AIR exists to empower those individuals at all levels to use data, analytics, information, and evidence to make decisions that are effective, ethical, and equitable and take actions that benefit all students and institutions and improve higher education AIR Read More Science Careers Science Careers is dedicated to being the world leader in matching qualified scientists with jobs in industry, academia, and government. We are committed to providing the best career resources for scientists as well as effective recruiting solutions for employers. Science Careers Read More Women in Research We work to advance the contributions and voice of women in research, both for themselves and for the greater good of the industry. Women in Research Read More Communities at UMass and Beyond In addition to joining the Connect UMass Career Community for Research , there are many other ways you can meet and collaborate with people in these industries. UMass Registered Student Organizations of Interest American Chemical Society Association of Women in Science Biochemistry Club BioSci Club Black Women in Medicine Inc. S.E.A.D. - Students to End Alzheimer's Disease American Chemical Society American Medical Student Association (AMSA) UMass Red Cross Association of Women in Science Black Women in Medicine Inc. S.E.A.D. - Students to End Alzheimer's Disease OM Chapter of Institute for Operations, Research and Management Sciences Professional Associations Association for Clinical Research Professionals National Organization for Research Professionals Association for Institutional Research Society of Clinical Research Associates National Council University Research Administrators Contact Information Career Development & Professional Connections Whether you’re wondering where to begin, looking for an internship, or starting your job search, we will guide you through the process of your unique career development. Address: Goodell Hall | 140 Hicks Way | Amherst, MA 01003 Main Office Number: (413) 545-2224 Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Footer Students Career Journey Career Centers Resource Library Employers Handshake Contact Us UMass collegiate M - University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2025 University of Massachusetts Amherst · Site Policies · Accessibility"
    },
    "https://www.umass.edu/careers/people/sustainability-environment-and-agriculture-career-community": {
      "title": "Sustainability, Environment, and Agriculture Career Community",
      "description": "Sustainability, Environment, and Agriculture Career Community : Career Development & Professional Connections : UMass Amherst Skip to main content The University of Massachusetts Amherst Open UMass Global Links Menu Visit Apply Give Search UMass.edu Menu Career Development & Professional Connections About Us Our Staff Career Centers Across UMass Our Newton Campus Handshake Login Student Outcomes Students Undergraduates Graduates Alumni Identity-Based Resources International Students Prospective Students UWW Students Employers Post Jobs and Internships Host an Event Career Fairs at UMass Why Recruit at UMass Internship Program Best Practices Recruiting Guidelines Contact Us Faculty Sponsor an Intern Career Events for Students Request a Presentation Resource Library Career Journey Expand Menu Item Self Discovery and Career Exploration Build Career Skills: Resumes, Job-searching, and Interviewing Learn Additional Technical, Creative, and Professional Skills Your Career Support Team Gain Experience: Internships, Co-ops, Research, and More! Is Graduate School Right for Me? Year-by-Year Checklist Tool Kits Expand Menu Item Resumes Cover Letters Career Fair Preparation Interviewing LinkedIn Learning Networking What Skills Do Employers Want? Applying to Grad School Photo Booth for Headshots Professional Wardrobe Closet Connections Expand Menu Item Career Communities Expand Menu Item Arts, Multimedia, and Entertainment Business, Financial Services, and Consulting Data and Information Technology Education, Human Services, and Counseling Engineering Government and Public Service Healthcare, Life Sciences, and Nursing Infrastructure and Transportation Law and Legal Services Research Sustainability, Environment, and Agriculture Career Centers Across UMass Expand Menu Item Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Education Engineering Graduate School Office of Professional Development Humanities & Fine Arts (HFA) Information & Computer Sciences (CICS) Isenberg School of Management (ISOM) Natural Sciences (CNS) Nursing Public Health and Health Sciences (SPHHS) Social & Behavioral Sciences (SBS) University Without Walls (UWW) Connect with UMass Alumni Using LinkedIn How to Network Jobs & Internships Expand Menu Item Internships, Co-ops, and Other Field Experiences Expand Menu Item Field Experience Definitions Internships Co-ops Research Civic Engagement and Service Learning Internships and Co-Ops at Charles River Campus UMass Internship Partner Programs Scholarships for Field Experiences Jobs Searching for Jobs & Internships Can I Do an Internship? Negotiating Job Offers Interviewing Using Handshake Join the Energy, Environment, and Agriculture Career Community Learn More Sustainability, Environment, and Agriculture Career Community Careers in Energy, the Environment and Agriculture fields include a wide range of tasks such as energy production or transmission, environmental policy and management, land use, sustainability, and other related professions. Jobs in the energy, environment and agricultural fields are characterized by the massive impact they have on society. Whether heating our homes, providing clean drinking water, or supplying us with the food we eat, careers in these sectors affect our daily life and well-being. Jobs in the energy sector work on energy infrastructure. Energy infrastructure is any system we use to get energy, including gas, water, sewer pipelines, electric and power lines, and power plants. Those working in the energy sector will work on these systems’ construction, operation, use, or maintenance. Is This Field Right for Me? Historically, energy has been one of the U.S.’s fastest-growing industries. While growth in this career path slowed at the start of the COVID-19 pandemic, the energy sector has picked up again and grew 4% in 2021 ( USEER 2022 National Report ), higher than the overall U.S. employment growth of 2.8%. Is a Green Career Right for Me? (Green New Careers) Learn more about \"Green Careers, and take a quick to learn if a green career is right for you. Is a Green Career Right for Me? (Green New Careers) Read More 10 Compelling Reasons Why an Environmental Career is Right for You (NREP) An article discussing 10 reasons why an environmental career could be a good fit for you. Want to save the world? Want to do something meaningful? Want to get a little sun while working in the great outdoors? Then studying the environmental sciences and becoming an ecological professional might be a perfect fit. 10 Compelling Reasons Why an Environmental Career is Right for You (NREP) Read More Which Green Building Career is Right for You? Looking to find out more about green building careers and see which one is right for you? Take our exploratory quiz to learn about green building and some of the occupations that support this industry. Which Green Building Career is Right for You? Read More Skills Need for Green Jobs of the Future (World Economic Forum) The United Nations Environment Programme has created GEO-6 for Youth - a digital guide on sustainable career choices and the skills required to thrive in green industries. Skills Need for Green Jobs of the Future (World Economic Forum) Read More What are Green Skills (United Nations Industrial Development Organization) Green skills are the knowledge, abilities, values and attitudes needed to live in, develop and support a sustainable and resource-efficient society. The need to transition towards more environmentally sustainable modes of production and consumption has become imperative, for developed as well as for developing countries. This article discusses the Green General Skill Index, which identifies four groups of work tasks that are especially important for green occupations. What are Green Skills (United Nations Industrial Development Organization) Read More Jobs In This Field Types of Jobs: Energy : Energy Consultant, Energy Operations for specific energy types such as Wind, Solar, Fuel Cell, etc., Power Distribution/Transmission, Energy Auditing Environment : National or state agency regulator or analyst, engineer/scientist, land management, compliance officer, remediation specialist Agriculture : Agricultural operations, animal systems, food processing systems, foresters, national or state agency analysts, plant/soil scientist 14 Renewable Energy Careers As more people become environmentally conscious, the renewable energy industry continues to increase in popularity. By exploring the various kinds of roles available in this industry, you can find one that aligns with your interests and values. 14 Renewable Energy Careers Read More What is an Environmental Scientist? Environmental scientists and specialists use their knowledge of the natural sciences to protect the environment and human health. They may clean up polluted areas, advise policymakers, or work with industry to reduce waste. What is an Environmental Scientist? Read More Certifications and LinkedIn Learning Recommendations In addition to your classes, certifications can often round out your education or enable you to become more specialized in a field of interest. Environmental Certifications (NREP) A comprehensive list of environmental certifications as collected by the National Registry of Environmental Professionals (NREP), including project management/coordination, auditing/assessment, and science/technology programs. Environmental Certifications (NREP) Read More Cert Prep: LEED Green Associate Earning the LEED Green Associate credential can help you advance your career by demonstrating your expertise in sustainable design, construction, and building operations. Instructor Fulya Kocak Gin gives an overview of what to expect on the LEED Green Associate exam and provides background on the key topics and concepts you need to know. Cert Prep: LEED Green Associate Read More Sustainable Business Strategies (LinkedIn Learning) David Bennell outlines how to establish your reputation as a company focused on sustainability, manage supply chains more responsibly and effectively, create sustainable products and services, and reduce energy use, waste, toxic substances, and emissions. Sustainable Business Strategies (LinkedIn Learning) Read More Green Jobs are Here to Stay (LinkedIn Learning) Instructor Fulya Kocak Gin walks you through the emerging green jobs market, with tips on customizing a strategy to effectively land a greener role, regardless of where you are in your career. Discover the new world of work and what you can do now to become a part of it. Green Jobs are Here to Stay (LinkedIn Learning) Read More Construction Technology: Establishing Return on Investment (ROI) William Carney helps you get a better understanding of technology in the construction business, equipping you with skills to evaluate your own job site so you can establish a return on investment (ROI) for your tools. Explore the basics of ROI, what it is, why it matters, and how to calculate it accurately. Construction Technology: Establishing Return on Investment (ROI) Read More In addition to your classes, certifications and online coursework can often round out your education or enable you to become more specialized in a field of interest. AAE Certifications The industry of energy and the environment offer many certifications to show mastery of various aspects in the field. AAE Certifications Read More Construction Technologies ROI (Return on Investment) and Energy Explore the basics of ROI, what it is, why it matters, and how to calculate it accurately. Find out how designers, contractors, and building owners can leverage a long-term return by choosing the right kinds of tech. Learn about the ROI for tools enabling visualization, reality capture, digital review, energy analysis, automation, and more. Construction Technologies ROI (Return on Investment) and Energy Read More LEED Exam Certification Preparation Are you passionate—and knowledgeable—about the latest green building principles and practices? If so, earning the LEED Green Associate credential can help you advance your career by demonstrating your expertise in sustainable design, construction, and building operations. LEED Exam Certification Preparation Read More Green jobs for sustainable careers Discover the new world of work and what you can do now to become a part of it. Explore the rising demand for green jobs, sustainable careers, and green skills, as Fulya shows you how to get started and land a role that works for you. Whether you are a student or entry-level candidate, or a career changer or advanced professional, there is a green job out there waiting for you. Green jobs for sustainable careers Read More How AI is Transforming Agriculture (LinkedIn Learning) Anil Gupta shows you how AI is deployed within six different industry sectors and explains the value it creates for users and companies. He begins with agriculture and the example of Aquabyte helping fish farmers monitor the health of the fish and get real-time guidance on how to care for and manage the fish. How AI is Transforming Agriculture (LinkedIn Learning) Read More How to Apply In addition to job boards like Handshake and LinkedIn , there are industry-specific job boards that can aid you in your search. Corporate Jobs Green Jobs Green Jobs Network is the #1 community for climate and social impact jobseekers. Green Jobs Read More Zippia Zippia provides industry-based job search tools to help narrow your search down more effectively. Zippia Read More Non-Profit Companies and NGOs Green Building Careers From USGBC: \"Our vision is that buildings and communities will regenerate and sustain the health and vitality of all life within a generation. Our mission is to transform how buildings and communities are designed, built and operated, enabling an environmentally and socially responsible, healthy, and prosperous environment that improves the quality of life. We're committed to transforming our built environment through LEED , the world’s most preeminent green building system. Today there are more than 105,000 LEED-certified buildings in nearly 190 countries.\" Green Building Careers Read More Idealist A top source for social-impact jobs, internships, and volunteer opportunities. Idealist Read More World Wildlife Fund As the world’s leading conservation organization, WWF works in nearly 100 countries. At every level, we collaborate with people around the world to develop and deliver innovative solutions that protect communities, wildlife, and the places in which they live. World Wildlife Fund Read More Government National Registry of Environmental Professionals The National Registry of Environmental Professionals® (NREPSM), is a resource of high-quality environmental safety professional certifications to provide assurance of professional excellence globally. National Registry of Environmental Professionals Read More U.S. Department of Agriculture From the USDA: \"We provide leadership on food, agriculture, natural resources, rural development, nutrition, and related issues based on public policy, the best available science, and effective management. We have a vision to provide economic opportunity through innovation, helping rural America to thrive; to promote agriculture production that better nourishes Americans while also helping feed others throughout the world; and to preserve our Nation's natural resources through conservation, restored forests, improved watersheds, and healthy private working lands.\" U.S. Department of Agriculture Read More U.S. Department of Energy Jobs The Department of Ene rgy (DOE) is the Nation’s solutions agency, engaged in a wide range of challenging and innovative work, including tackling the climate crisis, ensuring national security, and advancing basic research. Our employees positively impact the world in unimaginable ways. U.S. Department of Energy Jobs Read More U.S. Environmental Protection Agency The mission of EPA is to protect human health and the environment. EPA works to ensure that: Americans have clean air, land and water; National efforts to reduce environmental risks are based on the best available scientific information; Federal laws protecting human health and the environment are administered and enforced fairly, effectively and as Congress intended; Environmental stewardship is integral to U.S. policies concerning natural resources, human health, economic growth, energy, transportation, agriculture, industry, and international trade, and these factors are similarly considered in establishing environmental policy; All parts of society--communities, individuals, businesses, and state, local and tribal governments--have access to accurate information sufficient to effectively participate in managing human health and environmental risks; Contaminated lands and toxic sites are cleaned up by potentially responsible parties and revitalized; and Chemicals in the marketplace are reviewed for safety. U.S. Environmental Protection Agency Read More Communities at UMass and Beyond In addition to joining the Connect UMass Career Community for Energy, Environment, and Agriculture , there are many other ways you can meet and collaborate with people in these industries. UMass Registered Student Organizations of Interest Environmental Conservation MASSPIRG Outing Club (UMOC) Society of American Foresters Sustainable UMass Action Coalition Sustainability Projects Abroad Wind Energy Center Professional Associations American Institute of Architecture Students Association for Energy Service Professionals Association of Energy Engineers Association of Women in Science Environmental Business Council Gardenshare International Association for Energy Economics Massachusetts Clean Energy Center National Association of State Departments of Agriculture North American Association for Environmental Education Contact Information Career Development & Professional Connections Whether you’re wondering where to begin, looking for an internship, or starting your job search, we will guide you through the process of your unique career development. Address: Goodell Hall | 140 Hicks Way | Amherst, MA 01003 Main Office Number: (413) 545-2224 Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Footer Students Career Journey Career Centers Resource Library Employers Handshake Contact Us UMass collegiate M - University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2025 University of Massachusetts Amherst · Site Policies · Accessibility"
