      "title": "Welcome to BDIC Careers!",
      "description": "Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Career Resources : Career Development & Professional Connections : UMass Amherst Skip to main content The University of Massachusetts Amherst Open UMass Global Links Menu Visit Apply Give Search UMass.edu Menu Career Development & Professional Connections About Us Our Staff Career Centers Across UMass Our Newton Campus Handshake Login Student Outcomes Students Undergraduates Graduates Alumni Identity-Based Resources International Students Prospective Students UWW Students Employers Post Jobs and Internships Host an Event Career Fairs at UMass Why Recruit at UMass Internship Program Best Practices Recruiting Guidelines Contact Us Faculty Sponsor an Intern Career Events for Students Request a Presentation Resource Library Career Journey Expand Menu Item Self Discovery and Career Exploration Build Career Skills: Resumes, Job-searching, and Interviewing Learn Additional Technical, Creative, and Professional Skills Your Career Support Team Gain Experience: Internships, Co-ops, Research, and More! Is Graduate School Right for Me? Year-by-Year Checklist Tool Kits Expand Menu Item Resumes Cover Letters Career Fair Preparation Interviewing LinkedIn Learning Networking What Skills Do Employers Want? Applying to Grad School Photo Booth for Headshots Professional Wardrobe Closet Connections Expand Menu Item Career Communities Expand Menu Item Arts, Multimedia, and Entertainment Business, Financial Services, and Consulting Data and Information Technology Education, Human Services, and Counseling Engineering Government and Public Service Healthcare, Life Sciences, and Nursing Infrastructure and Transportation Law and Legal Services Research Sustainability, Environment, and Agriculture Career Centers Across UMass Expand Menu Item Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Education Engineering Graduate School Office of Professional Development Humanities & Fine Arts (HFA) Information & Computer Sciences (CICS) Isenberg School of Management (ISOM) Natural Sciences (CNS) Nursing Public Health and Health Sciences (SPHHS) Social & Behavioral Sciences (SBS) University Without Walls (UWW) Connect with UMass Alumni Using LinkedIn How to Network Jobs & Internships Expand Menu Item Internships, Co-ops, and Other Field Experiences Expand Menu Item Field Experience Definitions Internships Co-ops Research Civic Engagement and Service Learning Internships and Co-Ops at Charles River Campus UMass Internship Partner Programs Scholarships for Field Experiences Jobs Searching for Jobs & Internships Can I Do an Internship? Negotiating Job Offers Interviewing Using Handshake Carousel Welcome to BDIC Careers! Meet with a Career Counselor You aren’t alone on this journey. Schedule with Joanna Miles Schedule an Appointment through Handshake Schedule an Appointment through Handshake Build Your Brand BDIC is your superpower.  Learn how interdisciplinary studies give you a unique career advantage. BDIC > BDIC Superpower BDIC Is Your Superpower Internships BDIC students land great internships!  Learn where to find them and how to register for credit Jobs & Internships > Internships Learn More about Internships Outcomes BDIC students end up in a wide variety of industries. About > Student Outcomes Archive Find out where BDIC students go after graduation Work together to build out dreams on your timeline BDIC is your Superpower! As motivated students designing your interdisciplinary degree and brand, BDIC Careers is committed to offering personalized supports and career advising. We believe the power of interdisciplinary studies, combined with experiential learning and skills-based coursework, will rocket you towards your goals.  Not sure what you want to do yet?  No problem!  BDIC offers programming and advising to bring clarity to the career development process. Schedule a 1:1 Appointment with Joanna Miles Schedule a 1:1 Appointment with Joanna Miles BDIC Guides to Get You Started Who Am I? Who Am I? Explore and discover your skills, values, personality, and interests with tailored career assessment tools. Get Prepared Get Prepared Resume and cover letters, job market insights, Interview preparation and salary negotiation tips can all be found here. Complement Your Academics Complement Your Academics Build your skills with over 13,000 self-guided courses on LinkedIn Learning Career Communities Career Communities Join career communities to explore industries in-depth and connect with UMASS alumni eager to share great career advice Internships Internships BDIC students complete internships year-round. Learn more, including how to fund and register your internship experience. Post-Grad Plans Post-Grad Plans Let’s demystify what comes next. Discover your options for graduate school and the best resources for a successful job search. Career Development & Professional Connections Whether you’re wondering where to begin, looking for an internship, or starting your job search, we will guide you through the process of your unique career development. Address: Goodell Hall | 140 Hicks Way | Amherst, MA 01003 Main Office Number: (413) 545-2224 Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Footer Students Career Journey Career Centers Resource Library Employers Handshake Contact Us UMass collegiate M - University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2025 University of Massachusetts Amherst · Site Policies · Accessibility"
