    "https://www.umass.edu/careers/education": {
      "title": "Welcome to the Education Career Resources Page",
      "description": "Education Career Resources : Career Development & Professional Connections : UMass Amherst Skip to main content The University of Massachusetts Amherst Open UMass Global Links Menu Visit Apply Give Search UMass.edu Menu Career Development & Professional Connections About Us Our Staff Career Centers Across UMass Our Newton Campus Handshake Login Student Outcomes Students Undergraduates Graduates Alumni Identity-Based Resources International Students Prospective Students UWW Students Employers Post Jobs and Internships Host an Event Career Fairs at UMass Why Recruit at UMass Internship Program Best Practices Recruiting Guidelines Contact Us Faculty Sponsor an Intern Career Events for Students Request a Presentation Resource Library Career Journey Expand Menu Item Self Discovery and Career Exploration Build Career Skills: Resumes, Job-searching, and Interviewing Learn Additional Technical, Creative, and Professional Skills Your Career Support Team Gain Experience: Internships, Co-ops, Research, and More! Is Graduate School Right for Me? Year-by-Year Checklist Tool Kits Expand Menu Item Resumes Cover Letters Career Fair Preparation Interviewing LinkedIn Learning Networking What Skills Do Employers Want? Applying to Grad School Photo Booth for Headshots Professional Wardrobe Closet Connections Expand Menu Item Career Communities Expand Menu Item Arts, Multimedia, and Entertainment Business, Financial Services, and Consulting Data and Information Technology Education, Human Services, and Counseling Engineering Government and Public Service Healthcare, Life Sciences, and Nursing Infrastructure and Transportation Law and Legal Services Research Sustainability, Environment, and Agriculture Career Centers Across UMass Expand Menu Item Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Education Engineering Graduate School Office of Professional Development Humanities & Fine Arts (HFA) Information & Computer Sciences (CICS) Isenberg School of Management (ISOM) Natural Sciences (CNS) Nursing Public Health and Health Sciences (SPHHS) Social & Behavioral Sciences (SBS) University Without Walls (UWW) Connect with UMass Alumni Using LinkedIn How to Network Jobs & Internships Expand Menu Item Internships, Co-ops, and Other Field Experiences Expand Menu Item Field Experience Definitions Internships Co-ops Research Civic Engagement and Service Learning Internships and Co-Ops at Charles River Campus UMass Internship Partner Programs Scholarships for Field Experiences Jobs Searching for Jobs & Internships Can I Do an Internship? Negotiating Job Offers Interviewing Using Handshake Carousel Welcome to the Education Career Resources Page Resources for Education Students Discover a collection of career resources for education students, including resume and cover letter guides, interview tips, and more. Education Career Resources Education Career Resources Getting Started with Handshake Whether you want to schedule a 1:1 appointment with an advisor or look for a job, Handshake has resources to get your career to the next level. Resources > How to Use Handshake (for Students) Read More Job Application Materials Browse resources to help you put together your application materials, including your resume, cover letter, personal statement, and portfolio. Resources > Job Application Materials for Teachers Read More Interviewing Explore tips on how to show off your best self during an interview, including sample questions and practice resources. Resources > Interviewing Read More Networking with Education Alumni Visit the Education Career Community and connect with UMass Alumni in the field of education. Education, Human Services, and Counseling Career Community Read More Applying for Jobs in Education Resources for applying to jobs, including lists of job postings, career fairs, and more. Resources > Applying for Teaching Jobs Read More Applying to Grad School A graduate degree can open the door for many opportunities after graduation - see if getting a Master's or PhD is right for you. Resources > Applying to Grad School Read More Education Faculty: Interested in having a Career Professional present in your class? Click here to learn more! Welcome to The College of Education Career page. Whether you are trying to determine your ideal role as an educator, ready to apply for jobs, or need help preparing for an interview, we invite you to partner with us as you embark on your career development journey. Education News Read More Go to: How to Write Your LinkedIn Profile April 29, 2026 Internship Photo Contest 2026 Each year, the Career Hub at UMass hosts an internship photo contest with prizes for the best submissions. Any UMass Amherst student who completed an internship, co-op, research, or other field experience from September 1, 2025 to August 31st, 2026 is eligible to enter. Go to: How to Write Your LinkedIn Profile June 10, 2025 The Balanced Search: 5 Wellness Tips for Job Seekers Looking for work can feel like a full-time job, full of uncertainty, rejection, and self-doubt. It is easy to fall into a vicious cycle of endless applications, comparison, and burnout. By approaching your search with intention and self-compassion, you can reduce stress, protect your energy, and even improve your confidence and performance. Making space for your wellness can be the key to your success. Here are a few tips to boost your well-being during the job search. Go to: How to Write Your LinkedIn Profile May 6, 2025 Spotlight: Education Graduates from the Class of 2025 We have already seen many success stories from the Education Class of 2025. Here are a few of our standout stars, each exemplifying excellence, determination, and innovation in their respective fields. Their achievements inspire us and set a high standard for future classes. Meet Stephanie Lare Stephanie brings experience across a range of diverse programs and educational environments within higher education and is deeply passionate about supporting students as they thrive academically, personally, and professionally. In her role as Assistant Director of Career Advising and Student Success in the College of Education, she supports students in exploring internship opportunities and provides comprehensive career guidance. Stephanie takes a holistic, student-centered approach to every interaction, recognizing that each student’s journey is unique and offers tailored support to empower their success. Reach out to Stephanie to Make an Appointment Reach out to Stephanie to Make an Appointment Education Career Resources Getting Started with Handshake Whether you're looking for internships or want to schedule a 1:1 appointment, Handshake has resources to get your career to a new level. Read More Job Application Materials A guide to putting together your application materials, including your resume, cover letter, personal statement, and portfolio. Read More Interviewing Interview tips, including sample interview questions. Read More Network through Connect UMass Visit the Education Career Community and connect with UMass Alumni in the field of education. Read More Applying for Educator Jobs Resources for applying for jobs, including lists of job web sites, career fairs, and more. Read More Applying to Grad School A graduate degree can open the door for many opportunities after graduation - see if getting a Master's or PhD is right for you. Read More Career Development & Professional Connections Whether you’re wondering where to begin, looking for an internship, or starting your job search, we will guide you through the process of your unique career development. Address: Goodell Hall | 140 Hicks Way | Amherst, MA 01003 Main Office Number: (413) 545-2224 Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Footer Students Career Journey Career Centers Resource Library Employers Handshake Contact Us UMass collegiate M - University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2025 University of Massachusetts Amherst · Site Policies · Accessibility"
