    "https://www.umass.edu/humanities-arts/careers": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "HFA Career Services : College of Humanities & Fine Arts : UMass Amherst Skip to main content The University of Massachusetts Amherst Open UMass Global Links Menu Visit Apply Give Search UMass.edu College of Humanities & Fine Arts Main navigation Academics Toggle submenu for Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Certificate Programs Courses See All Academic Programs UMass Admissions Financial Aid and Scholarships Cornerstone Initiative Academic Advising Why HFA? Research Toggle submenu for Research Research Centers and Institutes Research News Funding, Awards, and Recognition Research Areas Campus & Outreach Toggle submenu for Campus & Outreach Community Engagement Faces of HFA Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Tiny Spaces, Big Ideas Student Leadership Group Support HFA HFA Days Advising & Careers Toggle submenu for Advising & Careers Exploratory Track Opportunity Scholars Financial Aid and Scholarships Academic Advising HFA Career Services About Toggle submenu for About News Events Directory Dean's Office Alumni and Friends Resources for Current Students Resources for Faculty & Staff Communications Support Contact Breadcrumb Home HFA Career Services We offer job and internship guidance, interview prep, career exploration, networking support, and resume reviews. Meet with a Career Advisor Find Jobs and Internships Access Career Guides Explore Career Paths Build Employment-Ready Skills Grow Your Network Schedule an Appointment Audiences We Serve: Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Alumni and Recent Graduates International Students Faculty and Staff Parents and Families Employers In the Spotlight \"One of the greatest gifts of a humanities education is that it teaches you to understand people. Studying literature, writing, and language helped me become a better listener, communicator, and critical thinker. It challenged me to consider perspectives different from my own and reminded me that every person has a story worth understanding.\" Warren Charleston , Bachelor of Arts in English 19 Featured Events See all events Online 10 Sep 12:00 pm Careers National Organization on Disability's Fall 2026 Virtual Career Fair Online 10 Sep 3:00 pm Careers Smithsonian - Internship Info Session 11 Sep 1:00 pm Careers Amherst Area Employers + Arts & Humanities Internship Fair - Fall 2026 In the News See all news Academics Melissa Mueller Edits New Collector's Edition of Barnard's Sappho A new collector's edition of Mary Barnard's translation of Sappho, edited by Professor Melissa Mueller, will be published Sept. 1. August 10, 2026 Every student deserves a meaningful career aligned with their values. You don’t have to have your career path figured out, and you don’t have to go it alone. Our resources are available to all HFA students, alums, faculty, and staff. HFA Career Services provides one-on-one career advising, career courses, skills training, post-graduation support, in-class presentations, experiential education programs, and employer events. Meet the HFA Career Services team Site footer College of Humanities & Fine Arts Find us on Facebook Find us on YouTube Find us on LinkedIn Find us on Instagram Find us on Bluesky Bluesky Address 150 Hicks Way Amherst , MA 01003-9274 United States Academics Explore Our Programs Undergraduate Graduate Continuing and Professional Education Research Research News Research Areas Research Centers and Institutes The School About HFA News Events Directory Contact Info for... Current Students Faculty & Staff University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2026 University of Massachusetts Amherst Site policies Privacy Non-discrimination notice Accessibility Terms of use"
