    "https://www.isenberg.umass.edu/career-success/chase-career-center": {
      "title": "Chase Career Center",
      "description": "Chase Career Center : Isenberg School of Management : UMass Amherst Skip to main content The University of Massachusetts Amherst Open UMass Global Links Menu Visit Apply Give Search UMass.edu Menu Isenberg School of Management One.Isenberg Admissions Contact Us About Expand Menu Item Office of the Dean Access, Collaboration, and Engagement for Success Rankings Strategic Priorities Centers Expand Menu Item Berthiaume Center for Entrepreneurship Business Communication Center Center for International Securities and Derivatives Markets Massachusetts Small Business Development Center McCormack Center for Sport Research & Education Virtual Center for Supernetworks Faculty & Research Expand Menu Item Research & Publications Our Faculty Academic Departments Expand Menu Item Accounting Business Communication Program Finance Hospitality & Tourism Management Management Mark H. McCormack Sport Management Marketing Operations & Information Management Titled Faculty Faculty & Research News Programs Expand Menu Item Undergraduate Programs Expand Menu Item On Campus Expand Menu Item Academics Majors Student Success Campus Life Admissions Tuition & Aid Bachelor's Degree Completion Expand Menu Item Academics Advising Admissions Tuition & Aid 4+1 Programs Graduate Programs Expand Menu Item Online MBA Expand Menu Item Academics Career Student Experience Admissions Advising Resources Hybrid MBA Expand Menu Item Academics Career Student Experience Admissions Advising Resources On-Campus MBA Expand Menu Item Academics Career Student Experience Admissions Advising Resources MS in Accounting Expand Menu Item MS in Accounting Professional Track Expand Menu Item Academics Career Student Experience Admissions Advising Resources MS in Accounting Transitions Track Expand Menu Item Academics Career Student Experience Admissions Advising Resources MS in Business Analytics Expand Menu Item On-Campus MSBA Expand Menu Item Academics Career Student Experience Admissions Advising Resources Online MSBA Expand Menu Item Academics Career Student Experience Admissions Advising Resources Master of Finance Expand Menu Item Academics Career Student Experience Admissions Advising Resources MS in Management Expand Menu Item Academics Admissions Advising Resources Career Student Experience MS in Sport Management Expand Menu Item Academics Admissions Student Experience Tuition & Aid MBA/MS Dual Degrees Doctoral Program Expand Menu Item Academics Concentrations Admissions Community Funding Online Programs Expand Menu Item Bachelor's Degree Completion Online MBA MS in Accounting MS in Business Analytics Certificates Certificates Expand Menu Item Undergraduate Certificates Graduate Certificates Career Expand Menu Item Office of Career Success IConnect - Career Services Hire our Students Outcomes for Success Expand Menu Item Undergraduate Outcomes Graduate Outcomes Community Expand Menu Item News & Stories Calendars & Events Social Networks Alumni Directory Info For Expand Menu Item Future Students Expand Menu Item Undergraduate Program Undergraduate Degree Completion 4+1 Programs Master's Degrees Doctoral Program Online Programs Certificates Admissions Connect With Us Current Students Expand Menu Item Undergrads Graduate Students Expand Menu Item On-Campus MBA Students Online MBA Students MF Students MS Accounting Students MS Accounting Transitions Students MS Sport Students Degree Completion Online Students Entrepreneurship IConnect - Career Services Calendars & Events School News International Graduate Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Career Success / Chase Career Center Chase Career Center About the Chase Career Center The Chase Career Center has an experienced team of career professionals who are dedicated to serving the career and professional development needs of Isenberg students, as well as the talent acquisition needs of the many valued employer partners. Students should begin their career exploration process early, so they are encouraged to visit during their first semester on campus. The Chase Career Center team is here for its students and is prepared to work with them at all stages of their career development process. Whether they’re unsure about a career path or actively seeking an internship or full-time job, the Chase Career Center’s goal is to help students build a career plan and develop the essential skills and insights they need for a successful and rewarding career journey. Working as a Career Peer has allowed me to not only interact and mentor top level students, but also has given me the opportunity to polish my own networking profile. The career coaches were instrumental in perfecting my interview skills to secure multiple internships, and eventually a full-time job. Colin Nally '24 Finance What truly defined my experience with Career Services is the personalized attention and genuine care they demonstrate. Whether I had questions about career paths, job opportunities, or doctoral school options, they were always there to offer guidance and support tailored to my individual needs and aspirations. I was able to secure an amazing job in my desired field even before graduating. Sherrell Riley '24 MBA/MSBA I utilized the resources at Chase during my sophomore year to improve my resume and prepare for interviews. Now, as a career peer, I feel energized and excited to connect with underclassmen and offer advice that is tailored to their individual path. Janna Chi '25 Accounting Previous Slide Next Slide 3 Visit IConnect to make an appointment to meet with a Career Coach or a Career Peer or to get the latest updates on jobs, internships, and career events – both in person and remote. Set up a personalized profile to receive relevant posts right when they come out. Access our career resources and tools, ready to use at any time. Dig in. There’s lots to discover! Visit IConnect Visit IConnect Profiles Chelsea Connelly Associate Director, Graduate Career Development Chelsea Connelly View Profile Lea Herrick Associate Director of Outreach & Employer Relations Lea Herrick View Profile Trista Hevey Executive Director, Graduate Employer Relations & Outreach Trista Hevey View Profile Bonnie Jurgensmier Assistant Director, Career Development Bonnie Jurgensmier View Profile Alaina Kendrick Associate Director, Graduate Career Development | Career Coach Alaina Kendrick View Profile Silas McClung Career Coach Silas McClung View Profile Noelle Bieda Associate Director, Employer Relations Noelle Bieda View Profile Haley Parker Office Manager Haley Parker View Profile Melissa Salva Executive Director, Employer Relations & Operations Melissa Salva View Profile Rachel Snyder Director, Graduate Career Development Rachel Snyder View Profile Amanda Upton Associate Director, Career Development Amanda Upton View Profile Previous Slide Next Slide Isenberg School of Management University of Massachusetts Amherst 121 Presidents Drive Amherst, MA 01003 https://www.linkedin.com/school/isenberg-school-of-management-umass-amherst/ https://www.facebook.com/isenbergumass https://www.instagram.com/isenbergumass https://www.youtube.com/IsenbergUMass https://x.com/Isenbergumass https://bsky.app/profile/isenbergumass.bsky.social Quick Links Apply Now Visit Us Give Back About Programs Departments Calendars & Events News & Stories Info For... Alumni Current Students Faculty & Staff Future Students International Grad Students UMass collegiate M - University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2025 University of Massachusetts Amherst · Site Policies · Accessibility"
    },
    "https://www.umass.edu/natural-sciences/advising/careers": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "Career and Professional Development : College of Natural Sciences : UMass Amherst Skip to main content The University of Massachusetts Amherst Open UMass Global Links Menu Visit Apply Give Search UMass.edu College of Natural Sciences Main navigation Academics Toggle submenu for Academics Undergraduate programs Graduate programs Certificate programs Flexible and online learning All academic programs Courses See all departments Degree requirements Info for prospective students Pre-college programs Student Success Toggle submenu for Student Success CNS Student Success Center Academic Advising Career and Professional Development Graduate Student Success Pre-Med/Pre-Health Advising Belonging and Strategic Engagement Your Academic Deans First Year Opportunities Advising FAQs Scholarships Student Organizations Research Toggle submenu for Research Research centers & institutes Undergraduate research Greenhouses Industry partnerships Research support CNS Bridge and Seed Funding (BSF) program Scientific glassblowing laboratory Campus & Outreach Toggle submenu for Campus & Outreach Diversity, Equity & Inclusion Student Success and Diversity Eureka! Community Connections Giving Center for Agriculture, Food, and the Environment UMass Extension About Toggle submenu for About News Stories Events People Meet the leadership Buildings and facilities Contact Information for faculty & staff Information for alumni Breadcrumb Home Student Success Career and Professional Development About CNS is committed to helping students gain experiential learning opportunities and professional training to prepare for meaningful careers. Come to us to learn about field experience opportunities (internships, co-ops, research, and more) and strategies to increase your visible value to employers well before you graduate. In addition to your academics, experiential learning is what will help you get into graduate school or land a job after college. Start building your experiential learning now. The CNS Career Center is located in Morrill II, Suite 321. We offer both remote and in-person career advising appointments. Meet with a Career Advisor sooner rather than later, so we can help you figure out next steps and work with you to bring out your skills and experiences to demonstrate to employers. Overview links Make a career advising appointment on Handshake Connect on LinkedIn Career Development Handbook Explore the Career Center Career advising Resumes and cover letters CNS Graduate Student Career Resources For employers Job, internship, and co-op searching Handshake Interviewing and job offers Applying to graduate school Frequently asked questions CNS Biochemistry and Neuroscience major talking about her internship experience Undergraduate Destination Reports Check out the first destinations of our recent graduates. Class of 2024 Class of 2023 Class of 2022 Class of 2021 Class of 2020 Site footer College of Natural Sciences Find us on X Find us on Facebook Find us on YouTube Find us on LinkedIn Find us on Instagram Address 101 Stockbridge Hall 80 Campus Center Way Amherst , MA 01003-9248 United States Phone number (413) 545-2766 Info for... Current students Faculty and staff Alumni Academics Explore our programs Departments The college About CNS News Events Contact Contact CNS Directory University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2026 University of Massachusetts Amherst Site policies Privacy Non-discrimination notice Accessibility Terms of use"
    },
    "https://www.umass.edu/careers/nursing": {
      "title": "Elaine Marieb College of Nursing Career Page",
      "description": "Elaine Marieb College of Nursing Career Resources : Career Development & Professional Connections : UMass Amherst Skip to main content The University of Massachusetts Amherst Open UMass Global Links Menu Visit Apply Give Search UMass.edu Menu Career Development & Professional Connections About Us Our Staff Career Centers Across UMass Our Newton Campus Handshake Login Student Outcomes Students Undergraduates Graduates Alumni Identity-Based Resources International Students Prospective Students UWW Students Employers Post Jobs and Internships Host an Event Career Fairs at UMass Why Recruit at UMass Internship Program Best Practices Recruiting Guidelines Contact Us Faculty Sponsor an Intern Career Events for Students Request a Presentation Resource Library Career Journey Expand Menu Item Self Discovery and Career Exploration Build Career Skills: Resumes, Job-searching, and Interviewing Learn Additional Technical, Creative, and Professional Skills Your Career Support Team Gain Experience: Internships, Co-ops, Research, and More! Is Graduate School Right for Me? Year-by-Year Checklist Tool Kits Expand Menu Item Resumes Cover Letters Career Fair Preparation Interviewing LinkedIn Learning Networking What Skills Do Employers Want? Applying to Grad School Photo Booth for Headshots Professional Wardrobe Closet Connections Expand Menu Item Career Communities Expand Menu Item Arts, Multimedia, and Entertainment Business, Financial Services, and Consulting Data and Information Technology Education, Human Services, and Counseling Engineering Government and Public Service Healthcare, Life Sciences, and Nursing Infrastructure and Transportation Law and Legal Services Research Sustainability, Environment, and Agriculture Career Centers Across UMass Expand Menu Item Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Education Engineering Graduate School Office of Professional Development Humanities & Fine Arts (HFA) Information & Computer Sciences (CICS) Isenberg School of Management (ISOM) Natural Sciences (CNS) Nursing Public Health and Health Sciences (SPHHS) Social & Behavioral Sciences (SBS) University Without Walls (UWW) Connect with UMass Alumni Using LinkedIn How to Network Jobs & Internships Expand Menu Item Internships, Co-ops, and Other Field Experiences Expand Menu Item Field Experience Definitions Internships Co-ops Research Civic Engagement and Service Learning Internships and Co-Ops at Charles River Campus UMass Internship Partner Programs Scholarships for Field Experiences Jobs Searching for Jobs & Internships Can I Do an Internship? Negotiating Job Offers Interviewing Using Handshake Carousel Elaine Marieb College of Nursing Career Page Resources for Nursing Students Review a collection of career resources for nursing students, including resume and cover letter guides, interview tips, and more. Nursing Career Resources Nursing Career Resources Nursing Faculty: Interested in having a Career Professional present in your class? Click here to learn more! Welcome to the Nursing Career Development page at UMass Amherst. In addition to the many wonderful resources you can find through the Elaine Marieb College of Nursing, you also have access to professional career support through the Career Hub. Browse these resources, make an appointment, and help yourself become the medical professional you want to be. Nursing Career Articles and Events Read More Go to: How to Write Your LinkedIn Profile April 29, 2026 Internship Photo Contest 2026 Each year, the Career Hub at UMass hosts an internship photo contest with prizes for the best submissions. Any UMass Amherst student who completed an internship, co-op, research, or other field experience from September 1, 2025 to August 31st, 2026 is eligible to enter. Go to: How to Write Your LinkedIn Profile June 10, 2025 The Balanced Search: 5 Wellness Tips for Job Seekers Looking for work can feel like a full-time job, full of uncertainty, rejection, and self-doubt. It is easy to fall into a vicious cycle of endless applications, comparison, and burnout. By approaching your search with intention and self-compassion, you can reduce stress, protect your energy, and even improve your confidence and performance. Making space for your wellness can be the key to your success. Here are a few tips to boost your well-being during the job search. Go to: How to Write Your LinkedIn Profile June 10, 2025 Spotlight: Nursing Graduates from the Class of 2025 We have already seen many success stories from the Nursing Class of 2025. Here are a few of our standout stars, each exemplifying excellence, determination, and innovation in their respective fields. Their achievements inspire us and set a high standard for future classes. Meet Dr. Elise Carrier Meet Dr. Elise Carrier Associate Director of Career and Professional Development Elise is an experienced higher education professional with an unwavering passion for empowering individuals to realize and achieve their professional aspirations. In her role as the Associate Director for Career and Professional Development at The Career Hub, Elise is instrumental in the creation and implementation of a diverse spectrum of career resources geared towards Nursing students. Her focus extends from fostering career exploration to providing skill-building opportunities, ensuring that students are equipped with the tools necessary to explore their nursing careers. Schedule an Appointment with Elise via Handshake Schedule an Appointment with Elise via Handshake Getting Started with Handshake Whether you're looking for internships or want to schedule a 1:1 appointment, Handshake has resources to get your career to a new level. Read More Job Application Materials A guide to putting together your application materials, including your resume and cover letter. Read More Interviewing Interview tips, including sample interview questions. Read More Networking for Nurses Meet with alumni through Connect UMass, or browse student and professional organizations related to the medical field. Read More Applying for Nursing Jobs Resources for applying for jobs, including lists of job web sites, career fairs, and more. Read More Applying to Grad School A graduate degree can open the door for many opportunities after graduation - see if getting a Master's or PhD is right for you. Read More Top Healthcare Employers at UMass Amherst Career Development & Professional Connections Whether you’re wondering where to begin, looking for an internship, or starting your job search, we will guide you through the process of your unique career development. Address: Goodell Hall | 140 Hicks Way | Amherst, MA 01003 Main Office Number: (413) 545-2224 Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Footer Students Career Journey Career Centers Resource Library Employers Handshake Contact Us UMass collegiate M - University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2025 University of Massachusetts Amherst · Site Policies · Accessibility"
    },
    "https://www.umass.edu/public-health-sciences/career-planning": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "Office of Career Planning : School of Public Health & Health Sciences : UMass Amherst Skip to main content The University of Massachusetts Amherst Open UMass Global Links Menu Visit Apply Give Search UMass.edu School of Public Health & Health Sciences Main navigation Academics Toggle submenu for Academics Academic programs Biostatistics Community Health Education Environmental Health Sciences Epidemiology Health Policy and Management Kinesiology Nutrition Professional Programs Public Health Sciences Speech, Language, and Hearing Sciences Graduate Admissions UMass Admissions Financial aid and scholarships Faculty directory Courses Research Toggle submenu for Research Center for Community Health Equity Research Center for Program Evaluation Institute for Global Health Research news and highlights Research areas Research centers and institutes Research Administration Office (RAO) Campus & Outreach Toggle submenu for Campus & Outreach Academic Dean & Office of Academic Success Center for Language, Speech, and Hearing Office of Career Planning Office of Public Health Practice and Outreach About Toggle submenu for About Accreditation Diversity, Equity and Inclusion News Events Directory Our New Building Support SPHHS Resources for current students Resources for faculty & staff Visit us Contact us Senior Recognition Ceremony Breadcrumb Home Office of Career Planning Working with students on a wide range of career planning activities and skill development. About Welcome! Our dedicated staff is ready to assist undergraduate and graduate SPHHS students with a variety of career-related needs. The SPHHS Office of Career Planning validates and empowers students to explore their unique strengths, interests, and competencies, guiding them to successfully navigate their career goals. The staff helps students develop lifelong career planning tools that inspire them to bring their authentic selves into a diverse and global workforce. Located in the SPHHS HUB - third floor, we are ready to help out with career decision making, internship/job searching, interviewing, cover letters, resumes, and so much more. You don’t have to go it alone. We are here for you whether you are just starting to explore your options or you know exactly where you are going. Hours: Monday – Friday 9am-5pm Overview links Schedule an appointment on Handshake SPHHS Job, Internship & Practicum Postings Student Local Employment Opportunities Follow us on Instagram 100% of respondents from career satisfaction surveys indicate they were very or extremely satisfied with OCP services 2022-23 99% of SPHHS undergraduates either get a job, post internship/fellowship, or go on to graduate/professional school 85% of organizations that hosted an SPHHS intern/practicum student hired them in the future 55+ different industries/sectors across all four SPHHS majors Student Resources Career Assessment Tools Career Resources by Major Identity and Career Resources Internships & Greater Boston Spring Semester Resumes and Cover Letters Interviewing Alumni Networking, Career Chats & Interviewing Applying to Graduate or Health Professions School Job, Internship & Practicum Postings, Offers Services Career Fairs, Events & Workshops AcademicWorks and SPHHS Scholarships FAQ For Graduate Students For Employers For Faculty and Staff Amplify Mentor Program (AMP) Careers in Public Health Virtual Career Chat Careers in Public Health Virtual Career Chat, Spring 2022 with three alumni in different fields. Community stories Image Marisa DaCosta BS in Public Health Sciences , ‘22 Medical student Meet Marisa Image Rithika Senthilkumar BS in Public Health Sciences , ‘22 Medical student Meet Rithika Image Annika Zimmerman Doctor of Audiology (AuD) , ‘21 Audiology extern, Walter Reed National Military Medical Center Meet Annika Image Alina Schmidt BS in Nutrition , ‘17 Clinical Dietitian, Baystate Medical Meet Alina Career Ambassadors The Office of Career Planning Career Ambassadors look forward to meeting with you! Please click below to view our Fall 2026 hours, located in the SPHHS HUB -Room 323. Career Ambassador Peer Advising Greater Boston Spring Internship Program SPHHS undergraduate students with at least 48 credits have the unique opportunity to earn academic credit while working and training in the Greater Boston area during the spring semester. Internship partner sites include major hospitals, rehabilitation programs, and more. Learn more Mary Ellen Liseno Director of Career Planning Oversees OCP strategic plan, coordinates the Career Ambassador program and designs and presents various career workshops and programs. meliseno [at] umass [dot] edu (meliseno[at]umass[dot]edu) Schedule an appointment Aimee Gilbert-Loinaz Assistant Director of Internships and Employer Engagement Aimee works to create & manage partnerships between SPHHS and employers in the field of public health. Her goal is to place students in challenging positions that are compatible with their background and professional goals. aimeegl [at] umass [dot] edu (aimeegl[at]umass[dot]edu) Schedule an appointment Rachel Comerford Assistant Director of Career Planning Focus on career exploration; weekly CareerSNAP newsletter; resume/cover letter/personal statement review; career-focused workshops; interview preparation; SPHHS graduate school fair rachel [dot] comerford [at] umass [dot] edu (rachel[dot]comerford[at]umass[dot]edu) Schedule an appointment Tracy Eason Assistant Director of Graduate Students and Mentorship Program Tracy works with graduate students on their career exploration and planning, while also coordinating the undergraduate mentor program for SPHHS. taeason [at] umass [dot] edu (taeason[at]umass[dot]edu) Schedule an appointment Site footer School of Public Health & Health Sciences Find us on Facebook Find us on YouTube Find us on LinkedIn Find us on Instagram Address SPHHS Hub 10 Eastman Lane Amherst , MA 01003 United States Academics Explore our programs Undergraduate Graduate Certificate Post Baccalaureate Research Research News Research Areas Research Centers & Institutes The School About SPHHS News Events Directory Visit Contact Info for... Current students Faculty & staff University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2026 University of Massachusetts Amherst Site policies Privacy Non-discrimination notice Accessibility Terms of use"
    },
    "https://sbspathways.umass.edu/channels/career/": {
      "title": "Career",
      "description": "Career – SBS Pathways | University of Massachusetts Amherst SBS Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests College of Social & Behavioral Sciences Home Labor Market Insights Make an Appointment Prospective Students Seek Your Pathways Academic Experiential Career SBS Pathways Center Explore Academics Anthropology Communication Economics Journalism Landscape Architecture Legal Studies Managerial Economics Political Science Public Policy Environmental & Natural Resource Economics Social Thought & Political Economy (STPEC) Sociology Sustainable Community Development SBS Exploratory Track Minors, Certificates, and More SBS 4+1 Accelerated Masters Programs Explore Careers What are Career Communities? Advertising / Public Relations / Marketing Business / Entrepreneurship / Management / Consulting Health / Research / Education / Culture Environment / Natural Resources / Sustainability Finance / Investment / Real Estate / Insurance Government / Public Policy / International Relations Law / Legal Services / Criminology / Forensics Media / Journalism / Entertainment Non-Profit / Social Justice / Activism Technology / Data / Analytics Explore Your Communities Communities rooted in identity, experience, and support SBS RISE: Remedying Inequity through Student Engagement Black, Indigenous & Students of Color First Generation Students International Students LGBTQIA+ Students Student Athletes Students with Disabilities Students with Financial Need Transfer Students Veterans Women in the Workforce Post-Grad Planning SBS 4+1 Accelerated Masters Programs Graduate School Labor Market Insights Explore Career Outcomes International Careers Job Search National Scholarships / Fellowships Pre-Law Advising Year of Service / Volunteering Who We Serve Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Faculty and Staff Employers Prospective Students How do I? Complete Academic/Degree Tasks Apply for Scholarships and Awards Declare an SBS Major Meet with an Academic Advisor Meet with an Academic Dean Suggest New Courses Petition for Late Add Petition for Pass/Fail Withdraw from a Class/Petition for Late Withdrawal Petition for Course Credit Overload Release Academic Information (FERPA) Withdraw from the University Explore Majors, Experiential, and Professional Pathways Apply for Funding for Internships, Study Abroad, Research, and other High-impact Opportunities Assess My Skills and Interests Explore Majors Find an Undergraduate Research Opportunity Get Involved on Campus Learn about Different Career Paths Study Abroad Take Courses through the Five Colleges Domestic Exchange Get Career Ready Apply for Scholarships to Support Research or Internships Develop My Job Search Skills & Strategy Look for Internships and Jobs Meet with a Career Advisor Negotiate an Offer Network and Connect with Mentors Prepare a Resume and Cover Letter Prepare for/Navigate a Career Fair Prepare for an Interview Register an Internship for Credit Write a Personal Statement for Graduate School Career Your professional skill development and exploration starts as soon as you get to campus! You don’t need to know what you want to do after college. Seek opportunities to the develop skills that every employer seeks – like public speaking, writing, interpersonal, and analytic skills. Your SBS career team is here to help you explore what’s out there, connect with alumni, learn job search strategies, build experience by asking for more responsibility or new projects at work, seek leadership positions in clubs or volunteer organizations, and lay the groundwork for internships, and ultimately that first job. EXPLORE CAREER OUTCOMES LABOR MARKET INSIGHTS EXPERIENCES HOW-TO GUIDES AND RESOURCES RESOURCES KNOW YOURSELF EXPLORE YOUR OPTIONS DEVELOP YOUR SKILLS SEARCH FOR JOBS Explore Your Career Pathways We’ll guide you as you pursue and develop the competencies needed for careers in business and nonprofit / public service settings, graduate study, and meaningful engagement in civic life. These competencies involve the ability to think critically, creatively, and analytically and to apply skills and knowledge strategically across a range of contexts. Your SBS Career & Professional Development team can help you know yourself, explore your options, build your skills, develop a job search strategy, and connect with alumni mentors, so don’t be a stranger. Come meet with us ! Explore different sectors and industries by checking out our Career Communities . Learn about the sector, student and alumni stories and advice, job and internship postings, relevant events, and much more. Follow as many career communities as you’d like to explore, and receive jobs, internships, and events announcements curated to your interests. As you pursue your own SBS Pathways, you will build the following skills and competencies and learn to integrate, communicate, and apply them in various settings. These are the very characteristics employers say they would like to see more of in their applicants and employees: Core Competencies Career/Self Development Critical Thinking/Problem Solving Written and Oral Communication Teamwork / Collaboration Leadership Work Ethic & Professionalism Global/Intercultural Perspectives Technology Skip filter options to posts Featured Articles Filter Clear Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Blog Categories: Academic Success Tips Alumni Highlights Employer Spotlights Expert-Recommended Posts Faculty Highlights Front Page News Guest Blog Hot Jobs & Internships Peer Advisors' Corner Professional Advice Program Promotion Recent News Student Stories Close Clear Filters SBS Award for Fall Internships – Now Open Share This: Share SBS Award for Fall Internships – Now Open on Facebook Share SBS Award for Fall Internships – Now Open on LinkedIn Share SBS Award for Fall Internships – Now Open on X Copy Link Are you exploring or have you been hired for unpaid or underpaid internship for the Fall 2026 semester? Don’t let that stop you from engaging in that important and exciting professional development opportunity. SBS is offering scholarship awards to help  … By Koni Denham Show author info Koni Denham Director of Student Success & Dir. of First Year Seminars - SBS Send Email Read more » Applications for UMass Women into Leadership (UWiL) are now open Share This: Share Applications for UMass Women into Leadership (UWiL) are now open on Facebook Share Applications for UMass Women into Leadership (UWiL) are now open on LinkedIn Share Applications for UMass Women into Leadership (UWiL) are now open on X Copy Link Have you considered a career in public service? Are you interested in learning more about leadership? Do you want to gain hands-on experience, expand your professional network, and jump-start your career? Apply now to join UMass Women into Leadership (UWiL) ! … By Carol Sharick Show author info Carol Sharick Exec. Director of Career and Professional Development, SBS Read more » Closed.  Next round starts Oct. 5.  See Propel website for more info.  Fall Undergrad Research Opps for SBS Majors – deadline Aug. 23 (don’t wait til then!) Share This: Share Closed.  Next round starts Oct. 5.  See Propel website for more info.  Fall Undergrad Research Opps for SBS Majors – deadline Aug. 23 (don’t wait til then!) on Facebook Share Closed.  Next round starts Oct. 5.  See Propel website for more info.  Fall Undergrad Research Opps for SBS Majors – deadline Aug. 23 (don’t wait til then!) on LinkedIn Share Closed.  Next round starts Oct. 5.  See Propel website for more info.  Fall Undergrad Research Opps for SBS Majors – deadline Aug. 23 (don’t wait til then!) on X Copy Link Closed.  Next round starts Oct. 5.  See Propel website for more info.  Fall Undergrad Research Opps for SBS Majors - deadline Aug. 23 (don't wait til then!) The Propel program of the UMass Office of Undergraduate Research (OURS) has opened the applications for fall semester research assistantships. Sun