Management (ISOM) Natural Sciences (CNS) Nursing Public Health and Health Sciences (SPHHS) Social & Behavioral Sciences (SBS) University Without Walls (UWW) Connect with UMass Alumni Using LinkedIn How to Network Jobs & Internships Expand Menu Item Internships, Co-ops, and Other Field Experiences Expand Menu Item Field Experience Definitions Internships Co-ops Research Civic Engagement and Service Learning Internships and Co-Ops at Charles River Campus UMass Internship Partner Programs Scholarships for Field Experiences Jobs Searching for Jobs & Internships Can I Do an Internship? Negotiating Job Offers Interviewing Using Handshake Can I Do an Internship for Credit? Careers Resources Can I Do Internship Credit The answer depends on your department. First things first: any student can do an internship without earning academic credit for the experience, so long as they meet the legal requirements to work. For students wishing to earn academic credit for an internship, you need to see if your department allows it within your curriculum. Below is a list of all departments at UMass Amherst and their policies towards obtaining academic credit towards the completion of your degree. Students : Please check with an academic advisor in your department to see if a credited internship will work for your specific academic requirements. Most departments require you to have completed at least 45 credits and have a minimum of a 2.0 GPA to do an internship for credit. International Students : In order to engage in a paid internship (for F-1 and J-1 visa students) or an unpaid internship (for J-1 visa students), you must obtain internship credit during the semester(s) in which you are working. Check with the Office of Global Affairs (formerly the International Programs Office) to see what you need to do to get started. Faculty/Staff : If you would like to suggest an edit to your department's description, contact @email . Click Your School/College Below: BDIC : Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration CICS : Manning College of Information and Computer Sciences CNS : College of Natural Sciences CoE : Riccio College of Engineering EDU : College of Education HFA : College of Humanities and Fine Arts ISOM : Isenberg School of Management NUR : Elaine Marieb College of Nursing SBS : College of Social and Behavioral Science SPHHS : School of Public Health and Health Sciences Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students Course(s) : BDIC 398A, BDIC 498A Contact : Rebecca Schwartz | [email protected] Notes: BDIC allows 6 credits of internship, which equals 2 BDIC courses, to satisfy upper level course requirements in the BDIC degree. BDIC also accepts internship credits from other departments and UMASS 298. Return to the Top of Page Manning College of Information and Computer Sciences Computer Science Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students and International Graduate Students Course(s) : Domestic Undergraduate: COMPSCI 398A International Undergraduate: CICS 398T International Graduate: CICS 598T Contact : Undergraduate: Brian Krusell | @email Graduate: Elizabeth Parolski | @email Notes : Most internships completed by CICS Computer Science students are paid, uncredited internships. A complete outline on how to navigate the internship process as a CICS student can be found on the CICS Guide to Internships . Informatics Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students Course(s) : UMASS 298 Contact : Michelle Trim | @email Notes : A complete outline on how to navigate the internship process as a CICS student can be found on the CICS Guide to Internships . Return to the Top of Page College of Natural Sciences Animal Biotechnology & Biomedical Sciences Internships for Credit Available? : No Animal Science & Pre-Veterinary Science (VASCI) Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students Course(s) : ANIMLSCI 298, ANIMLSCI 398, ANIMLSCI 398D, ANIMLSCI 398S, ANIMLSCI 398V, ANIMLSCI 498, ANIMLSCI 498S, ANIMLSCI 498V Contact : Janice Telfer | @email Notes: On a case by case basis, students can petition to have x98 internship credits replace major requirements for BS-ANIMLSCI and BS-PRE VET majors. The BS-VET TECH requires 12 credits of ANIMLSCI 498V internships. Applied Mathematics (Graduate) Internships for Credit Available? : For International Graduate Students for CPT only Course(s) : MATH 696 Contact : Markos Katsoulakis | @email Applied Molecular Biotechnology Internships for Credit Available? : For Graduate Students Course(s) : MICROBIO 698 (AMB Practicum) Contact: Jeffrey Kane | @email Notes: During the summer session, students will participate in an internship at a biotechnology or pharmaceutical company. Alternatively, students will stay on campus during the summer and complete their research project and participate in “Lab Modules”. Arboriculture and Community Forest Management Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students (Associate) Course(s) : STOCKSCH 198F, STOCKSCH 198G, STOCKSCH 198T, STOCKSCH 298, STOCKSCH 298A, STOCKSCH 298FS, STOCKSCH 298P, STOCKSCH 398, STOCKSCH 398A, STOCKSCH 398B, STOCKSCH 398T, STOCKSCH 498, STOCKSCH 498Y Contact: Kristina Bezanson | @email Astronomy Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students Course(s) : ASTRON 498Y Contact : Todd Tripp (Chief Undergraduate Advisor) | @email Biochemistry & Molecular Biology Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students Only Course(s) : BIOCHEM 298, BIOCHEM 498Y Contact : Amy Springer | @email Notes : The Biochemistry & Molecular Biology department does not currently allow students to complete internship credit towards their major requirements . Biology Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate and Graduate Students Course(s) : Undergraduate: BIOLOGY 398B/398E Graduate: BIOLOGY 698 Contact : Bruce Byers | @email Notes: The Biology department allows up to 6 internship credits (BIOLOGY 398B) to count toward the major requirements, but no more than 6 total credits from internship, independent study, and TA combined. Building & Construction Technology Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students Course(s) : BCT 398, BCT 498, BCT 498Y Contact : Alex Schreyer | @email Notes: BCT offers up to 15 credits for a practicum, which can be counted towards electives in the program. Chemistry Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students Only Course(s) : CHEM 396/496 Contact : Ruthanne Paradise | @email Notes: Internship credits do not currently satisfy major requirements in Chemistry. Earth Systems Internships for Credit Available? : At Advisor Discretion Contact : Steven Petsch | @email Notes: Specific internships need to be discussed with the Chief Undergraduate Advisor. Environmental Conservation Internships for Credit Available? : For Graduate Students Course(s) : ECO 698, ECO 698S Contact : Lena Fletcher | @email Environmental Science Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students Course(s) : Undergraduate: ENVIRSCI 298, ENVIRSCI 389, ENVIRSCI 398S, ENVIRSCI 498 Campus Sustainability Fellowship: ENVIRSCI 598S Contact : Deb Henson | @email Notes : Environmental Science students must complete two 2 “praxis” (hands-on) courses that provide practical experience and skills in an environmental field. Praxis requirements can be fulfilled by selected coursework, independent study research, and internship credits. Food Science Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate and Graduate Students Course(s) : Undergraduate: UMASS 298, FOOD-SCI 398E, FOOD-SCI 498Y Graduate: FOOD-SCI 696/796, FOOD-SCI 699 (Thesis/Dissertation) Contact : David Mcclements | @email Geography Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate and Graduate Students (for grad students, see note below) Course(s) : Undergraduate: GEOGRAPH 298, GEOGRAPH 398R, GEOGRAPH 498, GEOGRAPH 498Y, Graduate: GEOGRAPH 698G (GIST Master's Program only) Contact : Toby Applegate | @email Notes : Students in the Globalization & International Studies Concentration must complete at least 6 of the credits for the degree in conjunction with an appropriate international academic experience involving a period of residence outside the United States, which can include an internship. Consult with the Geography Chief Undergraduate Advisor. Geology Internships for Credit Available? : No Geosciences Internships for Credit Available? : For Graduate Students Course(s) : GEO-SCI 698/798 Contact : David Boutt | @email Horticultural Sciences Internships for Credit Available? : No Landscape Contracting Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students (Associate) Course(s) : STOCKSCH 198F, STOCKSCH 198G, STOCKSCH 198T, STOCKSCH 298, STOCKSCH 298A, STOCKSCH 298FS, STOCKSCH 298P, STOCKSCH 398, STOCKSCH 398A, STOCKSCH 398B, STOCKSCH 398T, STOCKSCH 498, STOCKSCH 498Y Contact : Michael Davidsohn | @email Mathematics Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students and International Graduate Students for CPT Course(s) : Undergraduate: MATH 398 (for departmental credit), MATH 498Y (for credits towards graduation) Graduate: MATH 696/796, MATH 699/899 (Dissertation/Thesis) Contact : Sohrab Shahshahani | @email Notes: An internship in the department can fulfill an upper-level math elective in actuarial, applied math, pure math, or stats concentrations. Microbiology Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students and International Graduate Students for CPT Course(s) : Undergraduate: MICROBIO 398, MICROBIO 398A, MICROBIO 398PF Graduate: MICROBIO 698 (for CPT) Contact: Undergraduate: Heather Reed | @email Graduate: Jeffrey Kane | @email Notes: 3 credits of Independent Study (396) or Practicum (398) may be applied to the 35 Microbiology credit requirement. Molecular & Cellular Biology Internships for Credit Available? : For G