ts seeking to earn internship credit can register for UMASS 298/398/498. International Undergraduate Students : Contact Todd Butynski for more information. International Graduate Students : Contact Christina Mata for more information. Internships for Credit Available? : For International Undergraduate Students and International Graduate Students (see note for domestic students) Course(s) : International Undergraduate: BMED-ENG-296/396 International Graduate: BMED-ENG 696 Contact : Undergraduate : Sam Wojda | @email Graduate: Seth Donahue | @email Notes : International students completing a paid internship for credit may use Biomedical Engineering course listings. Domestic students seeking internship credits should use UMASS 298/398/498. Chemical Engineering Note: while engineering students can do internships for credit, most will graduate with more credits than they need. As a result, internships are typically either completed without obtaining academic credit during the summer or by international students seeking CPT (for paid internships) or AT (for paid or internships). Domestic students seeking to earn internship credit can register for UMASS 298/398/498. International Undergraduate Students : Contact Todd Butynski for more information. International Graduate Students : Contact Christina Mata for more information. Internships for Credit Available? : For International Undergraduate Students and International Graduate Students (see note for domestic students) Course(s) : International Undergraduate: CHEM-ENG 396 International Graduate: CHEM-ENG 796 Contact : Undergraduate Contact : Wei Fan | @email Graduate Contact: Stephen Nonnenmann | @email Notes : International students completing a paid internship for credit may use Chemical Engineering course listings. Domestic students seeking internship credits should use UMASS 298/398/498. Civil & Environmental Engineering Note: while engineering students can do internships for credit, most will graduate with more credits