ate: AFRO-AM 398/498Y Graduate: AFRO-AM 696/699/899 Contact : Undergraduate: Amilcar Shabazz | @email Graduate : James Smethurst | @email Architecture Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate and Graduate Students Course(s) : Undergraduate: ARCH 498/498A/498D/498E/498G Graduate: ARCH 698/698P Contact : Undergraduate: Erika Zekos | @email Graduate: Carey Clouse | @email Notes : For the BS Architecture degree, Architecture accepts independent studies (x96) and practica (x98) for required classes (except Gen Ed requirements). Art Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate and Graduate Students Course(s) : Undergraduate: ART 298/398/498/498Y Graduate: ART 696/796 Contact : Jeffrey Kasper | @email Notes : Internship credits must be arts-related, sponsored by full-time department faculty, and approved by the Program Director. Art majors can take a maximum of 12 Independent Study and/or Practicum credits toward degree requirements as Studio Electives. Discipline requirements cannot be fulfilled by Independent Study or Practicum unless approved by the Undergraduate Program Director. Classics Internships for Credit Available? : Usually No - See Notes Course(s) : Undergraduate: CLASSICS 298/498/498Y, GREEK 498Y Graduate: LATIN-ED 500U Contact : Undergraduate: Brian Breed | @email Graduate: Virginia Closs | @email Notes : Classics does not have an explicit policy regarding internships for credit. Students may petition the department to allow an experience to count toward one of the major requirements if it is determined the experience sufficiently complements the curriculum. Comparative Literature Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students Only Course(s) : COMP-LIT 398/498Y Contact : Jessica Barr | @email Dance Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students Course(s) : DANCE 398J (Summer Only), DANCE 498Y Contact : Thomas Vacanti | @email Notes : Undergrad students can earn 1-18 credits for internships with DANCE 389J during the Summer, or DANCE 498Y during the rest of the year. East Asian Languages & Cultures Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate and Graduate Students Course(s) : Undergraduate: CHINESE 498Y, JAPANESE 498Y Graduate: CHINESE 698/698Y, JAPANESE 698/698Y Contact : Chinese Undergraduate: Zhijun Wang | @email Chinese Graduate: Elena Suet-Ying Chiu | @email Japanese Undergraduate: Yuki Yoshimura | @email Japanese Graduate: Bruce Baird | baird.umass.edu English Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate and Graduate Students Course(s) : Undergraduate: ENGLISH 298/398/498/498Y Graduate: ENGLISH 698 Contact : Undergraduate: Janis Greve | @email Graduate: Daniel Sack | @email Notes : Students can earn 200 or 300 elective credit with a 3+ credit internship if it is Letter-Graded ENGLISH 398 only. Film Studies Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students Only Course(s) : FILM-ST 398 Contact : Barbara Zecchi | @email Notes : Students can take 6 credits of internship as part of the 7 electives in Film Studies. More information available on the Film Studies Internship page. French and Francophone Studies Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate and Graduate Students Course(s) : Undergraduate: FRENCHST 298/498Y Graduate: FRENCHST 698/798P Contact : Undergraduate: Eva Valenta | @email Graduate: Luke Bouvier | @email German & Scandinavian Studies Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate and Graduate Students (German only) Course(s) : Undergraduate: GERMAN 398/498Y Graduate: GERMAN 698 Contact : Undergraduate: Sara E. Jackson | @email Graduate: Mariana Ivanova | @email Notes : For the German Studies track, students may replace any course with an internship. STEM-German majors have the option to earn 1-8 credits in an internship towards their STEM-German major. History Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate and Graduate Students Course(s) : Undergraduate: HISTORY 298/298Y/498Y Graduate: HISTORY 698/698A Contact : Undergraduate: Sarah Cornell | [email protected] Graduate: Joel Wolfe | @email History of Art & Architecture Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students Only Course(s) : ART-HIST 298/398 Contact : Undergraduate: Margaret Vickery | @email Graduate: Karen Kurczynski | @email Italian Studies Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate and Graduate Students Course(s) : Undergraduate: ITALIAN 298/398/498Y Graduate: ITALIAN 598 Contact : Undergraduate: Melina Masterson | @email Graduate: Michael Papio | @email Judaic & Near Eastern Studies Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students Course(s) : ARABIC 298/398 HEBREW 298/398/498Y JUDAIC STUDIES 298/398/498Y MIDEAST 289/398/498Y Contact : David Mednicoff | @email Linguistics Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate and Graduate Students Course(s) : See notes Contact : Undergraduate: Kristine Yu | @email Graduate: Rajesh Ghatt | @email Notes : Will allow internships to count toward major requirement on a case-by-case basis. Music Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate and Graduate Students Course(s) : Undergraduate: MUSIC 298/398/498 Graduate: MUSIC 798B Contact : Undergraduate: Erica Drake | @email Graduate: Nicole Avakian| @email Notes : Undergrad students can earn 1-18 credits for internships MUSIC 298, MUSIC 398, and MUSIC 498. Philosophy Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students or International Graduate Students (for CPT) Course(s) : PHIL 398/498Y; PHIL 600 (CPT only) Contact : Undergraduate: Vanessa de Harven | @email Graduate: Alejandro Perez Carballlo | @email Russian, Eurasian & Polish Studies Program Internships for Credit Available? : No Spanish & Portuguese Studies Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students Only Course(s) : SPANISH 398/498Y PORTUG 398/398B/498 Contact : Patricia Gubitosi | @email Notes : Internship (x98) credits do not count towards program requirements or program electives. They only contribute to a student's credit count towards graduation. Theater Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate and Graduate Students Course(s) : Undergraduate: THEATER 198/298/298A/398/498/498Y Graduate: THEATER 698/698A/798 Contact : Undergraduate: Amy Altadonna | @email Graduate: Gilbert McCauley | @email Women, Gender, Sexuality Studies Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate and Graduate Students (Certificate Program) Course(s) : Undergraduate: WGSS 298/398/298C/398/498 Graduate Certificate: WGSS 598/698/698C Contact : Undergraduate: Kiran Asher | @email Graduate: Angie Willey | @email Return to the Top of Page Isenberg School of Management Accounting Undergraduate Isenberg Majors: Visit the Isenberg Internship & Co-Op Process page on iConnect for a complete guide to these processes. In addition to the course options identified below, Isenberg undergraduates in all majors can earn internship credit as UMASS 298 and may count those credits towards the 120 credits required to graduate. Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students and International Graduate Students Course(s) : Undergraduate: ACCOUNTG 398/398V (VITA program), 498S ( Semester in the Profession program) Graduate: SCH MGMT 696 Contact : Undergraduate: Jennifer Roy | @email Graduate: Bobbi Hopkins | @email Business Analytics Masters Undergraduate Isenberg Majors: Visit the Isenberg Internship & Co-Op Process page on iConnect for a complete guide to these processes. In addition to the course options identified below, Isenberg undergraduates in all majors can earn internship credit as UMASS 298 and may count those credits towards the 120 credits required to graduate. Internships for Credit Available? : For International Graduate Students Course(s) :  SCH-MGMT 696 Contact : MSBA: Angela Amato | @email MSBA/MBA Dual Degree: Bobbi Hopkins | @email Finance Undergraduate Isenberg Majors: Visit the Isenberg Internship & Co-Op Process page on iConnect for a complete guide to these processes. In addition to the course options identified below, Isenberg undergraduates in all majors can earn internship credit as UMASS 298 and may count those credits towards the 120 credits required to graduate. Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students or International Graduate Students Seeking CPT Course(s) : Undergraduate: FINANCE 498/498Y Graduate: SCH-MGMT 696 (CPT only) Contact : Undergraduate: Fousseni Chabi-Yo | @email Graduate: Bobbi Hopkins | @email Notes : Undergraduate Finance majors can apply a maximum of 3 credits from a field experience to satisfy business/economics electives. Hospitality & Tourism Management Undergraduate Isenberg Majors: Visit the Isenberg Internship & Co-Op Process page on iConnect for a complete guide to these processes. In addition to the course options identified below, Isenberg undergraduates in all majors can earn internship credit as UMASS 298 and may count those credits towards the 120 credits required to graduate. Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students Course(s) : HT-MGT 298W/298Y/HT-MGT 398/HT-MGT 498Y Contact : Jenafer Andren | @email Notes : An HTM internship course cannot take the place of a program requirement. Credits earned for the internship can only be applied towards the university’s credit requirement. Management Undergraduate Isenberg Majors: Visit the Isenberg Internship & Co-Op Process page on iConnect for a complete guide to these processes. In addition to the course options identified below, Isenberg undergraduates in all majors can earn internship credit as UMASS 298 and may count those credits towards the 120 credits required to graduate. Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduates Students and International Graduate Students Course(s) : Undergraduate: MANAGMNT 398/498Y Graduate: SCH-MGMT 696 Contact : Undergraduate: Jennifer Merton | @email Graduate: Bobbi Hopkins | @email Notes : The Management Department has allowed up to three credits of internship to apply to the major (MANAGMNT 398) and it is recorded as an elective. Management majors can apply a maximum of three credits from MANAGMT 398 to satisfy an Aspect of Change elective. Marketing Undergraduate Isenberg Majors: Visit the Isenberg Internship & Co-Op Process page on iConnect for a complete guide to these processes. In addition to the course options identified below, Isenberg undergraduates in all majors can earn internship credit as UMASS 298 and may count those credits towards the 120 credits required to graduate. Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students Course(s) : MARKETNG 398, MARKETNG 498B (Advertising Practicum) Contact : Elizabeth Miller | @email Notes : Students can apply up to three credits of an internship to satisfy the upper-level business elective requirement of the marketing major. Masters of Business Administration (MBA) Undergraduate Isenberg Majors: Visit the Isenberg Internship & Co-Op Process page on iConnect for a complete guide to these processes. In addition to the course options identified below, Isenberg undergraduates in all majors can earn internship credit as UMASS 298 and may count those credits towards the 120 credits required to graduate. Internships for Credit Available? : For Graduate Students Course(s) : SCH-MGMT 696 (for CPT), SCH-MGMT 698 Contact : Bobbi Hopkins | @email Operations & Information Management (OIM) Undergraduate Isenberg Majors: Visit the Isenberg Internship & Co-Op Process page on iConnect for a complete guide to these processes. In addition to the course options identified below, Isenberg undergraduates in all majors can earn internship credit as UMASS 298 and may count those credits towards the 120 credits required to graduate. Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students Course(s) : OIM 498/498Y Contact : Senay Solak | @email Notes : Operations and Information Management majors can apply a maximum of three credits from field experience to satisfy upper-level electives. Sport Management Undergraduate Isenberg Majors: Visit the Isenberg Internship & Co-Op Process page on iConnect for a complete guide to these processes. In addition to the course options identified below, Isenberg undergraduates in all majors can earn internship credit as UMASS 298 and may count those credits towards the 120 credits required to graduate. Internships for Credit Available? : Undergraduate and Graduate Students Course(s) : Undergraduate: SPORTMGT 298/498 Graduate: SPORTMGT 698/798A, SCH-MGMT 698 Contact : Emily Must | @email Notes : For undergraduate Sport Management, 12 credits of SPORTMGT 498 replaces two sport management electives. SPORTMGT 298 can count towards overall credit requirement. More information about the process can be found on the Sport Management Internship page. Return to the Top of Page Elaine Marieb College of Nursing Nursing (Undergraduate) Traditional credited internships are not typically a part of the nursing plan of study. Nursing students engage in clinical learning experiences, which are all required to be taken at specific times in a nursing student's experience. While these are credited experiences, they are strictly regulated and require training under vetted nurse proctors. To learn more about clinical learning experiences, reach out to your department advisor. You can also reach out to Dr. Elise Carrier ( @email ) for more information. Nursing (Graduate) Traditional credited internships are not typically a part of the nursing plan of study. Nursing students engage in clinical learning experiences, which are all required to be taken at specific times in a nursing student's experience. While these are credited experiences, they are strictly regulated and require training under vetted nurse proctors. To learn more about clinical learning experiences, reach out to your department advisor. You can also reach out to Dr. Elise Carrier ( @email ) for more information. Return to the Top of Page College of Social and Behavioral Sciences Anthropology Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate and Graduate Students Course(s) : Undergraduate: ANTHRO 298/398/398A/498/498C/498Y Graduate: ANTHRO 698 Contact : Undergraduate: Boone Shear | @email Graduate: Brigitte Holt | @email Notes : Anthropology majors may count up to 4 credits of internship experience towards their major requirements. See Anthropology Internship Opportunities for more information. Communication Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students Only Course(s) : UMASS 298 Contact : Marianne Neal-Joyce | @email Notes : For Communication, all internship credits count to the student's 120 credits, but do not count for any departmental requirements Economics Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate and Graduate Students Course(s) : Undergraduate: ECON 298/298Y/398/398C/398Y/498/498Y Graduate: ECON 598 Contact : Undergraduate: Valerie Voorheis | @email Graduate: Deepankar Basu | @email Notes : Internship credits may not be used towards major requirements Journalism Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students Course(s) : JOURNAL 398 Contact : Beth Wallace | @email John Ciampa | @email Notes: Journalism majors in the Public Relations and Sports Journalism concentrations are required to do an internship. Labor Studies Internships for Credit Available? : For Graduate Students Course(s) : LABOR 698L/698R/798 Contact : Nellie Taylor | @email Landscape Architecture Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate and Graduate Students Course(s) : Undergraduate: LANDARCH 398/498Y Graduate: LANDARCH 698/698A (Practicum Master's Project) Contact: Undergraduate:Patricia McGirr | @email Graduate: Frank Sleegers | @email Latin American, Caribbean & Latino Studies Internships for Credit Available? : No (Practicum courses dropped after Spring 2022) Legal Studies Students looking to pursue an internship in Legal Studies should check with Alan Gaitenby . Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students Course(s) : LEGAL 298; LEGAL 298C (Citizen's Police Academy) Contact : Alan Gaitenby | @email Notes : Students may take up to 18 total internship credits towards graduation completion. 3 credits of LEGAL 298 or Legal 298C may be used to replace a Law-Related Liberal Arts Course. Political Science Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students Course(s) : Undergraduate: POLISCI 298; POLISCI 498D Graduate: POLISCI 698 Contact : Undergraduate: Adrian Grace | @email Graduate: Paul M. Collins | @email Notes : Students may take up to 18 total internship credits towards graduation completion. Political Science allows up to 3 credits of POLISCI 298 or POLISCI 498D internship experience to count towards the 200-level major requirements if you were admitted to UMass Summer 2023 or later. Students need to be sponsored by a Political Science faculty member to enroll in those internship classes. Students admitted prior to that can apply POLISCI 498D to the 300-level requirements of major. This graded course requires significant work with a Political Science faculty member. Public Policy & Administration Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate and Graduate Students Course(s) : SPP 396 Contact : Undergraduate: Faith Nussbaum | @email Graduate: Marcie Muehlke | @email Notes : Graduate Students in the School of Public Policy complete a policy- or management-related internship or experiential learning class. Regional Planning Internships for Credit Available? : For Graduate Students Course(s) : REGIONPL 698/698A (Practicum Masters Project) Contact : Henry Renski | @email Resource & Managerial Economics Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate and Graduate Students Course(s) : Undergraduate: RES-ECON 398 Graduate: RES-ECON 698 Contact : Undergraduate: Colby Gray | @email Graduate: Nathan Chan | @email Notes: In Resource Economics, internship credits can only serve as elective credit toward the University 120 credit requirement, and cannot be used in place of any major requirement. Social & Behavioral Science Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students Course(s) : SOC-BEHAV 398B: SBS in Boston Internship SOC-BEHAV 398D: SBS in DC Practicum SOC-BEHAV 398W: SBS int he World Internship Practicum Contact : Carol Sharick | @email Social Thought & Political Economy Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students Course(s) : STPEC 298/398/498Y Contact: Monica Garcia | @email Notes : STPEC students are required to complete 120 hours of internship work (one 3 credit internship). See STPEC Internship Requirement for more information. Sociology Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students Only Course(s) : SOCIOL 398/498 (counts towards department credit); SOCIOL 298 (counts only towards graduation requirements) Contact : Kat Fabel | @email Notes: Sociology majors can replace their 4-credit, 200-level sociology elective requirement with a 4-credit, letter-graded, sociology-related internship that has been approved by an advisor. See Sociology Internships for a list of internship sites and more details about completing an internship. Sustainable Community Development Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students Course(s) : SUSTCOMM 298/398/498Y Contact : Peter Dunn | @email Notes: Sustainable Community Development may count practicum or independent study credit as a free elective or in limited exceptional contexts as a concentration elective, but not as a substitute for a core requirement. Return to the Top of Page School of Public Health and Health Sciences Biostatistics & Epidemiology Internships for Credit Available? : For Graduate Students Course(s) : BIOSTAT 896, EPI 698 Contact :  Elizabeth Donohoe Cook | @email Environmental Health Sciences Internships for Credit Available? : For Graduate Students Course(s) : EHS 698 Contact :  Alexander Suvorov | @email Notes :  All Master's of Public Health (MPH) Environmental Health Sciences students complete a practicum. Health Promotion & Policy Internships for Credit Available? : For Graduate Students Course(s) : HH 698 Contact :  Jennifer Whitehill | @email Notes :  Master's of Public Health (MPH) tracks of Community Health Education and Health Policy & Management have practicum requirements. Kinesiology Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students and International Graduate Students Course(s) : Undergraduate: KIN 398, KIN 398A, KIN 498, KIN 498Y International Graduate: KIN 696 Contact : Undergraduate: Eliza Freshette | @email Graduate: John Sirard | @email Notes: Up to 3 credits of KIN X98 credits can cover a KIN elective for KIN majors Nutrition Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate and Graduate Students Course(s) : Undergraduate: NUTRITN 198/298/398/498 Graduate: NUTRITN 698 Contact : Nicole Goldstein | @email Notes: There are three tracks in nutrition and students can use NUTR 298, 398 or 498 for internship credit, which counts for credit but not toward major requirement. Public Health Sciences Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate and Graduate Students Course(s) : Undergraduate: PUBLHLTH 398 Graduate: PUBLHLTH 698 Contact : Sofija Zagarinx | @email Notes: In some instances the Public Health Sciences Department allows internships to cover a course requirement for an elective, but it’s on a case by case basis. Consult with an academic advisor in Public Health Sciences. Speech, Language, and Hearing Sciences Internships for Credit Available? : For Undergraduate Students Only Course(s) : SLHS 398, SLHS 498Y Contact : Gwyneth Rost | @email Notes: Students in Speech, Language, and Hearing Sciences are required to take an elective course in the major numbered 300 or above and can meet that requirement with an internship. Return to the Top of Page Career Development & Professional Connections Whether you’re wondering where to begin, looking for 