      "title": "How to Use Handshake",
      "description": "How to Use Handshake : Career Development & Professional Connections : UMass Amherst Skip to main content The University of Massachusetts Amherst Open UMass Global Links Menu Visit Apply Give Search UMass.edu Menu Career Development & Professional Connections About Us Our Staff Career Centers Across UMass Our Newton Campus Handshake Login Student Outcomes Students Undergraduates Graduates Alumni Identity-Based Resources International Students Prospective Students UWW Students Employers Post Jobs and Internships Host an Event Career Fairs at UMass Why Recruit at UMass Internship Program Best Practices Recruiting Guidelines Contact Us Faculty Sponsor an Intern Career Events for Students Request a Presentation Resource Library Career Journey Expand Menu Item Self Discovery and Career Exploration Build Career Skills: Resumes, Job-searching, and Interviewing Learn Additional Technical, Creative, and Professional Skills Your Career Support Team Gain Experience: Internships, Co-ops, Research, and More! Is Graduate School Right for Me? Year-by-Year Checklist Tool Kits Expand Menu Item Resumes Cover Letters Career Fair Preparation Interviewing LinkedIn Learning Networking What Skills Do Employers Want? Applying to Grad School Photo Booth for Headshots Professional Wardrobe Closet Connections Expand Menu Item Career Communities Expand Menu Item Arts, Multimedia, and Entertainment Business, Financial Services, and Consulting Data and Information Technology Education, Human Services, and Counseling Engineering Government and Public Service Healthcare, Life Sciences, and Nursing Infrastructure and Transportation Law and Legal Services Research Sustainability, Environment, and Agriculture Career Centers Across UMass Expand Menu Item Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Education Engineering Graduate School Office of Professional Development Humanities & Fine Arts (HFA) Information & Computer Sciences (CICS) Isenberg School of Management (ISOM) Natural Sciences (CNS) Nursing Public Health and Health Sciences (SPHHS) Social & Behavioral Sciences (SBS) University Without Walls (UWW) Connect with UMass Alumni Using LinkedIn How to Network Jobs & Internships Expand Menu Item Internships, Co-ops, and Other Field Experiences Expand Menu Item Field Experience Definitions Internships Co-ops Research Civic Engagement and Service Learning Internships and Co-Ops at Charles River Campus UMass Internship Partner Programs Scholarships for Field Experiences Jobs Searching for Jobs & Internships Can I Do an Internship? Negotiating Job Offers Interviewing Using Handshake How to Use Handshake Careers Resources How Use Handshake You'll see Handshake advertised all over UMass Amherst's career pages, and for good reason: it's the platform we use for many of our career functions. From posting jobs and internships, to advertising events and career fairs, to making an appointment with a career advisor, Handshake offers many resources that will help you succeed in your career. Log into Handshake Using Handshake Getting Started on Handshake As a UMass Amherst student, you already have access to Handshake! Logging in as simple as the steps below: Go to umass.joinhandshake.com/ Login using your UMass Net ID and Password Complete Your Profile When you first log onto Handshake, you'll be asked to complete your profile and answer questions about your career interests. Filling out this information will help Handshake learn more about what information to present to you based on your background and goals. The most important section to complete and keep updated is “Your Career Interests.” Profiles are automatically set to private, so if you want your profile to be viewable by employers or for networking, you need to change it to a Community Profile. A community profile is only viewable by employers connected with UMass Amherst. You can have a community profile and keep some information (for example, your GPA) private. How to Change Profile Privacy Settings Click the circle with your initial in the top right corner Select \"Settings\" Scroll down to the Privacy section and select the option that meets your privacy preference Note: If you want to participate in virtual career fairs, you should to set your profile to community. GPA Privacy Setting Click the circle with your initial in the top right corner Select My Profile Click the edit symbol in the Education section and Select the options that meets your privacy preference Make an Appointment with a Career Advisor With the exception of Isenberg School of Management students who make appointments with career counselors through Navigate , all undergraduate UMass Amherst students use Handshake to schedule an appointment. To Make an Appointment through Handshake: Login to Handshake Select “Career Center” from the left-hand navigation bar Click Appointments underneath the header Click on the ‘Schedule a New Appointment’ button Pick your Category and Appointment Type Choose whichever option most closely matches your need. This selection helps us to prepare for your appointment. Note: The list is personalized based on your profile. You may not be eligible for all appointment types. The more information you provide before the appointment, the better we can help. Use the arrows and calendar to find the date you want the appointment Select the time slot you want and click ‘Request'. Note that most Handshake appointments are set to automatically accept your request, so once you've found a time slot that works for you and a career advisor, you're set! Review or edit your appointment by returning to ‘Appointments’. If you find out you have a conflict with your appointment time prior to your appointment, Handshake provides the option to cancel on this screen. Don’t “no-show”! Job Searching With thousands of employers posting jobs on the platform, Handshake is a powerful tool for your internship and job search needs! Click Jobs on the left navigation menu Use the following methods to identify the most relevant jobs and narrow down your search: Search Bar : search for jobs based on keywords, job titles, job ids, or by employer. Looking for remote opportunities? Use the keyword search! UMass Amherst Collections : find jobs curated specifically for your school by your career services department. Location : find jobs in a particular city, state, zip code, or country. Note: the location filter defaults to a 50 mile radius. Use the slider to move the dot across the line to change the radius, left to decrease and right to increase the mileage. On-site/Remote : filter on jobs that are in-person, hybrid, or work from home. Full-time Job : browse available full-time positions. Internship : browse internships. Part-time : browse available part-time positions. All Filters : access even more search filters to narrow your search! Results using the above search filters are displayed immediately on the left side of the page. Using Handshake for a Virtual Fair Handshake advertises both in-person fairs, as well as virtual fairs that can be attended on Handshake. In order to book appointments and join a virtual fair: Log in: https://umass.joinhandshake.com (Use Chrome, FireFox or the Handshake mobile app) Choose \"Events\" from the menu on the left side of the page --> Click the \"Career fairs at your school\" button right above All Events Click the Register button to the right of the fair name (note that scheduling typically opens a week before the fair) Review the details of the fair, as well as the companies and the positions offered. You can use filters and save favorite companies for your own notes. Once you know which companies you'd like to meet, start scheduling your meetings. There are two types of possible meeting offered by employers: one-to-one meetings and group sessions. Right above the listed Contact information, there are three tabs: Available sessions - click this tab to review and register for available employer sessions Your schedule - once you've signed up for at least one session, this is where the session details are listed (and how you'll join a session when it starts) Career fair details - the default tab that loads with fair setup details Make sure your resume is up-to-date before your first session Profile Visibility needs to be on Community, not Private If you need to cancel your meetings for any reason, click “Your Schedule” on the right side On the day of the fair, click “Your Schedule” to join sessions you've signed up for up to 5 mins. before the meeting starts Join the session by clicking the blue \"Join Video\"  button Applying for Jobs and Internships on Handshake UMass Amherst requires that all employers recruiting UMass Amherst students adhere to Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) guidelines, the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) Principles for Ethical Professional Practice, and the terms and conditions set forth by UMass Amherst’s career centers. As such, any job postings shared by employers on Handshake and that are accessible by UMass Amherst students are expected to be in-line within these defined guidelines and compliant with federal and state law. Students are encouraged to apply to any postings of interest, regardless of any limitations on immigration/citizenship status stated in the job description. For information on positions that may exempt applications based on immigration/citizenship status, visit the Immigrant and Employee Rights Section website. UMass Amherst students are expected to do their due diligence while reviewing job applications by considering the qualifications for each job carefully before applying. Neither UMass Amherst nor Handshake will prevent you from applying for any position listed on Handshake.com. Video: The UMass Guide to Handshake (7 Mins) For the visual learners, here is a great 7-minute video by UMass Amherst Career Services highlighting: What is Handshake Setting up & maximizing your profile (1:05) Connect with employers (3:52) Events – how to search & register (4:47) UMass Career Centers & schedule a career advising appointment (5:37) The opportunities and/or programs presented herein are for informational purposes only, and are not sponsored, arranged, endorsed, promoted, or administered by the University of Massachusetts, or by University faculty or staff members. Career Development & Professional Connections Whether you’re wondering where to begin, looking for an internship, or starting your job search, we will guide you through the process of your unique career development. Address: Goodell Hall | 140 Hicks Way | Amherst, MA 01003 Main Office Number: (413) 545-2224 Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Footer Students Career Journey Career Centers Resource Library Employers Handshake Contact Us UMass collegiate M - University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2025 University of Massachusetts Amherst · Site Policies · Accessibility"
    },
