    "https://www.umass.edu/careers/announcements/internship-photo-contest-2026": {
      "title": "Internship Photo Contest 2026",
      "description": "Internship Photo Contest 2026 : Career Development & Professional Connections : UMass Amherst Skip to main content The University of Massachusetts Amherst Open UMass Global Links Menu Visit Apply Give Search UMass.edu Menu Career Development & Professional Connections About Us Our Staff Career Centers Across UMass Our Newton Campus Handshake Login Student Outcomes Students Undergraduates Graduates Alumni Identity-Based Resources International Students Prospective Students UWW Students Employers Post Jobs and Internships Host an Event Career Fairs at UMass Why Recruit at UMass Internship Program Best Practices Recruiting Guidelines Contact Us Faculty Sponsor an Intern Career Events for Students Request a Presentation Resource Library Career Journey Expand Menu Item Self Discovery and Career Exploration Build Career Skills: Resumes, Job-searching, and Interviewing Learn Additional Technical, Creative, and Professional Skills Your Career Support Team Gain Experience: Internships, Co-ops, Research, and More! Is Graduate School Right for Me? Year-by-Year Checklist Tool Kits Expand Menu Item Resumes Cover Letters Career Fair Preparation Interviewing LinkedIn Learning Networking What Skills Do Employers Want? Applying to Grad School Photo Booth for Headshots Professional Wardrobe Closet Connections Expand Menu Item Career Communities Expand Menu Item Arts, Multimedia, and Entertainment Business, Financial Services, and Consulting Data and Information Technology Education, Human Services, and Counseling Engineering Government and Public Service Healthcare, Life Sciences, and Nursing Infrastructure and Transportation Law and Legal Services Research Sustainability, Environment, and Agriculture Career Centers Across UMass Expand Menu Item Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Education Engineering Graduate School Office of Professional Development Humanities & Fine Arts (HFA) Information & Computer Sciences (CICS) Isenberg School of Management (ISOM) Natural Sciences (CNS) Nursing Public Health and Health Sciences (SPHHS) Social & Behavioral Sciences (SBS) University Without Walls (UWW) Connect with UMass Alumni Using LinkedIn How to Network Jobs & Internships Expand Menu Item Internships, Co-ops, and Other Field Experiences Expand Menu Item Field Experience Definitions Internships Co-ops Research Civic Engagement and Service Learning Internships and Co-Ops at Charles River Campus UMass Internship Partner Programs Scholarships for Field Experiences Jobs Searching for Jobs & Internships Can I Do an Internship? Negotiating Job Offers Interviewing Using Handshake Internship Photo Contest 2026 Careers Announcements Internship Photo Contest 2026 Wednesday, April 29, 2026 By Joe Van Allen The Career Development and Professional Connections Hub is thrilled to announce that the 2026 Internship Photo Contest is now open for submissions! For over 10 years, Career Services at UMass Amherst has been hosting an internship photo contest for students of the University. Its purpose is to showcase the amazing work that our students do every year across dozens of industries. Whether you've done an internship, co-op, research, or other professional experience, we want to see you in action! By sharing your internships (and by proxy your journey), you can help the next generation of UMass students learn what it looks like to do an internship and the difference it can make in their careers. We're so excited to see what you are up to, we're even including prizes for the top voted pictures! Prizes include: $50 gift card as a top prize $25 gift card for second through fifth place Winners have their picture mounted on display in the UMass Career Hub Submit your Internship Photos Here! Past Winners: Leila R | Major: Pre-Veterinary Science | Woodlands Wildlife Refuge Ana V.T. | Major: Natural Resource Conservation | Museum of Science Elsa H. | Major: Public Health Science | Boston Children's Hospital Katherine C. | Major: Civil Engineering PhD | National Renewable Energy Laboratory Mia S. | Major: Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration | McCarthy River Tours Pradhyum V. | Major: Mechanical Engineering | Newport News Shipbuilding Jabin C. | Major: Mechanical Engineering | Amazon Robotics Jadyn B. | Major: Public Health | Brockton Neighborhood Health Center Chiruza M. | Major: Biology | Vertex Pharmaceuticals Tia Bella H. | Major: Veterinary and Animal Science | Camel Training Internship Photo Contest Submission Guidelines: Have someone take a high-quality picture of you at your internship. Previous winners are often actively working, have a company logo or mascot if appropriate, and/or doing something unique and interesting. You should be the focus! Generally, other people should not be included in your picture (especially children). Celebrities are okay, as well as people who have fully consented to be in your picture and to have it shared. Internships should have been engaged in between Fall 2025 through Summer 2026. Your submission must be turned in no later than Friday, September 11, 2026. Advice for high-quality pictures: Make sure the camera is focused on you so that you have a clear picture Wipe off the lens with a dry cloth (microfiber if you've got it, a t-shirt will suffice in desperate times) Rooms with bright lights, or photos taken outdoors, often lead to the best quality photos due to ample lighting Typically higher-quality pictures take up more memory (that's a good thing in this case!). Pictures from your phone or a camera will usually be higher res than pictures posted on social media or sent via e-mail. YOU are a part of what makes pictures high-quality. Smiles, energy, enthusiasm, poses, and creativity all count for extra points. We let you submit up to 5 pictures, so feel free to submit a few. Eligibility for Participation: You must currently be or have been a UMass Amherst student during the window of the contest (September 1, 2025 - August 31, 2026) You must have completed an internship, co-op, research, or other field experience during that same window of time Field experiences can be paid or unpaid, as well as credited and not for credit All participants agree to the publication of their name and photo on UMass Amherst publications, posters, websites, social media, and marketing materials. About Joe Van Allen Joe Van Allen is the Senior Data Analyst and  Associate Director of Communications at the UMass Amherst Career Development and Professional Connections Hub. He's passionate about connecting students with opportunities that showcase their skills, and bridging the gaps between what someone wants to do and their current experience. And spreadsheets - he can't get enough of spreadsheets. Articles by Joe Van Allen More Articles by Joe Van Allen Related Articles Go to: How to Write Your LinkedIn Profile April 1, 2025 The New Way to Get Your Professional Picture Taken UMass Amherst now has the Iris Pro Photo Booth on-site. Students can book an appointment on Handshake to have their professional picture taken for free throughout the semester. Go to: How to Write Your LinkedIn Profile March 18, 2025 Internship Photo Contest 2025 Each year, the Career Hub at UMass hosts an internship photo contest with prizes for the best submissions. Any UMass Amherst student who completed an internship, co-op, research, or other field experience from September 1, 2024 to August 31st, 2025 is eligible to enter. Go to: How to Write Your LinkedIn Profile October 30, 2023 Negotiation Skills for Anyone Negotiating is one of those skills that feels intimidating on the outset, but is actually pretty easy to develop. With a few strategies and an adjustment in mindset, you can help increase your earning potential for years to come. Career Development & Professional Connections Whether you’re wondering where to begin, looking for an internship, or starting your job search, we will guide you through the process of your unique career development. Address: Goodell Hall | 140 Hicks Way | Amherst, MA 01003 Main Office Number: (413) 545-2224 Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Footer Students Career Journey Career Centers Resource Library Employers Handshake Contact Us UMass collegiate M - University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2025 University of Massachusetts Amherst · Site Policies · Accessibility"
    },
    "https://www.umass.edu/careers/announcements/considering-relocating-after-graduation-maybe-you-should": {
      "title": "Considering Relocating After Graduation? Maybe You Should.",
      "description": "Considering Relocating After Graduation? Maybe You Should. : Career Development & Professional Connections : UMass Amherst Skip to main content The University of Massachusetts Amherst Open UMass Global Links Menu Visit Apply Give Search UMass.edu Menu Career Development & Professional Connections About Us Our Staff Career Centers Across UMass Our Newton Campus Handshake Login Student Outcomes Students Undergraduates Graduates Alumni Identity-Based Resources International Students Prospective Students UWW Students Employers Post Jobs and Internships Host an Event Career Fairs at UMass Why Recruit at UMass Internship Program Best Practices Recruiting Guidelines Contact Us Faculty Sponsor an Intern Career Events for Students Request a Presentation Resource Library Career Journey Expand Menu Item Self Discovery and Career Exploration Build Career Skills: Resumes, Job-searching, and Interviewing Learn Additional Technical, Creative, and Professional Skills Your Career Support Team Gain Experience: Internships, Co-ops, Research, and More! Is Graduate School Right for Me? Year-by-Year Checklist Tool Kits Expand Menu Item Resumes Cover Letters Career Fair Preparation Interviewing LinkedIn Learning Networking What Skills Do Employers Want? Applying to Grad School Photo Booth for Headshots Professional Wardrobe Closet Connections Expand Menu Item Career Communities Expand Menu Item Arts, Multimedia, and Entertainment Business, Financial Services, and Consulting Data and Information Technology Education, Human Services, and Counseling Engineering Government and Public Service Healthcare, Life Sciences, and Nursing Infrastructure and Transportation Law and Legal Services Research Sustainability, Environment, and Agriculture Career Centers Across UMass Expand Menu Item Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Education Engineering Graduate School Office of Professional Development Humanities & Fine Arts (HFA) Information & Computer Sciences (CICS) Isenberg School of Management (ISOM) Natural Sciences (CNS) Nursing Public Health and Health Sciences (SPHHS) Social & Behavioral Sciences (SBS) University Without Walls (UWW) Connect with UMass Alumni Using LinkedIn How to Network Jobs & Internships Expand Menu Item Internships, Co-ops, and Other Field Experiences Expand Menu Item Field Experience Definitions Internships Co-ops Research Civic Engagement and Service Learning Internships and Co-Ops at Charles River Campus UMass Internship Partner Programs Scholarships for Field Experiences Jobs Searching for Jobs & Internships Can I Do an Internship? Negotiating Job Offers Interviewing Using Handshake Considering Relocating After Graduation? Maybe You Should. Careers Announcements Considering Relocating After Graduation Maybe You Should Thursday, January 22, 2026 Have you ever considering relocating after graduation? If not, you may want to. The Wall Street Journal just released the top cities where the class of 2025 landed jobs and the list is a little surprising. The list highlights a bunch of great, developing cities you may not have considered. For these cities to make the list, they must have a strong employer hiring demand spread across many companies. That means lots of positions that are probably not receiving the same volume of applications as a city not on this list; so, less competition for these roles. Many of these cities are also in locations with a very reasonable cost of living, especially when compared to the Greater Boston area. Early career opportunities are designed for gaining experience to create momentum in your career. Moving to a new city may be scary, but keep in mind, that experience could be \"the thing\" that sets you up for an amazing next opportunity in your location of choice. About Tiffany Appleton Tiffany is the Executive Director of Employer Engagement and Partnerships at the University of Massachusetts Amherst. In her employer relations role, Tiffany is behind the scenes working with companies and organizations across the region, state, and beyond to create awareness about hiring UMass Amherst students for internships, co-ops, full-time jobs, and more. Tiffany coordinates many of the career fairs and employer events across campus to help facilitate these connections. Articles by Tiffany Appleton More Articles by Tiffany Appleton Career Development & Professional Connections Whether you’re wondering where to begin, looking for an internship, or starting your job search, we will guide you through the process of your unique career development. Address: Goodell Hall | 140 Hicks Way | Amherst, MA 01003 Main Office Number: (413) 545-2224 Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Footer Students Career Journey Career Centers Resource Library Employers Handshake Contact Us UMass collegiate M - University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2025 University of Massachusetts Amherst · Site Policies · Accessibility"
    },
    "https://www.umass.edu/careers/announcements/amherst-area-internship-fair-kicks-career-fair-season-umass": {
      "title": "Amherst Area Internship Fair Kicks Off Career Fair Season",
      "description": "Amherst Area Internship Fair Kicks Off Career Fair Season at UMass : Career Development & Professional Connections : UMass Amherst Skip to main content The University of Massachusetts Amherst Open UMass Global Links Menu Visit Apply Give Search UMass.edu Menu Career Development & Professional Connections About Us Our Staff Career Centers Across UMass Our Newton Campus Handshake Login Student Outcomes Students Undergraduates Graduates Alumni Identity-Based Resources International Students Prospective Students UWW Students Employers Post Jobs and Internships Host an Event Career Fairs at UMass Why Recruit at UMass Internship Program Best Practices Recruiting Guidelines Contact Us Faculty Sponsor an Intern Career Events for Students Request a Presentation Resource Library Career Journey Expand Menu Item Self Discovery and Career Exploration Build Career Skills: Resumes, Job-searching, and Interviewing Learn Additional Technical, Creative, and Professional Skills Your Career Support Team Gain Experience: Internships, Co-ops, Research, and More! Is Graduate School Right for Me? Year-by-Year Checklist Tool Kits Expand Menu Item Resumes Cover Letters Career Fair Preparation Interviewing LinkedIn Learning Networking What Skills Do Employers Want? Applying to Grad School Photo Booth for Headshots Professional Wardrobe Closet Connections Expand Menu Item Career Communities Expand Menu Item Arts, Multimedia, and Entertainment Business, Financial Services, and Consulting Data and Information Technology Education, Human Services, and Counseling Engineering Government and Public Service Healthcare, Life Sciences, and Nursing Infrastructure and Transportation Law and Legal Services Research Sustainability, Environment, and Agriculture Career Centers Across UMass Expand Menu Item Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Education Engineering Graduate School Office of Professional Development Humanities & Fine Arts (HFA) Information & Computer Sciences (CICS) Isenberg School of Management (ISOM) Natural Sciences (CNS) Nursing Public Health and Health Sciences (SPHHS) Social & Behavioral Sciences (SBS) University Without Walls (UWW) Connect with UMass Alumni Using LinkedIn How to Network Jobs & Internships Expand Menu Item Internships, Co-ops, and Other Field Experiences Expand Menu Item Field Experience Definitions Internships Co-ops Research Civic Engagement and Service Learning Internships and Co-Ops at Charles River Campus UMass Internship Partner Programs Scholarships for Field Experiences Jobs Searching for Jobs & Internships Can I Do an Internship? Negotiating Job Offers Interviewing Using Handshake Amherst Area Internship Fair Kicks Off Career Fair Season at UMass Careers Announcements Amherst Area Internship Fair Kicks Career Fair Season Umass Monday, September 22, 2025 The Amherst Area Internship Fair returned to the Campus Center Auditorium on Friday, September 5, bringing together more than 40 local businesses, non-profits, and campus departments offering part-time jobs, internships, and work-study opportunities. Now in its fifth year, the fair has grown steadily—from 17 employers in its first year to more than 40 this fall—reflecting the strong demand for meaningful student work experiences in the Pioneer Valley. Dozens of employers, including The Eric Carle Museum of Picture Book Art, shared internship and work opportunities with UMass Amherst students on September 5, 2025. Co-hosted by the Amherst Area Chamber of Commerce and the UMass Arts Extension Service, the fair featured organizations such as the Eric Carle Museum of Picture Book Art, Big Y Foods, Amherst Cinema, and Amherst Innovative Living, as well as campus partners including Alumni Relations and the Mount Ida Campus. Students praised the fair for its approachable environment. One attendee shared, “I liked having the opportunity to talk to people representing local internships in a setting that was not overtly formal. I think the atmosphere and friendly staff made the event a lot less stressful.” Feedback like this reflects a larger trend—1,160 students attended this year’s fair, marking the third consecutive year with attendance over 1,000. Employers echoed the enthusiasm, noting how engaged students were and how smoothly the event was organized. The Amherst Area Internship Fair is one of more than 20 career fairs and recruiting events hosted annually by UMass Amherst. As the first fair of the year, it kicks off the fall recruiting season. Students can look forward to more opportunities in the coming weeks, including the Engineering Career Fair, the Isenberg School of Management Career Day, the Tech Jobs & Internships Fair, and the Life Sciences & Biotech Fair. Students can find a complete list of upcoming fairs and events is available on Handshake. About Joe Van Allen Joe Van Allen is the Senior Data Analyst and  Associate Director of Communications at the UMass Amherst Career Development and Professional Connections Hub. He's passionate about connecting students with opportunities that showcase their skills, and bridging the gaps between what someone wants to do and their current experience. And spreadsheets - he can't get enough of spreadsheets. Articles by Joe Van Allen More Articles by Joe Van Allen Related Articles Go to: How to Write Your LinkedIn Profile April 29, 2026 Internship Photo Contest 2026 Each year, the Career Hub at UMass hosts an internship photo contest with prizes for the best submissions. Any UMass Amherst student who completed an internship, co-op, research, or other field experience from September 1, 2025 to August 31st, 2026 is eligible to enter. Go to: How to Write Your LinkedIn Profile September 16, 2025 Dell Night Connects UMass Amherst Students with Dell Technologies Leaders and Alumni More than 250 students gathered in the Campus Center Auditorium on September 16 for Dell Night, an evening of career exploration, networking, and inspiration hosted by Dell Technologies in partnership with UMass Career Services. The event gave undergraduate and graduate students an opportunity to meet with Dell leaders and recruiters, hear from UMass alumni thriving in diverse roles at the company, and learn about internship and full-time opportunities across Dell’s business units. Go to: How to Write Your LinkedIn Profile September 10, 2025 Fidelity Day Connects 375 Students with Alumni and Career Opportunities More than 375 students gathered in Goodell Hall on September 10 for Fidelity Day, an employer highlight event hosted by the UMass Amherst Career Development and Professional Connections Hub in partnership with Fidelity Investments. Career Development & Professional Connections Whether you’re wondering where to begin, looking for an internship, or starting your job search, we will guide you through the process of your unique career development. Address: Goodell Hall | 140 Hicks Way | Amherst, MA 01003 Main Office Number: (413) 545-2224 Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Footer Students Career Journey Career Centers Resource Library Employers Handshake Contact Us UMass collegiate M - University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2025 University of Massachusetts Amherst · Site Policies · Accessibility"
    },
    "https://www.umass.edu/bdic/resources/career-services": {
      "title": "Breadcrumb",
      "description": "Career Services : Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) : UMass Amherst Skip to main content The University of Massachusetts Amherst Open UMass Global Links Menu Visit Apply Give Search UMass.edu Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) Super Nav Give to BDIC FAQs Contact Us Main navigation How to Apply Student Resources Toggle submenu for Student Resources Advising Career Services Forms and Documents About Toggle submenu for About Directory Events Senior Recognition Ceremony Explore Concentrations Newsletter and Alumni Updates Breadcrumb Home Resources Career Services BDIC is your Superpower! As motivated students designing your interdisciplinary degree and brand, BDIC Careers is committed to offering personalized supports and career advising. We believe the power of interdisciplinary studies, combined with experiential learning and skills-based coursework, will rocket you towards your goals. Whether you’re wondering where to begin, looking for an internship, or starting your job search, we will guide you through the process of your unique career development. Connect with your career advisor via Handshake to get started. Meet Your Career Advisor Joanna Miles Associate Director, Professional Transitions Joanna (she/her) is the dedicated career advisor for Bachelor’s Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) students at UMass Amherst. With over 20 years of experience in career development, she has supported students across fields from business to film and everything in between. She believes BDIC is your superpower—and is passionate about helping you leverage your interdisciplinary degree to launch confidently into your next steps. Connect with her to learn more about internships, research, graduate school, how to job search, resumes, interviews and more. Whether you have a clear vision for your future or are still exploring possibilities, Joanna is here to guide you every step of the way. Schedule a 1:1 Appointment with Joanna Schedule a 1:1 Appointment with Joanna BDIC Guides to Get You Started Who Am I? Explore and discover your skills, values, personality, and interests with tailored career assessment tools. Learn More Get Prepared Resume and cover letters, job market insights, interview preparation and salary negotiation tips can all be found here. Learn More Complement Your Academics Build your skills with access to more than 13,000 self-guided courses offered through LinkedIn Learning. Learn More Career Communities Join career communities to explore industries in-depth and connect with UMass alumni eager to share great career advice. Learn More Internships BDIC students complete internships year-round. Learn more, including how to fund and register your internship experience. Learn More Post-Grad Plans Let's demystify what comes next. Discover your options for graduate school and the best resources for a successful job search. Post Grad Plans As you strategize your career plans, there are many tools that can help you be successful. Resumes Resumes Cover Letters Cover Letters Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) 350 Campus Center Way Amherst, MA 01003 Phone: (413) 545-2504 Email: [email protected] Powered by University Without Walls Facebook Instagram University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2026 University of Massachusetts Amherst Site policies Privacy Non-discrimination notice Accessibility Terms of use"
    },
    "https://cns.umass.edu/careers": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "Career and Professional Development : College of Natural Sciences : UMass Amherst Skip to main content The University of Massachusetts Amherst Open UMass Global Links Menu Visit Apply Give Search UMass.edu College of Natural Sciences Main navigation Academics Toggle submenu for Academics Undergraduate programs Graduate programs Certificate programs Flexible and online learning All academic programs Courses See all departments Degree requirements Info for prospective students Pre-college programs Student Success Toggle submenu for Student Success CNS Student Success Center Academic Advising Career and Professional Development Graduate Student Success Pre-Med/Pre-Health Advising Belonging and Strategic Engagement Your Academic Deans First Year Opportunities Advising FAQs Scholarships Student Organizations Research Toggle submenu for Research Research centers & institutes Undergraduate research Greenhouses Industry partnerships Research support CNS Bridge and Seed Funding (BSF) program Scientific glassblowing laboratory Campus & Outreach Toggle submenu for Campus & Outreach Diversity, Equity & Inclusion Student Success and Diversity Eureka! Community Connections Giving Center for Agriculture, Food, and the Environment UMass Extension About Toggle submenu for About News Stories Events People Meet the leadership Buildings and facilities Contact Information for faculty & staff Information for alumni Breadcrumb Home Student Success Career and Professional Development About CNS is committed to helping students gain experiential learning opportunities and professional training to prepare for meaningful careers. Come to us to learn about field experience opportunities (internships, co-ops, research, and more) and strategies to increase your visible value to employers well before you graduate. In addition to your academics, experiential learning is what will help you get into graduate school or land a job after college. Start building your experiential learning now. The CNS Career Center is located in Morrill II, Suite 321. We offer both remote and in-person career advising appointments. Meet with a Career Advisor sooner rather than later, so we can help you figure out next steps and work with you to bring out your skills and experiences to demonstrate to employers. Overview links Make a career advising appointment on Handshake Connect on LinkedIn Career Development Handbook Explore the Career Center Career advising Resumes and cover letters CNS Graduate Student Career Resources For employers Job, internship, and co-op searching Handshake Interviewing and job offers Applying to graduate school Frequently asked questions CNS Biochemistry and Neuroscience major talking about her internship experience Undergraduate Destination Reports Check out the first destinations of our recent graduates. Class of 2024 Class of 2023 Class of 2022 Class of 2021 Class of 2020 Site footer College of Natural Sciences Find us on X Find us on Facebook Find us on YouTube Find us on LinkedIn Find us on Instagram Address 101 Stockbridge Hall 80 Campus Center Way Amherst , MA 01003-9248 United States Phone number (413) 545-2766 Info for... Current students Faculty and staff Alumni Academics Explore our programs Departments The college About CNS News Events Contact Contact CNS Directory University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2026 University of Massachusetts Amherst Site policies Privacy Non-discrimination notice Accessibility Terms of use"
    },
    "https://www.umass.edu/uww/interdisciplinary-studies/career-services": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "Career Services for Interdisciplinary Students : University Without Walls : UMass Amherst Skip to main content The University of Massachusetts Amherst Open UMass Global Links Menu Visit Apply Give Search UMass.edu Menu University Without Walls Main navigation About UWW Programs UWW Dept. of Interdisciplinary Studies Exploratory Pathways Program Jump In Program Professional Development Contact Us Student HQ Career Services for Interdisciplinary Students Breadcrumb UWW Interdisciplinary Studies Career Services Personalized Career Support Career Services is committed to offering personalized support and career advising for motivated students designing their interdisciplinary degree and brand. We believe the power of interdisciplinary studies, combined with experiential learning and skills-based coursework, will rocket you towards your goals. Whether you’re wondering where to begin, looking for an internship, or starting your job search, we will guide you through the process of your unique career development. Meet Your Career Advisor Joanna Miles Director of Career Planning in Interdisciplinary Studies Joanna (she/her) is the career advisor for University Without Walls Interdisciplinary Studies students at UMass Amherst. With more than 20 years of experience, she helps students use their interdisciplinary degree to plan next steps. Connect with her for support with internships, research, graduate school, job searches, resumes, and interviews. Whether you have a clear direction or are still exploring, Joanna is here to help you move forward. Schedule an Appointment with Joanna via Handshake Get Started with Handshake Whether you're looking for internships or want to schedule a one-on-one appointment, handshake has resources to get your career to a new level. LEARN MORE Strategies for Career Transitions Discover job search tools, interview preparation resources, and more. LEARN MORE Flexible Internships and Projects Micro internships company sponsored projects, stimulations, and remote projects are just some ways you can add flexible experiential learning. LEARN MORE Upscale Your Interdisciplinary Skills Discover skills based online courses, learning paths, certifications, and more from our partners at LinkedIn Learning. LEARN MORE Connect with the Alumni Network Join the 7000+ strong UMass online network that spans coast to coast and even overseas. LEARN MORE Explore Career Communities Explore our 11 industry clusters with tailored resources for next steps. LEARN MORE Resume Resources for UWW Students Explore tips and tricks to make your resume stand out from the rest. LEARN MORE Write Effective Cover Letters Learn how to write a cover letter that showcase your unique talents and skills. LEARN MORE Career and Self-Assessment Toolkit Skills interests values and personality assessments to bring clarity to your career exploration and decision making. LEARN MORE It's YOUR turn to finish your degree. We’re here to help. Admissions Start your tomorrow today. Apply now to finish your degree and change your future. Request Information Connect with our dedicated staff to learn more. We look forward to hearing from you soon. Tuition and Fees Learn how much college will cost and how to pay for it, from loans to scholarships. Credit for Experience Bring in or earn up to 105 credits for previous coursework, professional trainings and certifications, and more. Give Support vital scholarship funds, and pay it forward to the next generation of adult students. Student Headquarters Your one-stop shop as a current student. Find the information and resources you need to cross the finish line. University Without Walls As a member of SARA ,\n                      we accept students from all 50 states into our online classes and programs. Facebook Twitter YouTube Instagram LinkedIn UWW Programs UWW Dept. of Interdisciplinary Studies Exploratory Pathways Program Jump In Program Professional Development Powered by UWW Bachelor's Degree with Individual Concentration (BDIC) IT Program Innovate Certificate Interdisciplinary Exploratory Track Pre-College @ UMass UMass collegiate M - University of Massachusetts Amherst ©2025 University of Massachusetts Amherst · Site Policies · Accessibility"
    },
    "https://www.facebook.com/UMassCareers/": {
      "title": "UMass Amherst Career Development & Professional Connections HUB",
      "description": "UMass Amherst Career Development & Professional Connections HUB | Amherst MA | Facebook Facebook Log In Log In Forgot Account? UMass Amherst Career Development & Professional Connections HUB 1.9K followers • 142 following Posts About Reels Photos More Posts About Reels Photos UMass Amherst Career Development & Professional Connections HUB Intro UMass Amherst Career Development & Professional Connections aka \"The HUB\"  helps undergraduate & graduate students connect their UMass Amherst education to meaningful and satisfying careers. Page · Campus Building 130 Hicks Way, Amherst, MA, United States, Massachusetts (413) 545-2224 careerservices@umass.edu umass.edu/careers Not yet rated (1 review) ﻿ Photos See all photos Privacy · Consumer Health Privacy · Terms · Advertising · Ad Choices · Cookies · More UMass Amherst Career Development & Professional Connections HUB 15h · Shared with Public Welcome to the fall semester! Want to get a jump start on your career this week? UMass Career Services is hosting their annual Amherst-Area Internship Fair this Friday … See more Like Comment See more from UMass Amherst Career Development & Professional Connections HUB | Amherst MA See more from UMass Amherst Career Development & Professional Connections HUB | Amherst MA Email or phone number Password Log In Forgot password? or Create new account"
